2 CONT
2 CONT b)         PIETRO Visconti (-after 1301).  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Petrus Vicecomes Dominus Seprii et frater patris Matthæi" rebelled against "Matthæum Vicecomitem Dominum civitatis Mediolani" in 1301 but was captur
2 CONC ed and held "in castro de Serezano"[60].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Pietro´s wife is not known.  Pietro & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *i)          daughter .  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by the Annales Mediolanenses which record that "Petrus Vicecomes Dominus Seprii et frater patris Matthæi" incited "Ruscam Dominum civitatis Cumanæ generum suum" to 
2 CONC rebel against Matteo [I] Visconti Lord of Milan in 1301, the succeeding passage recording "Conradus Rusca Dominus civitatis Cumanæ" among the rebels[61].  '''m''' CORRADO "Rusca" Signore di Cuma, son of --- (-after 1301). 
