2 CONT **a)         '''GIACOMO della Torre''' .  The Annales Mediolanenses name "Martinus giganteus" as father of "Jacobus"[7].  '''m''' ---.  The name of Giacomo´s wife is not known. Giacomo & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ***i)          PAGANO della Torre (-1247).  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Jacobus" had "tres filii…Paganus…primus de Domo Turrianorum dominus civitatis, et Jacobus, et Antimanus archiprebyter"[8].  -         see below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ***ii)         GIACOPO della Torre .  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Jacobus" had "tres filii…Paganus…primus de Domo Turrianorum dominus civitatis, et Jacobus, et Antimanus archiprebyter"[9]. ''' m''' ---.  The name of Gia
2 CONC copo´s wife is not known. Giacopo & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ****(a)       MARTINO "Magno" della Torre (-18 Jan 1264, bur Chiaravalle Abbey).  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Giacopo" had two sons "Martinus Magnus et Philippus Magnus"[10].  The Annales Mediolanenses records the death
2 CONC  18 Jan 1264 of "Martinus Magnus de la Turre", his burial "in Claravalle…juxta tumulum Pagani de la Turre patris sui", and the succession of "Philippo fratri suo" to "dominium civitatis Mediolani et civitatis Laudensis et Novariæ"
2 CONC [11]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ****(b)       FILIPPO "Magno" della Torre (-1265).  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Giacopo" had two sons "Martinus Magnus et Philippus Magnus"[12].  The Annales Mediolanenses record the death in 1265 of "Dominum Philippum 
2 CONC de la Turre…civitatum…Brixiæ, Cumarum, Pergami, Novariæ, Vercellarum et Laude", leaving "filium…Salvinus", but the succession of "Neapoleo sive Napus consanguineus eius germanus" to "dominium civitatis Mediolani"[13].  '''m''' ---
2 CONC .  The name of Filippo´s wife is not known. Filippo & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *****(1)       SALVINO della Torre .  The Annales Mediolanenses record the death in 1265 of "Dominum Philippum de la Turre…civitatum…Brixiæ, Cumarum, Pergami, Novariæ, Vercellarum et Laude" leaving "filium…Salvinus"[14]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ***iii)        ANTIMANO della Torre .  The Annales Mediolanenses record that "Jacobus" had "tres filii…Paganus…primus de Domo Turrianorum dominus civitatis, et Jacobus, et Antimanus archiprebyter"[15]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
