2 CONT
2 CONT (1)     '''  ARGENTINA Spinola ''' .  The Chronicon Astense records the marriage in 1306 of "Theodorus filius Imperatoris Græcorum" and "filiam Opecini Spinolæ dicti de Luculis tunc Capitanei Januæ…Argentinam"[400].  Pachymeres re
2 CONC cords the marriage of "quidam Spinulus…filia" and "filium imperatoris Theodorum", dated to [1306] from the context[401].  Benvenuto di San Giorgio, quoting Ruffino Ventura Astense, records the marriage of "Theodorus filius Imperat
2 CONC oris Græcorum" and "filiam Oppicini Spinulæ tunc Capitanei Januæ…Argentinam"[402].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1306) TEODORO Paleologo Marchese di Monferrato, son of Emperor ANDRONIKOS II & his second wife Yolanda [Eirene] di Monferrato ([1291]-21 Apr 1338). 
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodore I, Marquess of Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1307 he married a Genoese lady, Argentina Spinola, daughter of the lord of that city, Opicino Spinola. They had two children, John (1313-1372) and Yolande (1318-1342), who married Aimone, Count of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
