2 CONT a)     '''    OBIZZO Spinola''' (-after 1270).  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Novocastro names "Conradus de Antiochia et Margarita soror eius" as the two children of "Fridericus de Antiochia" and his wife, adding that "Marg
2 CONC arita" and her husband (unnamed) had "Beatricem" who married "Opizo filio Raynaldi Spinule"[170].  The Chronicon Astense records that "Obertus Spinola et Obertus Auria" were installed as "capitanei generales Januæ" in 1270[171].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' BEATRICE, daughter of --- & his wife Margherita di Antiochia.  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Novocastro names "Conradus de Antiochia et Margarita soror eius" as the two children of "Fridericus de Antiochia" and his 
2 CONC wife, adding that "Margarita" and her husband (unnamed) had "Beatricem" who married "Opizo filio Raynaldi Spinule"[172].  
2 CONT
