1 OCCU Podestà di Verona, Herr von Verona als Mitregent seines älteren Bruders Alberto II. della Scala seit dem Jahr 1329
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/GDC9-V1L
2 CONT
2 CONT - http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mastino_II_della_Scala
2 CONT
2 CONT Mastino II della Scala (1308 – June 3, 1351) was lord of Verona. He was a member of the famous Scaliger family of northern Italy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alboino I della Scala and Beatrice da Correggio. At the death of Cangrande I, he and his brother Alberto II were associated in the rule of Verona. Soon, however, Mastino's intraprendence overshadowed the brother'
2 CONC s presence. In the first part of his reign, abandoning the careful policy of balance held by his father, he conquered Brescia (1332), Parma (1335) in Lombardy and Lucca (1335) in Tuscany.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, the extension of Mastino's power spurred the creation of League of all the other local powers (Florence, Siena, Bologna, Perugia and Venice). In the first year of war he managed to resist, but in 1336 the League was joine
2 CONC d by Azzone Visconti of Milan, the Este of Ferrara, the Gonzaga of Mantua and the Papal States. Surrounded by every side, he could only ask for a treaty of peace through the intermediation of Emperor Louis IV of Bavaria, which he 
2 CONC obtained in 1339. His territories were restricted to Verona and Vicenza, the remaining part split among the victorious enemies.
2 CONT
2 CONT An attempt to recover part of his lands with the German mercenaries that had remained in Vicenza after the war, led by Lodrisio Visconti, was unsuccessful.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Verona in 1351. He his buried in the Gothic mausoleum near the church of Santa Maria Antica, in one of the famous Scaliger Tombs.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Family
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1328 he married Taddea da Carrara (daughter of Jacopo I of Padua) and Anna Gradenigo. She gave him the following three legitimate sons and one daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Cangrande (1332–1359)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alboino (1333-1375)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cansignorio (c. 1334–1375)
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice Regina della Scala (1331- 18 June 1384), who married Bernabò Visconti on 27 September 1350
2 CONT
2 CONT His illegitimate children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fregnano (died 1394)
2 CONT
2 CONT Viridis (died 1394), who married Niccolò II d'Este in 1362
2 CONT
