1 OCCU Comte, de Genève, Greve i Geneve c1080-1128, COUNT OF GENEVA, graaf van Genève
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Foundation for Medieval Genealogy:
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkgenev.htm#AimonIGenevadied1128B
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''AIMON [I] de Genève''', son of GERAUD Comte de Genève & his [second] wife Tetberga --- ([1060/65]-12 May [1125/28]).  "Patris Geraldi et fratris Cononis, comes Aymo successor" donated property to the church of Leman, at the req
2 CONC uest of "fratris Burchardi monachi", by undated charter[38].  Comte de Genève.  Vassal of the bishop of Geneva.  Avoué of St Victor, Geneva.  "Aymo comes Gebennensis et filius meus Giroldus" founded the priory of Chamonix by undat
2 CONC ed charter, dated to [1088/99], signed by "uterini fratres comitis, Willelmus Fulciniacus et Amedeus…"[39].  "Aymo…Genevensium comes" donated property to the monastery of Saint-Eugendi by charter dated 1090, signed by "Itæ uxoris 
2 CONC eius, Geraldi filii eius"[40].  "Aymo comes Gebennensis et Amadeus filius eius" renounced rights to certain property in favour of the church of Saint-Martin by undated charter[41].  "Aymone…comite" approved the donation by Guy Bis
2 CONC hop of Geneva of the church of Saint-Jean de Genève to the monastery of Ainay, near Lyon, by charter dated 1113[42].  A charter dated 1124 records an agreement between Humbert Bishop of Geneva and "Aymone comite"[43].  The necrolo
2 CONC gy of Saint-Claude records the death "IV Id Mai" of "Aymo comes Gebennensis"[44]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [firstly] ITA, daughter of --- (-after 1090).  "Aymo…Genevensium comes" donated property to the monastery of Saint-Eugendi by charter dated 1090, signed by "Itæ uxoris eius, Geraldi filii eius"[45]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[m''' secondly ---.  The chronology of this family suggests that Comte Amédée [I] may have been his father’s son by an otherwise unrecorded second marriage.''']''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Aimon [I] & his [first] wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         GERAUD (-after 1090). ... ...
2 CONT
2 CONT   Aimon [I] & his [second] wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *2.         AMEDEE [I] ([1100/10]-28 Jun 1178). ... .... ... . . .  . . . . .. .    . . . . . . 
2 CONT
2 CONT *3.         GUILLAUME (-before 1153).  ... ...
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
