1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 722244664. Count of Aimoin II De Geneve, Count, born Abt. 1060 in Geneva, Switzerland; died Aft. 1134. He was the son of Gerard=Gerold II De Geneve, Count and Thiburge De Savoie. He married 722244665. Ide=Ida De Fa
2 CONC ucigny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT       722244665. Ide=Ida De Faucigny, born Abt. 1086. She was the daughter of Seigneur Louis I De Faucigny, Seigneur and Thiburge De Savoie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Ide=Ida De Faucigny: Ide=Ida De Faucigny (Andre Roux: Scrolls, 174) (Stuart, Royalty for Commoners, ISBN: 0-8063-1344-7, Page 134, Line 175-30) ( E.S. Band XI, Tafel 158 (1986)). Married Name: De Geneve. Born: before 107
2 CONC 6 in Savoie, France, daughter of Louis I, Seigneur De Faucigny. Ide is presumed to have been at Least 15 years of age by the time her son, Gerold, was born. Married before 1091: Aimoin II, Count De Geneve, son of Gerard=Gerold II,
2 CONC  Count De Geneve and Thiburge De Savoie. Died: after 1100. Some sources indicate that Ita died circa 1091. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Aimoin De Geneve and Ide=Ida De Faucigny is: 
2 CONT   361122332 i.   Count of Aime I De Geneve, Count, born Abt. 1100 in Geneva, Geneva, Switzerland; died June 26, 1178; married (1) N? De Domene in , France; married (2) Mathilde De Cuiseaux, Countess of Geneva Bef. 1130. 
