1 NOTE When the Empire of Austria was divided in 1879, Duke Leopold III established the House of Leopold.  He ruled his half of the empire until 1386, and was succeeded by his son, Duke William.  Upon the division of Austria in 1879 Leop
2 CONC old was given Styria; Carinthia; Tyrol, etc.  Leopold III was a war-like ruler, fought with the Bavarians, Venetians, and the Swiss.  He was killed by the Swiss at Sempach in 1386.
2 CONT
2 CONT Leopold III, son of Albert II of Austria, became co-Regent of the Empire of Austria in 1365.  He served until 1379.  Founder of the Leopoldine Line of succession.  As head of the House of Leopold he ruled until 1386, and was succe
2 CONC eded by his son, Duke William.
1 NOTE DUKE OF STYRIA 1365-1386; DUKE OF CARINTHIA AND TYROL; FROM WHOM DESCENDS THE
2 CONT LEOPOLDINE LINE OF STYRIA AND TYROL
