1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Elisabeth Wittelsbach, Kurfürstin zu Brandenburg''' was born on November 13, 1383 in Landshut, Bayern, Deutschland(HRR). Her parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-31824143 Friedrich, Herzog von Bayern-Landshut] and [https:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/profile-19808011 Madalena Visconti]. She was a Prinsessa. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth married [https://www.geni.com/profile-12224887 Friedrich, I Kurfürst von Brandenburg] on September 18, 1401 in Schougau, Bayern, Deutschland. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-384817
2 CONC 02 Elisabeth Hohenzollern, Herzogin zu Liegnitz, Herzogin zu Teschen]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-12224363 John II the Alchemist, Margrave of Brandenburg-Kulmbach]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-31824106 Margarethe Hohenzollern
2 CONC , Herzogin zu Mecklenburg, Herzogin zu Bayern-Ingolstadt, Gräfin]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-38481693 Magdalene Hohenzollern, Herzogin zu Braunschweig-Lüneburg, Fürstin zu Lüneburg]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-23568035 Fred
2 CONC erick II Hohenzollern, Elector]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-15181575 Albrecht III Achilles, Elector of Brandenburg]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-31824117 Sofie von Hohenzollern, Margravine of]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-3
2 CONC 4660566116 Dorothea Hohenzollern, Herzogin zu Mecklenburg-Schwerin]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-31824119 Frederich III der Fette von Brandenburg, Markgraf von Brandenburg und Herr der Altmark]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-563
2 CONC 70660 Cäcilie von Brandenburg, Fürstin zu Braunschweig-Wolfenbüttel]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on November 13, 1442 in Ansbach, Bayern, Deutschland(HRR) and was buried in Kloster Heilsbronn, Heilsbronn, Bayern, Deutschland/HRR). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Probably the most re-occurring ancestor of Queen Elizabeth II who descends form at least 3 of her children, more than once.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==die Schöne Else==
2 CONT '''Links:'''
2 CONT *[http://www.thepeerage.com/p344.htm The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=15557 Geneall] '''Wikipedia:''' [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elisabeth_von_Bayern_(1383%E2%80%931442)_ Deutsch]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT '''''Die Frauen der Wittelsbacher: Ein Frauenbild vom Mittelalter bis in die '''''... -https://books.google.com/books?id=deGMBAAAQBAJ&pg=PA12&lpg=PA12&dq=Elisabeth+von+Bayern Landshut+Wittelsbach,+Kurfürstin+zu+Brandenburg&source=
2 CONC bl&ots=5B2ke4LWdC&sig=MmHC-jVg5ZzinDEpdEhV5XK76eg&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwifu8jY2fvaAhVKyWMKHcb2CY0Q6AEwBXoECAUQAQ#=onepage&q=Elisabeth%20von%20BayernLandshut%20Wittelsbach%2C%20Kurfürstin%20zu%20Brandenburg&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Elisabeth of Bavaria-Landshut (1383 – 13 November 1442), nicknamed "Beautiful Beth", was an Electress of Brandenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was a daughter of Duke Frederick "the Wise" of Bavaria-Landshut and his second wife Maddalena Visconti. On 18 September 1401 she married Frederick VI of Hohenzollern, Burgrave of Nuremberg, who was promoted to Elector of
2 CONC  Brandenburg in 1415 and ruled as "Elector Frederick I". During her husband's long journeys to Italy, Hungary, and to the Council of Constance, she represented him wisely despite the great political problems Brandenburg was experi
2 CONC encing at the time. She is the ancestress of the royal line of the House of Hohenzollern by her third son Albert III Achilles, Elector of Brandenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT With Frederick she had ten children: Elisabeth (1403–31 October 1449, Liegnitz), married: in Konstanz 1418 Duke Louis II of Brieg and Legnica (1380/5–1436); in 1438 Duke Wenzel I of Teschen (1413/18–1474). John "the Alchemist" (14
2 CONC 06–1465), Margrave of Brandenburg-Kulmbach. married in 1416 Princess Barbara of Saxe-Wittenberg (1405–1465) Cecilia (c. 1405–4 January 1449), married: in Berlin 30 May 1423 Duke William I of Brunswick-Lüneburg(1392–1482). Margaret
2 CONC  (1410–27 July 1465, Landshut), married: in 1423 to Duke Albert V, Duke of Mecklenburg (1397–1423); in Ingolstadt 20 July 1441 to Louis VIII, Duke of Bavaria (1403–1445); in 1446 to Count Martin of Waldenfels (d. 1471). Magdalene 
2 CONC (c. 1412 –27 October 1454, Scharnebeck), married: in Tangermünde 3 July 1429 to Duke Frederick of Brunswick-Lüneburg (1418–1478). Frederick II (1413–1471), Elector of Brandenburg married in 1446 Princess Catherine of Saxony (1421–
2 CONC 1476) Albrecht Achilles, (1414–1486), Elector of Brandenburg, married: in 1446 Princess Margarete of Baden (1431–1457) in 1458 Princess Anna of Saxony (1437–1512) Sofie, born and died 1417. Dorothea (9 February 1420–19 January 149
2 CONC 1, Rehna), married: in 1432 Duke Henry IV, Duke of Mecklenburg (1417–1477) Frederick "the Fat" (c. 1424–6 October 1463, Tangermünde), Lord of Altmark, married: in 1449 Princess Agnes of Pomerania (1436–1512)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Wikipedia Added by: Janet Milburn 11/08/17
2 CONT
2 CONT The new horrible version of Find A Grave, Why did they have to change something good for this? Daughter  of Bernabò Viscontis and Beatrice della Scala. She married Friedrich von Bayern-Landshut in 1381.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maddalena Visconti BIRTH 1361 DEATH 24 Aug 1404 BURIAL  Kloster Raitenhaslach  Altotting, Altöttinger Landkreis, Bavaria (Bayern), Germany MEMORIAL ID 142110400
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by Janet Milburn 11/08/17
