1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *http://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacopino_della_Scala  (...>1248)
2 CONT *https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LT82-5HQ
2 CONT *https://gw.geneanet.org/capreolus?lang=en&n=della+scala&oc=0&p=jacopino
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT http://genealogy.euweb.cz/italy/scalla1.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Della Scala (Scalighieri) family=
2 CONT One Balduino, +1166, Consul of Verona in 1147 had issue:
2 CONT * ...
2 CONT *A2. Isnardino, +after 1186
2 CONT ** ...
2 CONT **B2. Leonardino/Sigiberto, +after 19.12.1228
2 CONT ***C1. Zocco, +executed, Verona 22.8.1245
2 CONT **** ...
2 CONT ***C2. '''Iacopino, Vicario Imperiale in Oneglia, Podeste di Cerea, +after 21.9.1248'''; <br> 1m: Margherita Giustiniani; <br> 2m: Elisa Superbi
2 CONT ****D1. [1m.] Manfredo, Bishop of Verona (1241-56), *1215, +1256
2 CONT ****D2. Leonardino also Mastino I, Podeste di Cerea 1258, Podeste di Verona I.1259, Capitano del Popolo di Verona (Lord of Verona) (1262-77), Podeste di Pavia 1267, +killed, Verona 26.10.1277; m.Giglia/Zilia N
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT ****D3. Alberto I, Podeste di Verona (1275-76), Lord of Verona (1277-1301), +Verona 3.9.1301; m.before 1263 Verde di Salizzole (+25.12.1306)
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT ****D4. Federico called Bocca, +k.a.near Villafranca 1269
2 CONT ***** ...
2 CONT ****D5. Guido, +XI/XII.1273
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacopino_della_Scala 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacopino della Scala (died ''1215 /!\''), an Italian merchant and politician, was a member of the Scaliger family of future lords of Verona. He was the son of Leonardo della Scala, and also the grandson of Karafina Gambarelli and 
2 CONC her husband Balduino della Scala, son of Arduino della Scala, who gave rise to the Della Scala dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT Initially he worked as wool trader, not rich and without any noble title. However, his friendship network and political skills granted him the title of Imperial vicar at Ostiglia, and podestà of Cerea. He was an ancestor of most E
2 CONC uropean monarchs.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of Mastino I (Leonardo), Alberto I, Manfredo and Bocca della Scala. He is the first relative of Napoleon I, Emperor of the French.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT Carrara, M. (1966). Gli Scaligeri. Varese: Dell'Oglio.
