1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT - Guecellone VII da Camino (c. 1275 – 1324) was an Italian nobleman and lord of Treviso. ([http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guecellone_VII_da_Camino Wikipedia])
2 CONT
2 CONT The second son of Gherardo III da Camino, he was initially destined to the ecclesiastical career. After the assassination of his elder brother and lord of Treviso, Rizzardo IV da Camino, to which he perhaps took part, he became Ge
2 CONC neral Captain of Treviso. He continued the pro-Guelph stand of his father, keeping good relationships with the Patriarchate of Aquileia and the Republic of Venice, and supporting the Paduans against Cangrande della Scala, lord of 
2 CONC Verona. He later changed side, and allied with the Veronese Alboino I della Scala.
2 CONT
2 CONT His unsteady conduct caused the Trevigiani people to rebel against him, under the lead of Rambaldo di Collato: Guecellone was forced to flee the city, ending the family's lordship in Treviso after 29 years (15 December 1312). In 1
2 CONC 317, with the help of Cangrande della Scala, he besieged the city and the bishop's castle of San Martino at Ceneda, but in vain. Later he reconciled with the bishops, being confirmed by the latter in the investiture of Feltre, Cen
2 CONC eda and Cadore, which had been conquered by Cangrande the previous year. The following year, he was excommunicated by the pope due to a dispute about his brother's testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Serravalle in 1324.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT -http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/guecellone-da-camino_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Nel suo testamento del 12 ag. 1324, il C. nominò suo erede l'unico figlio ancora in vita, Rizzardo (III). Fu sepolto, come il padre e il fratello, in S. Francesco a Treviso.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aveva sposato, non sappiamo esattamente quando, Mabilia di San Bonifacio, figlia del conte Vinciguerra e di Cappellina degli Scrovegni (Federici, p. 45). Da lei aveva avuto due figli, 
2 CONT *Gherardo, morto in giovine età, 
2 CONT *e Rizzardo (III); 
2 CONT *ed una figlia, Aica, che, già promessa a Cecchino della Scala, nipote di Cangrande, sposò poi, nel 1326, Iacopo Pappafava da Carrara (ibid., pp. 64 s.).
