1 OCCU Count, Comte de Genevre, Gerold II, comte de Genève, Comte, de Genève, http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liste_der_Grafen_von_Genf, Greve i Geneve c1023-1080, Greve i Geneve, COUNT OF GENEVA
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/G%C3%A9rold_de_Gen%C3%A8ve
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00027360&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkgenev.htm#GeneveMMathildeBurgundy
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          '''GERAUD''' ([1010/20]-after [1065/80]).  "Rodulfus rex et Mathildis soror eius" are named as children of "Mathilde…filia…Gerberga" in the Continuator of Flodoard, which specifies that Mathilde was mother of Berta who
2 CONC  was mother of "Geroldus Genevensis"[22].  As Géraud’s son Conon was probably adult when he donated property, recorded in a charter dated to [1061] (see below), it is unlikely that Géraud was born much later than [1020].  Comte de
2 CONC  Genève.  Géraud Comte de Genève supported the challenge by Eudes II Comte de Blois to the succession of Emperor Konrad I [II] King of Germany to the kingdom of Burgundy after the death of King Rudolf III in 1033[23].  Herimannus 
2 CONC records that "Reginolf et Gerolt Burgundiones" submitted to Heinrich III King of Germany "apud Solodurum" [Solothurn] in 1045[24].  "Cono Geraldi comitis filius" donated property to the abbey of Ainay, with the consent of "Geraldi
2 CONC  comitis patris sui", by charter dated to [1061][25].  
2 CONT
2 CONT [m firstly GISELA, daughter of ---.  Guichenon names Gisela as the first wife of Géraud Comte de Genève[26].  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.]  [A family relationship is indicated betwee
2 CONC n Rudolf von Rheinfelden King of Germany and Géraud Comte de Genève: a continuation of the Annales of St Gallen records that in 1064 “Rudolfus dux” attacked “Burgundiones” and expelled “sui sororini...rebellis Geroldi” from Geneva
2 CONC [27].  The term “sororinus” is rarely encountered in medieval documents.  Ducange provides three possible definitions: “sororis maritus”, “uxoris frater”, and “filiolus sororis”[28].  The second of these can be excluded in the con
2 CONC text of the Rheinfelden family given our knowledge about the families of Rudolf’s wives, as well as the third given the chronology of the lives of Géraud and Rudolf which suggests that the former was born earlier than the latter. 
2 CONC  “Sister’s husband” is therefore the most likely possibility, with which Hlawitschka agrees[29]: 
2 CONT if that is correct, Géraud married --- von Rheinfelden, daughter of Kuno Graf von Rheinfelden & his wife ---.  This is consistent with “sororinus” being derived from “soror” and maybe being a variation of “sororius”.  As shown her
2 CONC e, Géraud is recorded with two possible wives.  Given the likely dating of his [second] marriage, it is difficult to assess whether, in this scenario, his [first wife] Gisela or his [second] wife Tetberga would have been the daugh
2 CONC ter of Kuno Graf von Rheinfelden.  It should be noted that Armin Wolf, linking the etymology of “sororinus” with “sobrinus” and by extension “consobrinus”, suggests that Géraud and Rudolf were first cousins, sons of two sisters[30
2 CONC ].  However, this interpretation requires reading “sororini” as “consororini”, which stretches the natural interpretation of the passage.  If Géraud’s wife was Rudolf’s sister, presumably she could have been the same person as Kun
2 CONC o’s daughter shown in the document SWABIA NOBILITY (in which case she would be identified as Géraud’s [first wife] Gisela).]  
2 CONT
2 CONT m [secondly] ([1060/70] ) as her second husband, TETBERGA, 
2 CONT widow of LOUIS Seigneur de Faucigny, daughter of ---.  Her first marriage is proved by the charter dated 4 Sep 1119 by which "Wido…Gebennensis episcopus" donated "ecclesiam de Condominio" for the souls of "…matrie mee Teberge" to 
2 CONC Cluny[31].  Her second marriage is confirmed by the undated charter, dated to [1088/99], under which "Aymo comes Gebennensis et filius meus Giroldus" founded the priory of Chamonix, signed by "uterini fratres comitis, Willelmus Fu
2 CONC lciniacus et Amedeus…"[32].  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT   Géraud & his [first] wife had [one possible child:
2 CONT * (a)       [JEANNE (-[1095]).  Guichenon names Jeanne as the wife of Comte Amédée II referring to various secondary sources[725].  Her origin is not known with certainty, but Guichenon, referring to "Henninges" (no precise citati
2 CONC on), suggests "avec…assurance et…probabilité" that she was the daughter of Gerold Comte de Genève and his first wife Gisela ---[726].  From his discussion, it does not appear that this speculation is based on any surviving primary
2 CONC  source and it is not known how accurate it might be.  m ([1065/70]) AMEDEE de Savoie, son of ODDON Comte de Chablais & his wife Adelaida di Susa ([1048/50]-26 Jan 1080, bur Saint-Jean de Maurienne).  He succeeded his brother in 1
2 CONC 078 as AMEDEE II Comte de Savoie, Marchese di Susa.]  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Géraud & his [first/second] wife had one child:
2 CONT *(b)       CONON (-before 1080).  "Cono Geraldi comitis filius" donated property to the abbey of Ainay, with the consent of "Geraldi comitis patris sui", by charter dated to [1061][727].  The chronology suggests that Conon must ha
2 CONC ve been considerably older than his brother Aimon [I] and therefore was probably born from his father´s [first] marriage.  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Géraud & his [second] wife had one child:
2 CONT *(c)       AIMON [I] ([1065/80]-12 May [1125/28]).  "Patris Geraldi et fratris Cononis, comes Aymo successor" donated property to the church of Leman, at the request of "fratris Burchardi monachi", by undated charter[728].  Comte 
2 CONC de Genève. -        see below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
