1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Adrian_V
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pope Adrian V''' (Latin: Adrianus V; c. 1210/1220 – 18 August 1276), born '''Ottobuono de' Fieschi''', was the head of the Catholic Church and ruler of the Papal States from 11 July 1276 to his death on 18 August 1276. He was a
2 CONC n envoy of [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-Clement-IV/6000000035439285835 Pope Clement IV] sent to England in May 1265 who successfully completed his task of resolving disputes between  King [https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-II
2 CONC I-king-of-England/979118 Henry III of England] and his barons. Adrian V was elected pope following the death of Innocent V, but died of natural illness before being ordained to the priesthood.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Divine Comedy, [https://www.geni.com/people/Dante-Alighieri/6000000012442001730 Dante] meets Adrian V in the fifth terrace of Purgatorio where Adrian V cleanses for the vice of avarice.
2 CONT
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Adrian_V#Biography Biography]
2 CONT
2 CONT #	[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pope_Adrian_V#Pope_Adrian_V_in_Dante's_Divine_Comedy Pope Adrian V in Dante's Divine Comed]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
