2 CONT Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azala%C3%AFs_of_Montferrat (English) Azalaïs of Montferrat] | [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alasia_del_Monferrato (italiano) Alasia del Monferrato]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Azalaïs of Montferrat''' (also '''Adelasia''' or '''Alasia''') (died 1232), was marchioness and regent of Saluzzo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Azalaïs was one of at least three daughters of William V of Montferrat and his wife Judith of Babenberg. Her brothers included William of Montferrat, Count of Jaffa and Ascalon, Conrad I of Jerusalem, and Boniface of Montferrat.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Marquis Manfred II of Saluzzo before 1182, in which year she received lands in Saluzzo, Racconigi, Villa, Centallo and Quaranta, in case her marriage (like that of her sister Agnes) should need to be annulled for reaso
2 CONC ns of sterility. However, after this date, she bore at least five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Agnes '''m.''' Comita III, giudice of Logudoro, in Sardinia. 
2 CONT * Boniface (the heir, who predeceased his father) '''m.''' Maria of Torres (daughter of Agnes's husband). 
2 CONT * Margaret '''m.''' Geoffrey de Salvaing. 
2 CONT * (unnamed daughter) '''m.''' Marquis William II of Ceva. 
2 CONT *Thomas.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/alasia_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT
2 CONT Figlia di Guglielmo il Vecchio del Monferrato, in anno imprecisato andò sposa a Manfredi II di Saluzzo: ne era già consorte nel 1173, come appare da una convenzione stipulata tra Manfredi e Giordano di Barge. Nel 1182 ricevette in
2 CONC  dono terre in Saluzzo, Racconigi, Villa, Centallo e Quaranta, con una clausola riguardante lo scioglimento del matrimonio in caso di sterilità....
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT PLZ source for exact date of death: 22/07/1232
2 CONT
