2 CONT 1. '''GUGLIELMO [I]''' (-after 10 Nov 1204).  '''Marchese di Ceva'''.  
2 CONT "''Gulielmus de Ceva filius quondam Anselmi Marchionis''" donated property to "''ecclesiæ B. M. Casularum''" by charter dated 4 Jul 1188[852].   
2 CONT "''Dominus Guilielmus Marchio de Ceva''" donated "''hæreditate Domini Bonifacii Marchionis de Curtemilia''" to the consuls of Asti by charter dated 26 May 1190[853].   
2 CONT A charter dated Oct 1198 records an agreement between Bonifazio Bishop of Asti and "''Wiermus de Ceva''", who confirms that "''dominum Bonefacium fratrem et nepotes suos et dominum Othonem et Henricum de Carreto''" will respect it
2 CONC [854].   
2 CONT A charter dated 8 Mar 1202 records an agreement between the commune of Alessandria and "''dominum Othonem de Carretto Marchionem suo nomine et nomine domini Vermi de Ceva Marchionis et domini Anrici Marchionis de Pulzono''"[855]. 
2 CONC
2 CONT "''Dominus Oto de Carreto marchio et Henricus marchio frater eius et Guillelmus dominus de Ceua et Bonifacius marchio de Crauesana frater eius''" donated property to the monastery of Santa Maria di Casanova by charter dated 10 Nov
2 CONC  1204[856].   
2 CONT
