1 TITL Lady
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Katherine FitzAlan Hussey received assignment of dower to the property October 1, 1349. On August 6, 1350 license was granted "to Katherine, late the wife of Henry Huse, tenant-in-chief, to marry whosoever she will
2 CONC  of the king's allegiance," according to "Patent Rolls." She was married shortly afterwards to Sir Andrew Peverell. According to "Complete Peerage" she made her will as his widow on "Sunday after St. Luke" 1375 at Ewhurst, desirin
2 CONC g burial at the monastery at Lewes, Sussex. She gave bequests to the shire of St. Richard of Chichester, Sussex, to the Friars of Lewes and to the Friars of Arundel, Sussex, etc, and mentioned "my lord's cousin, Andrew Peverell." 
2 CONC She died in 1375, according to "History of Gloucestershire." The will was proved in 1376.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 23, 1376 the escheator [official who received custody of property reverting to the crown] of Gloucestershire was ordered to "take into the King's hand lands late of Katherine, late wife of Sir Andrew Peverell, who held in d
2 CONC ower of Sir Henry Hussee."
