1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Aline FitzAlan=
2 CONT * Birth:  1325 in England
2 CONT * Death: 20 Jan 1386  Oswestry, Shropshire Unitary Authority, Shropshire, England 
2 CONT * Burial  Black Friars Priory  Shrewsbury, Shropshire Unitary Authority, Shropshire, England Memorial ID 122600753
2 CONT * Daughter of Edmund FitzAlan, 9th Earl of Arundel and Alice de Warenne, Countess of Arundel 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She obtained a license dated Jan. 3, 1382 allowing her daughter Lucqery to be married to William, son of Sir William de Willoughby, lord of Eresby, in her oratory within the castle at Middle, Shropshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/FitzAlan-619
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline was the daughter of Edmund FitzAlan, 2nd Earl of Arundel, and Alice de Warenne.[1][2][3][4] Her birth date is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline married Roger le Strange[3][4][5] before July 1351.[1][2] They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John[1][2][4][5]
2 CONT # Roger[1][2][5]
2 CONT # Ebles, who became rector of Wistanstow, Shropshire and Gresforrd, Denbighshire[1][2]
2 CONT # Edward[1][2][5]
2 CONT # Edmund[1][2]
2 CONT # Joan, who married Thomas Poynings[1][2]
2 CONT # Lucy, who married William Willoughby[1][2][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1369 John de Rochford and his wife Isabel sued Aline and her husband for Isabel's downright to a third of the manor of Shenstone, Staffordshire.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline received 1500 marks under the 1375 will of her brother Richard, in addition to 1000 marks which he had already given her and her husband.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Following her husband's death in 1382, Aline asked Richard de Ellesmere, who held the living of Llanymynech, Shropshire, to secure her dower rights.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline died on 20 January 1385/6.[1][2]
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Aline's brother Richard names "my nephews and nieces sons and daughters of Roger le Strange and to my sister Dame Alaine le Strange wife to the said Roger." (Cited in Medlands - https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH
2 CONC %20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#AlineFitzAlanMRogerLestrange.) That gives proof that Aline, daughter of Edmund FitzAlan, married Roger le Strange.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Marlyn Lewis gives a confused account of this family and should not be trusted - in particular confusing Aline's son Ebles, a priest who died before 12 December 1401, with Ebles le Strange, Lord of Knockin, who died in 1335 and MA
2 CONC Y have been the father of an illegitimate daughter Isabel.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Title seen as “Countess of Hertford” without attribution.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&lpg=RA2-PA301&ots=qwCnLE-afi&dq=stapleford-foulk%20manor%20cheshire&pg=RA2-PA301#v=onepage&q=stapleford-foulk%20manor%20cheshire&f=false page 301] of Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study 
2 CONC In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STRANGE.htm#Roger%20Le%20STRANGE%20(5%C2%BA%20B.%20Strange%20of%20Knockin '''STRANGE FAMILY From The Tudor Place''']
2 CONT * [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alice_de_Warenne,_Countess_of_Arundel '''Alice de Warenne, Countess of Arundel, by Wikipedia''']
2 CONT * [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Fitzalan,_2nd_Earl_of_Arundel '''Edmund Fitzalan, 2nd Earl of Arundel, by Wikipedia''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-357463831-1-500942/aline-knockyn-le-strange-born-fitzalan-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-0c2ea3e1ed30c1e465b17ed63ae584f9&mrid=adfff4616cb851046477ad2
2 CONC 2744b932e MyHeritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 4 2017, 23:29:31 UTC'
2 CONT * http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00026705&tree=LEO
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/stream/lestrangerecords00lestuoft#page/323/mode/1up Page 323] of Le Strange records : a chronicle of the early Le Stranges of Norfolk and the March of Wales A.D. 1100-1310, with the lines of Knockin and Blac
2 CONC kmere continued to their extinction Author Le Strange, Hamon, 1840-1918
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/stream/lestrangerecords00lestuoft#page/337/mode/1up Page 337] ibid
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/FitzAlan-619 cites 
2 CONT # Colonial and Medieval Families, 4 vols, ed. Kimball G. Everingham, 2nd edition (Salt Lake City: the author, 2011), Vol. IV, pp. 123-124, STRANFE 6
2 CONT # Douglas Richardson. Royal Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 5 vols, ed. Kimball G. Everingham (Salt Lake City: the author, 2013), Vol. V, pp. 64-65, STRANGE 8
2 CONT # R W Eyton. The Antiquities of Shropshire, Vol VII, John Russell Smith, 1858, p 229 HathiTrust
2 CONT # G E Cokayne. Complete Peerage, revised edition, Vol. XII Part 1, St Catherine Press, 1953, p. 354, viewable on Familysearch
2 CONT # Hamon le Strange. A Chronicle of the Early le Stranges of Norfolk and the March of Wales A.D. 1100–1310: With the Lines of Knockin and Blackmere Continued to Their Extinction, Longmans, Green, 1916, p. 323, Internet Archive
2 CONT # George Wrottesley. Extracts from the Plea Rolls of the Reign of Edward III and Richard II, 'Collections for a History of Staffordshire', Vol. XIII, William Salt Archaeological Society, 1892, pp. 49, Internet Archive and 60, Inte
2 CONC rnet Archive and passim
2 CONT # Nicholas Harris Nicolas. Testamenta Vetusta, Vol. I, Nichols and Son, 1826, pp.94-96, InternetArchive
2 CONT #  Marlyn Lewis. 'Our Royal, Titled, Noble and Commoner Ancestors', entry for Sir Roger le Strange, 5th Lord Strange https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p528.htm#i15865
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She is a Direct Descendant of Charlemagne.'''
2 CONT This is her lineage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlemagne
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis I, The Pious
2 CONT
2 CONT Giséle of Cysoing 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengar I, emperor of the Romans
2 CONT
2 CONT Gisela of Friuli 
2 CONT
2 CONT Berengar II of Ivrea, king of Italy 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adalbert II, king of Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT Otto Guillaume I, comte de Bourgogne et de Mâcon 
2 CONT
