2 CONT >1.         EDMUND (1 May 1285-executed Hereford 17 Nov 1326).  Inquisitions following a writ dated "15 Jan. 30 Edw. I”, after the death of “Richard Earl of Arundel”, record “Edmund his son, aged 16, is his next heir…aged 18 at th
2 CONC e feast of SS. Philip and James last…aged 17 on the day of St. Thomas the Apostle, 30 Edw. I”[133].  He succeeded his father in 1302 as Earl of Arundel.  He was loyal to King Edward II but was captured in Shropshire by supporters 
2 CONC of Queen Isabelle and beheaded without trial, and subsequently attainted whereupon his honours were forfeited[134].  m (1305) ALICE de Warenne, daughter of WILLIAM de Warenne & his wife Joan de Vere of Oxford ([May/Jul 1287]-befor
2 CONC e 23 May 1338).  Earl Edmund & his wife had four children: 
