2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_FitzAlan,_9th_Earl_of_Arundel _______________
2 CONT *John de Bohun, 5th Earl of Hereford (23 November 1306 – 20 January 1336) was born in St Clement's, Oxford to Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl of Hereford and Elizabeth of Rhuddlan, a daughter of Edward I of England.
2 CONT *After his father's death at the Battle of Boroughbridge, the family lands were forfeited. It was not until after the fall of the Despensers that John was permitted to succeed to his inherited position as Earl of Hereford and Esse
2 CONC x and hereditary Constable of England.
2 CONT *'''He married firstly, in 1325, to Alice FitzAlan (1314-1385/86)''', daughter of Edmund FitzAlan, 9th Earl of Arundel, and secondly to Margaret Basset (died 1355).[citation needed] After the marriage, it was discovered that the c
2 CONC ouple were related to the fourth degree of consanguinity and they were forced to live apart. An appeal to the Pope resulted on 19 February 1331 in a papal commission to the bishops of Lichfield and London to hold an enquiry into t
2 CONC he case.[1] However, Roger Northburgh, the Bishop of Coventry and Lichfield, failed to act and the case was still pending when the Pope issued a further demand for an enquiry in 1334. [2]
2 CONT *He did not play much of a public role, despite his high titles and offices, most likely because he had some sort of incapacity.[3] His younger brothers were often deputed to fulfill his duties as Constable. He died at Kirkby Thor
2 CONC e, Westmorland and was interred in Stratford Langthorne Abbey, London.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_de_Bohun,_5th_Earl_of_Hereford ______________
2 CONT *'''Sir John de Bohun
2 CONT *Birth: 	Nov. 23, 1306, England
2 CONT *Death: 	Jan. 20, 1336, England
2 CONT *Knight, Earl of Hereford and Essex, Constable of England
2 CONT *Second but first surviving son of Sir Humphrey de Bohun and Elizabeth of England. Grandson of Sir Humphrey de Bohun, Earl of Hereford and Maud de Fiennes, Edward I, King of England and Eleanor of Castile. John was born in St Clem
2 CONC ents.
2 CONT *'''John married Alice de Arundel''', the daughter of Edmund de Arundel FitzAlan and Alice de Warrene, the daughter of Sir William. '''They were married by dispensation dated 22 Feb 1325 as they were related in the 4th degree, and
2 CONC  had no issue. 
2 CONT *John married secondly, Margaret Basset, the daughter of Lord Ralph Basset, and Joan de Grey, daughter of Lord Grey of Wilton. They were married before 19 Feb 1331, again the date of dispensation as they were related in the fourth
2 CONC  degree, and had no issue. 
2 CONT *After his death, Margaret went to Santiago and other foreign holy places of pilgrimage for a year.
2 CONT *Family links: 
2 CONT * Parents:
2 CONT *  Humphrey de Bohun (1276 - 1322)
2 CONT *  Elizabeth Plantagenet (1282 - 1316)
2 CONT * Siblings:
2 CONT *  Humphrey de Bohun*
2 CONT *  Mary de Bohun*
2 CONT *  Margaret De Bohun (1302 - 1304)*
2 CONT *  Eleanor de Bohun (1304 - 1363)*
2 CONT *  John de Bohun (1306 - 1336)
2 CONT *  Humphrey De Bohun (1309 - 1361)*
2 CONT *  Margaret de Bohun Courtenay (1311 - 1391)*
2 CONT *  William De Bohun (1312 - 1360)*
2 CONT *  Isabel de Bohun (1316 - 1316)*
2 CONT *Burial:  Stratford Abbey, Newham, London Borough of Newham, Greater London, England
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 107668237
2 CONT *From: http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=107668237 _____________
2 CONT *RICHARD FitzAlan, son of JOHN FitzAlan Lord of Clun and Oswestry & his wife Isabel de Mortimer (3 Feb 1267-9 Mar 1302, bur Haughmond Abbey, Shropshire).  He succeeded his father in 1272 as Lord of Clun and Oswestry, and as owner 
2 CONC of the title and honour of the castle of Arundel, and had seisin of his lands 8 Dec 1287.  He was created Earl of Arundel [Sussex] in 1289, although this is the last time that the old title Earl of Sussex is heard of[99].  “Ric co
2 CONC mes de Arundell et dom de Albo” confirmed donations of property by “bonæ memoriæ Wil. filii Alani antecessoris nostri” to Shrewsbury Abbey by charter dated “die Martiis in festo Annunciationis beatæ Mariæ anno regni regis Edwardi 
2 CONC vicesimo”[100]. 
2 CONT *m (before 1285) ALASIA di Saluzzo, daughter of TOMASO I Marchese di Saluzzo & his wife Luisa di Ceva (-25 Sep 1292). 
2 CONT *Earl Richard & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT **	1.         EDMUND (1 May 1285-executed Hereford 17 Nov 1326).  He succeeded his father in 1302 as Earl of Arundel.  He was loyal to King Edward II but was captured in Shropshire by supporters of Queen Isabelle and beheaded with
2 CONC out trial, and subsequently attainted whereupon his honours were forfeited[101].  m (1305) ALICE de Warenne, daughter of WILLIAM de Warenne & his wife Joan de Vere of Oxford ([May/Jul 1287]-before 23 May 1338).  Earl Edmund & his 
2 CONC wife had four children: 
2 CONT ***		a)         RICHARD ([1313]-Arundel 24 Jan 1376, bur Lewes Priory, Sussex).  He was restored as Earl of Arundel in 1331.   
2 CONT ***		-        see below. 
2 CONT ***'''		b)         ALICE (-bur Walden Abbey).  The History of the foundation of Walden abbey names “Alicia Arundell” as the wife of “Johannes de Boon, comes Herefordiæ et Essexiæ” and records that she was buried at Walden[102].  A
2 CONC  manuscript which narrates the descents of the founders of Lanthony Abbey records the marriage of “Johannes de Bohun comes”, son of “Humfredus octavus”, and “Aliciam filiam domini Edmundi comitis Arundeliæ” after the death of his 
2 CONC father, and her burial at Walden[103].  m (Papal dispensation Feb 1325) as his first wife, JOHN de Bohun Earl of Hereford and Essex''', son of HUMPHREY de Bohun Earl of Hereford and Essex & his wife Elizabeth of England (St Clemen
2 CONC ts 23 Nov 1306-Kirkby Thore, co. Westmoreland 20 Jan 1336, bur Stratford Abbey near London). 
2 CONT ***		c)         ALINE (-20 Jan 1386).  The will of "Richard Earl of Arundel and Surrey", dated 5 Dec 1375, bequeathed property to “Richard my son...my son Thomas Bishop of Ely...John my son...Joane my daughter [...Countess of Here
2 CONC ford]...Alice my daughter...the eldest daughter of my said son John...Henry and Edward the younger sons of my said son John...William another son of my said son John...my nephews and nieces sons and daughters of Roger le Strange a
2 CONC nd to my sister Dame Alaine le Strange wife to the said Roger...my...uncle John Arundell”[104].  m (1338 or before) ROGER Le Strange, son of ROGER Le Strange Lord Strange (of Knokyn) & his first wife Matilda --- ([1326/27]-Keneyle
2 CONC swode [Kenwick’s Wood, Ellesmere parish, Shropshire?] 23 Aug 1382).  He succeeded his father in 1349 as Lord Strange (of Knokyn)[105]. 
2 CONT ***		d)         KATHERINE (-before 23 May 1376, bur Lewes Priory).  The will of "Katherine wife of Andrw Peverell Knight", dated 21 Oct 1375, chose burial “in the monastery of Lewes”, and bequeathed property to “Andrew Peverell co
2 CONC usin to my lord...the Earl of Arundel my brother...Richard his son my nephew” and names “Henry Huse late my husband”[106].  m firstly (before 16 Oct 1347) as his second wife, HENRY Husee Lord Husee, son of HENRY Husee Lord Husee &
2 CONC  his wife Isabel --- ([1301/02]-1 Jul 1349).  m secondly (after 6 Aug 1350) ANDREW Peverell, son of --- (-before 1375). 
2 CONT **2.         JOHN de Arundel (-after 5 Dec 1375).   .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#AliceFitzAlanMJohnBohunHerefordEssex _____________
2 CONT *'''Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ...
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&pg=RA1-PA77&lpg=RA1-PA77&dq=Alice+FitzAlan+1375&source=bl&ots=qvGkLv2ikk&sig=-KzXNYF4IPb0LcxS49MeXbSkt1A&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CDAQ6AEwAzhGahUKEwjBrYuOl4fIAhUPNIgKHayWCn8#v=onepage&q=bohun
2 CONC &f=false
2 CONT *Pg.63
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *9. EDMUND DE ARUNDEL (or FITZ ALAN), Knt., 9th Earl of Arundel, of the Castle and honor of Arundel, Sussex, of Clun and Oswestry, Shropshire, Chief Butler of England, Captain General north of the Trent, 1316, Privy Councillor, 13
2 CONC 18 .... He married after 30 Dec. 1304 ALICE DE WARENNE, daughter of William de Warenne, Knt., .... They had four sons, Richard, Knt. [Earl of Arundel and Surrey], John, Edmund [Treasurer of Chichester, Warden of the Hospital of St
2 CONC . Nicholas, Portsmouth], and Michael (clerk), and six daughter, Eleanor, Alice, Katherine, Aline, Elizabeth, and Mary. .... etc.
2 CONT *Pg.65
2 CONT *Children of Edmund de Arundel, Knt., by Alice de Warenne:
2 CONT **	i. RICHARD DE ARUNDEL, Knt., Earl of Arundel and Surrey [see next].
2 CONT **	ii. JOHN DE ARUNDEL, occurs 1373. .... etc.
2 CONT **	iii. EDMUND DE ARUNDEL, clerk, Treasurer of Chichester, Warden of the Hospital of St. Nicholas, Portsmouth. He died shortly before 24 March 1348. .... etc.
2 CONT **	iv. ELEANOR DE ARUNDEL, married (1st) before 1323 (date of settlement) WILLIAM DE SAINT JOHN, .... She married (2nd) after 3 Dec. 1329 (as his 1st wife) GERARD DE LISLE, Knt., of Stowe .... etc.
2 CONT **Pg.69
2 CONT **'''	v. ALICE DE ARUNDEL, married JOHN DE BOHUN, Knt., Earl of Hereford and Essex, Constable of England [see BOHUN 8.iii].
2 CONT **	vi. KATHERINE DE ARUNDEL, married (1st before 16 Oct. 1347 (as his 2nd wife) HENRY HUSEE (or HUSE), Knt., 2nd Lord Husee, of Harting, Sussex, Moreton, Berkshire .... His widow Katherine married (2nd) after 6 Aug. 1350 ANDREW PE
2 CONC VEREL, Knt., of Ifield, Ewhurst (in Shermanbury),  .... etc.
2 CONT **	vii. ALINE DE ARUNDEL, married ROGER LE STRANGE, Knt., 5th Lord le Strange of Knockin [see STRANGE 10].
2 CONT **	viii. ELIZABETH DE ARUNDEL, married WILLIAM LE LATIMER, K.G., 4th Lord Latimer [see SCAMPSTON 8].
2 CONT **	ix. MARY DE ARUNDEL, married JOHN LE STRANGE, Knt., 4th Lord le Strange of Blackmere [see BLACKMERE 9].
2 CONT *Pg.307
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT **'''	iii. JOHN DE BOHUNE, Knt., Earl of Hereford and Essex, Constable of England''', 2nd but 1st surviving son and heir, born in St. Clements 23 Nov. 1306. ....  '''He married (1st) by dispensation dated 22 Feb. 1325 (they being 
2 CONC related in the 4th degree of kindred) ALICE DE ARUNDEL''', daughter of Edmund de Arundel (or Fitz Alan), 9th Earl of Arundel (descendant of King John), by Alice, daughter of William de Warenne, Knt. (descendant of Geoffrey Plantag
2 CONC enet) [see FITZ ALAN 9 for her ancestry]. '''His wife, Alice died in childbirth in 1326. .... His wife Alice, was buried at Walden Abbey, He married (2nd)''' before 19 Feb. 1331 (they being related in the 4th degree of kindred) MA
2 CONC RGARET BASSET, daughter of Ralph Basset, .... SIR JOHN DE BOHUN, Earl of Hereford and Essex, died at Kirkby-Thore, Westmorland 20 Jan. 1335/6, and was buried at Stratford Abbey near London. .... etc. ___________________________
2 CONT *Links
