2 CONT John , 3rd Baron Segrave SEGRAVE
2 CONT Birth: 1314  Death: 20 MAR 1352/1353  Identification Number: IV Lord Seg  Father: Stephen John de SEGRAVE 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Alice de ARUNDEL (d. 7 FEB 1339/1340)
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1: Margaret , Duchess of Norfolk de BROTHERTON (b. 1322, Norfolk,England; d. 24 MAR 1398/1399) Marriage: 1327 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Margaret, Duchess of Norfolk From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT he married firstly in 1337 to Sir John de Segrave, 4th Baron Segrave by whom she had four children: Edmund de Segrave, died in the cradle. Elizabeth de Segrave (1338-1368), married John de Mowbray, 4th Baron Mowbray John de Segrav
2 CONC e (13 September 1340 - 1349) Anne de Segrave, Abbess of Barking
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1350, Margaret and John de Segrave began seeking a divorce based on the premise that they were contracted in marriage before she was of age, and that she had never consented to marry him. Furthermore, she had begun a relationsh
2 CONC ip with a knight of great renown, Sir Walter Manny, 1st Baron Manny, as she crossed the channel in October 1350 to meet with him in Calais, without the king's permission. The inquisition regarding this incident shows that Margaret
2 CONC  illegally crossed the Channel and met with Manny's servant, who broke his lantern with his foot so she could pass unnoticed. John de Segrave died in 1353, before their divorce could be finalized; the next year Margaret wed Walter
2 CONC  Manny shortly before 30 May 1354.
2 CONT
2 CONT =============
2 CONT
2 CONT b. 4 May 1315 d. 26 Mar. 1353 m. Margaret, Duchess of Norfolk, son of Stephen de Segrave, 3rd Lord Segrave and Alice or Aline de Arundell.
