1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#_ftnref1248
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         CARLO di Zuccarello (-1421).  A charter dated 20 Mar 1385 records a dispute between the commune of Genoa and “dominos Lazarinum et Karolum marchiones de Carreto natos quondam domini Georgiii...et vice Georgini nepotis 
2 CONC ipsorum nati quondam domini Enriceti...” concerning their fiefs, and a settlement agreed by “dominus Carolus de Carreto ex marchionibus Saone...et...Lazarinum de Carreto marchionem Saone fratrem suum...”, by charter dated 13 Jan 1
2 CONC 385[1249].  “Dominorum Manuelis quondam domini Enrici et Antonii filii quondam domini Alerami marchionum de Carreto...marchiones Savone et Cravexane”, implementing an arbitration dated 16 Apr 1385, exchanged “dimidia marchionatiis
2 CONC  Cravexane” for “medietatem...castrorum Finarii” with “dominum Manuelem quondam domini Frederici marchionis de Cravexana” by charter dated 19 Apr 1385[1250], and transferred the interest in Finali to “dominis Lazarino et Carolo ma
2 CONC rchionibus de Carreto” by charter dated 20 Apr 1385[1251].   “Dominum Lazarinum marchioniem de Carreto” bought his share in “castri...Finarii” from “dominum Karolum...frat[rem suum]” by charter dated 13 Apr 1390[1252].  Marchese d
2 CONC i Zuccarello, Signor di Balestrino e Aquila d’Arroscia, Podeste of Genoa.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (1375) POMELLINA Adorno, daughter of GABRIELE Adorno Doge of Genoa & his wife --- (Genoa [1355]-Genoa [1410/11]).  They were ancestors of the family of the Marchesi di Zaccarello.   
