2 CONT
2 CONT i)      '''    JOHANN [IV]''' (-18 May 1408).  His parentage is confirmed by the 9 Dec 1372 charter quoted below.  "Graf Rudolf von Hasbspurg, frow Elzabeth sin...frow und Graf Henseli ir sun“ granted rights to the citizens of Lau
2 CONC fenburg by charter dated 22 Nov 1377[301].  Graf von Laufenburg.  "Elsbetha Gräffin von Habsburg und Graff Hanse ir sun“ confirmed the rights granted to the citizens of Laufenburg by charter dated 25 Feb 1383 (O.S.)[302].  Landvog
2 CONC t im Thurgau, Aargau und Schwarzwald 1389, 1396/98, and 1405/06.  A contemporary manuscript of Kloster Rheinau records that "ultimum ex stirpe Habspurgo-Laufenbergica advocatum nostrum Joannem IV" died 18 May 1408[303].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' (9 Dec 1372, terminated) to HERZLAUDE von Rappoltstein, daughter of ULRICH Herr von Rappoltstein & his first wife Herzlaude von Fürstenberg (-before 18 Jun 1400).  “Graf Rudolf von Habspurg herre ze Loffenberg” pro
2 CONC mised payments to “grafe Hansen unsern sun” when he married “Ulrichen herren zu Rappoltstein...Herczeladen...tohter” by charter dated 9 Dec 1372[304].  This betrothal did not proceed as shown by the 4 Jul 1378 charter under which 
2 CONC [her uncle] Bruno Herr von Rappoltstein confirmed that he had not permitted the marriage to proceed, which resulted in legal proceedings in Nürnberg as shown by a charter dated 25 Aug 1379[305].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (after [1373] ) as her second husband, AGNES von [Hohen-]Landenberg-Greifensee, 
2 CONT '''widow''' of HANS von Wessenberg, 
2 CONT daughter of HERMANN "dem Jüngeren" von [Hohen-]Landeberg-Greifensee & his wife Adelheid von Sonnenberg.  She was created Gräfin by Imperial Order 14 May 1393[306].  1431. 
2 CONT   Graf Johann [IV] & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT ''  PLZ check whether by born around 1360, does not mean the decade: 
2 CONT otherwise, the mother would have been twelve years old.
2 CONT
