1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ben M. Angel's summary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationships:
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: William de Burgh (1312 - 1333), 3rd Earl of Ulster, murdered by the Mandevilles while en route to Parliament to be made Lord Burgh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda (Maud) de Lancaster (1310-1377), Canoness of Campsey (1347-1364), Nun at Bruisyard Abbey (1364-1377)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Only child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Lionel "of Antwerp" (1338-1368), Guardian of England (1345-1346), Earl of Ulster de iure uxoris (1347-1368), Duke of Clarence (1672-1368), Chief Governor of Ireland (1361-1365, 1367)
2 CONT
2 CONT Child: 1. Philippa (1355-1378/1381) Countess of Ulster, wife of Edmund Mortimer (1352-1381), Earl of March (to 1381), Earl of Ulster, Lord of Connaught, and Lord of Clare (1368-1381), Marshal of England (to 1376), King's Lieutenan
2 CONC t in Ireland (1379-1381)
2 CONT
2 CONT Basic information and justifications:
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:17 September 1312 at Carrickfergus Castle, County Ulster, Ireland (FMG, Wikipedia, Lundy, etc.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 10 December 1363 at Dublin (Wikipedia)
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried: Clare Priory, Clare, Suffolk, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: 4th Countess of Ulster (6 June 1333 - 10 December, 1363; FMG, Wikipedia, Lundy, etc.), Duchess of Clarence (Plaque at Clare Priory)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate names: None noted. (Was written in one source document as "Elizabetha de Borrow" but this is probably more a reflection on how her name was pronounced - much like Jedburgh in southern Scotland sounds like "Jedborrow".)
2 CONT
2 CONT Special note: Should not be confused with Elizabeth de Burgh, wife of Richard de Richmond (different person). This Elizabeth was also never married to his brother, Elyas de Richmond, or any de Richmond for that matter, a mistake t
2 CONC hat some GEDCOMs apparently transmit - check sources, this person is pretty well documented.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth_de_Burgh,_4th_Countess_of_Ulster
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10688.htm#i106872
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=16607584
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.mathematical.com/burghelizabeth1332.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 4th Countess of Ulster
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Elizabeth de Burgh, Duchess of Clarence, suo jure 4th Countess of Ulster and 5th Baroness of Connaught, was a Norman-Irish noblewoman who married Lionel of Antwerp, 1st Duke of Clarence.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth died in Dublin in 1363 during her husband's term as Governor of Ireland. She is buried in Clare Priory, Suffolk, England.
