1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT "Edward III (13 November 1312 – 21 June 1377) was King of England from 1327 until his death; he is noted for his military success and for restoring royal authority after the disastrous reign of his father, Edward II. Edward III tr
2 CONC ansformed the Kingdom of England into one of the most formidable military powers in Europe; his reign also saw vital developments in legislation and government—in particular the evolution of the English parliament—as well as the r
2 CONC avages of the Black Death. He is one of only five British monarchs to have ruled England or its successor kingdoms for more than fifty years."
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================================
