1 NOTE Edward the Black Prince (1330-76), eldest son of Edward III of England; created Duke of Cornwall (1337) and Prince of Wales (1343); commanded the van at Crecy (1346); said to be so called the Black Prince from the color of the arm
2 CONC or he wore at this battle; defeated and took captive John, king of France, at Poitiers, and brought him to London; created Prince of Aquitaine and Gascony (1362). [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
