1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''JOHN "of Gaunt", St Bavon’s Abbey, Ghent [Feb/Mar] 1340-[Leicester Castle or Ely Place, Holborn, London] 3/4 Feb 1399, bur Old St Paul’s Cathedral, London)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT s/o  EDWARD III King of England & Philippa de Hainaut 
2 CONT
2 CONT x '''Mistress (1)''': (before 1359?) MARIE de Saint-Hilaire, daughter of NN (-after 7 Apr 1399)
2 CONT >14.       BLANCHE ([1358/60?]-[1388/89]).
2 CONT
2 CONT xx (Reading Abbey 19 May 1359) '''BLANCHE of Lancaster''', daughter of HENRY Duke of Lancaster & his wife Isabel de Beaumont (25 Mar 1345-Bolingbroke Castle, Lincolnshire of the Black death 12 Sep 1369, bur Old St Paul’s Cathedral
2 CONC , London) 
2 CONT >1.         PHILIPPA (Leicester Castle 31 Mar 1360-Odivelas near Lisbon 19 Jul 1415, bur Odivelas Abbey, later removed to Batalha Abbey). 
2 CONT >2.         JOHN ([1362 or 1364]-young, bur Leicester St Mary’s Church)
2 CONT >3.         ELIZABETH (Burford, Shropshire before 21 Feb 1363-24 Nov 1425, bur Burford Church, Shropshire).  
2 CONT >4.         EDWARD ([1365]-1365, bur Leicester, St Mary’s Church). 
2 CONT >5.         JOHN (before 4 May 1366-young, bur Leicester, St Mary’s Church).
2 CONT >6.         HENRY "of Bolingbroke" (Bolingbroke Castle, Lincolnshire [3] Apr 1367-Jerusalem Chamber, Westminster Abbey 20 Mar 1413, bur Canterbury Cathedral). HENRY IV King of England 
2 CONT >7.         [ISABELLA ([1368]-young).  Weir names Isabella “born in c. 1368 and died young” as the youngest child of John of Gaunt by his first wife[1076].  The primary source on which this information is based has not been identi
2 CONC fied.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT xxx (Roquefort, Guyenne 21 Sep 1371) '''Infanta doña CONSTANZA de Castilla''', [illegitimate] daughter of PEDRO I “el Cruel” King of Castile & his mistress [first wife] doña María de Padilla (Castrojerez [Jun/Jul] 1354-Leicester C
2 CONC astile 24 Mar 1394, bur Newark Abbey, Leicester). 
2 CONT >8.         KATHERINE (Hertford Castle [6 Jun 1372/31 Mar 1373]-Valladolid 2 Jun 1418, bur Toledo). 
2 CONT >9.         JOHN “of Gaunt” (Gent [Nov 1375]-young).  
