1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alice Holland, Countess of Kent (c. 1350 – 17 March 1416), formerly Lady Alice FitzAlan, was an English noblewoman, a daughter of the 10th Earl of Arundel, and the wife of the 2nd Earl of Kent, the half-brother of 
2 CONC King Richard II. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the maternal grandmother of Anne Mortimer, thus an ancestor of King Edward IV and King Richard III. Through her daughter, Margaret, King Henry VII was her descendant. She was also the maternal grandmother of Joan Beaufort,
2 CONC  Queen of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was appointed a Lady of the Garter in 1388.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together Thomas Holland and Alice had ten children:
2 CONT # Alianore Holland (1373- October 1405), married firstly Roger Mortimer, 4th Earl of March, by whom she had issue, including Anne Mortimer and Edmund Mortimer, 5th Earl of March; she married secondly, Edward Charleton, 5th Baron C
2 CONC herleton, by whom she had two daughters.
2 CONT # Thomas Holland, 1st Duke of Surrey (1374- 7 January 1400), married Joan Stafford, but the marriage was childless.
2 CONT # John Holland (died young)
2 CONT # Richard Holland (died young)
2 CONT # Elizabeth Holland (died 4 January 1423), married Sir John Neville, Lord Neville by whom she had issue.
2 CONT # Joan Holland (1380- 12 April 1434), married firstly as his second wife, Edmund of Langley, 1st Duke of York; married secondly William de Willoughby, 5th Lord Willoughby de Eresby; married thirdly Henry le Scrope, 3rd Baron Scrop
2 CONC e of Masham, her fourth husband was Henry Bromflete, 1st Lord Vessy. All her marriages were childless.
2 CONT # Edmund Holland, 4th Earl of Kent (6 January 1384 – 15 September 1408), married Lucia Visconti[5] (1372-14 April 1424), but the marriage was childless. He fathered an illegitimate daughter Eleanor de Holland (born 1406), by his m
2 CONC istress Constance of York.
2 CONT # Margaret Holland (1385- 30 December 1439), married firstly John Beaufort, 1st Earl of Somerset, by whom she had issue including John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset and Joan Beaufort, Queen of Scotland; she married secondly Thoma
2 CONC s of Lancaster, 1st Duke of Clarence.
2 CONT # Eleanor Holland (1386- after 1413), married Thomas Montacute, 4th Earl of Salisbury, by whom she had one daughter, Alice Montacute, 5th Countess of Salisbury.
2 CONT # Bridget Holland (died before 1416), a nun at Barking Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alice_Holland,_Countess_of_Kent
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p10490.htm#i104899
2 CONT * http://www.geneall.net/U/per_page.php?id=46819
2 CONT * http://www.stepneyrobarts.co.uk/4106.htm
2 CONT * http://www.genealogy4u.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I616&tree=western2007
2 CONT * http://www.englishmonarchs.co.uk/plantagenet_77.html
2 CONT * http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p123.htm#i3680
2 CONT * http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/FITZALAN.htm#Alice FITZALAN3
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#AliceFitzAlandied14141416
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Alice Fitzalan, Countess of Kent, Lady Holand, was a daughter of Richard Fitzalan, 10th Earl of Arundel (1306 - 1376) and Eleanor of Lancaster (1318 - 1372). Alice was the wife of Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent, the half-br
2 CONC other of King Richard II of England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Alice was born in 1350 at Arundel Castle in Sussex, England, the second eldest daughter of Richard Fitzalan, '"Copped Hat", 10th Earl of Arundel, and Eleanor of Lancaster. Her paternal grandparents were Edmund Fitzalan, 9th E
2 CONC arl of Arundel, and Alice de Warenne. Her maternal grandparents were Henry, 3rd Earl of Lancaster, and Maud Chaworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice was the wife of Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent, Baron Holand ((1354 - 1397); they were married April 10, 1364, He was one of the half-brothers of the future King Richard II of England by his mother Joan of Kent's first mar
2 CONC riage to Thomas Holland, 1st Earl of Kent. Upon her marriage, Alice was styled as Lady Holand. Alice would not assume the title of Countess of Kent until 1381, when her husband was created earl.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1366, Alice's husband was appointed captain of the English forces in Aquitaine, and in 1375, he was made a Knight of the Garter. In 1377, his half-brother Richard succeeded to the throne of England, as Richard II. Alice's husba
2 CONC nd would become one of the young king's chief councillors and exert a strong influence over his brother which led to the enrichment of Thomas and Alice. In 1388, she was appointed the 23rd "Lady of the Garter" in 1388.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together Thomas and Alice had ten children:
2 CONT *Alianore Holland (1373- October 1405), married firstly Roger Mortimer, 4th Earl of March, by whom she had issue, including Anne Mortimer and Edmund Mortimer, 5th Earl of March; she married secondly, Edward Charleton, 5th Baron Ch
2 CONC erleton, by whom she had two daughters.
2 CONT *Thomas Holland, 1st Duke of Surrey (1374- 7 January 1400), married Joan Stafford, but the marriage was childless.
2 CONT *John Holland (died young)
2 CONT *Richard Holland (died young)
2 CONT *Elizabeth Holland (died 4 January 1423), married Sir John Neville, Lord Neville by whom she had issue.
2 CONT *Joan Holland (1380- 12 April 1434), married firstly as his second wife, Edmund of Langley, 1st Duke of York; married secondly William de Willoughby, 5th Lord Willoughby de Eresby; married thirdly Henry le Scrope, 3rd Baron Scrope
2 CONC  of Masham, her fourth husband was Henry Bromflete, 1st Lord Vessy. All her marriages were childless.
2 CONT *Edmund Holland, 4th Earl of Kent (6 January 1384-15 September 1408), married Lucia Visconti (1372-14 April 1424), but the marriage was childless. He fathered an illegitimate daughter Eleanor de Holland (born 1406), by his mistres
2 CONC s Constance of York.
2 CONT *Margaret de Holland (c. 1380/1385 - 30 December 1439), married firstly John Beaufort, 1st Earl of Somerset, by whom she had issue including John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset and Joan Beaufort, Queen of Scotland; she married sec
2 CONC ondly Thomas of Lancaster, 1st Duke of Clarence.
2 CONT *Eleanor Holland (1386 - after 1413), married Thomas Montacute, 4th Earl of Salisbury, by whom she had issue.
2 CONT *Bridget Holland (died before 1416), a nun at Barking Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=97917907
2 CONT
