1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie of Anjou
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Anjou (October 14, 1404–1463) was the daughter of Louis II of Anjou, King of Naples, titular King of Sicily, and Yolande of Aragon, Queen of Aragon, herself daughter of John I of Aragon.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married King Charles VII in 1422 at Bourges, and became queen consort of France. However, her husband's affection was primarily directed towards his mistress, Agnès Sorel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie was the mother of twelve children
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis XI, King of France (1423-1483)
2 CONT
2 CONT John of France (1424-1425)
2 CONT
2 CONT Radegonde de France (1428-1444)
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (1428-1446), married Charles de Charolais, future Charles le Téméraire, Duke of Burgundy, in 1440
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques de France (1432-1437)
2 CONT
2 CONT Yolande de France (1434-1478), married the future Amadeus IX, Duke of Savoy in 1452. Upon his death in 1472, she became regent of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (1435-1482), married the future John II, Duke of Bourbon in 1452
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of France (1437-1438)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary of France (7 September 1438 - 14 February 1439)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne (7 September 1438 - 26 December 1446)
2 CONT
2 CONT Magdalena of Valois (1443-1486), married Gaston de Foix,
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, Duc de Berry (1446-1472)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Anjou died in 1463 at the Abbaye de Chateliers-en-Poitou.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
