1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anna Brunswick-Grubenhagen=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Erich I, Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen and Elisabeth von Braunschweig-Göttingen
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married= 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  (1) '''Albert III, Duke of Bavaria''' on January 22 1437
2 CONT * Married: (2) 	'''Frederick III, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg''' in 1424
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.thepeerage.com/p738.htm#i7374 The Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anne von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #7374, b. circa 1414, d. 14 October 1474
2 CONT Last Edited=9 Jan 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen was born circa 1414. She was the daughter of Erich I Herzog von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen and Elisabeth von Braunschweig-Göttingen. She married, firstly, Albrecht III Herzog von Oberbayern-München,
2 CONC  son of Ernst Herzog von Oberbayern-München and Elisabetta Visconti, on 22 January 1437.1 She married, secondly, Friedrich II Herzog von Braunschweig-Kalenberg, son of Wilhelm I Herzog von Braunschweig-Lüneburg and Cecilie von Hoh
2 CONC enzollern, on 1 February 1463. She married Albrecht III Herzog von Oberbayern-München, son of Ernst Herzog von Oberbayern-München and Elisabetta Visconti.1 She died on 14 October 1474.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1 February 1463, her married name became von Braunschweig-Kalenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Anne von Braunschweig-Grubenhagen and Albrecht III Herzog von Oberbayern-München'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Johann IV Herzog von Oberbayern-München''' 1 b. 4 Oct 1437, d. 18 Nov 1463
2 CONT * '''Sigismund Herzog von Oberbayern-München''' 1 b. 1439, d. 1 Feb 1501
2 CONT * '''Margherita von Bayern''' + b. 1 Jan 1442, d. 14 Oct 1479
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth von Oberbayern-München''' +1 b. 2 Mar 1443, d. 5 Mar 1484
2 CONT * '''Albrecht IV Herzog von Bayern''' +1 b. 15 Dec 1447, d. 18 Mar 1508
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [S130] Wikipedia, online http;//www.wikipedia.org. Hereinafter cited as Wikipedia.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anna_of_Brunswick-Grubenhagen-Einbeck Anna of Brunswick-Grubenhagen-Einbeck]
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna of Brunswick-Grubenhagen-Einbeck (1414 – 4 April 1474) was a daughter of Duke Eric I of Brunswick-Grubenhagen and his wife, Elisabeth of Brunswick-Göttingen, daughter of Otto I, Duke of Brunswick-Göttingen.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anna's first marriage was with Duke Albert III of Bavaria.[1]  They had the following children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''John IV''' (1437–1463), Duke of Bavaria
2 CONT * '''Ernest''' (1438–1460)
2 CONT * '''Sigismund of Bavaria''' (1439–1501)
2 CONT * '''Albert''' (1440–1445)
2 CONT * '''Margaretha''' (1442–1479), married in 1463 with Marquess Frederick I of Mantua[1]
2 CONT * '''Elisabeth''' (1443–1484), married in 1460 with Elector Ernest of Saxony (1441–1486)
2 CONT * '''Albert IV''' (1447–1508)
2 CONT * '''Christopher''' (1449–1493)
2 CONT * '''Wolfgang''' (1451–1514)
2 CONT * '''Barbara''', a nun in Munich
2 CONT
2 CONT After Albert's death, she married Duke Frederick III of Brunswick-Calenberg-Göttingen. This marriage remained childless.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources= 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  James, Carolyn (2020). A Renaissance Marriage: The Political and Personal Alliance of Isabella d'Este & Francesco Gonzaga, 1490-1519. Oxford University Press.
