1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Louis de Faucigny'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Faucigny origin is unclear.. According to some, they were relatives and vassals of the Counts of Geneva.
2 CONT
2 CONT  The family of Faucigny gave this name to the castle to the town and a province of the Duchy of Savoy (The Faucigny ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkgenev.htm#LouisFaucignyMTetberga
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''LOUIS''' .  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 4 Sep 1119 by which his son "Wido…Gebennensis episcopus" donated "ecclesiam de Condominio" for the souls of "patris mei Ludovici et avi mei Ermenradi…" to C
2 CONC luny[315].  "Wido…Genevensis episcopus" donated "ecclesiam Sanctæ Mariæ...in villa...Contamina" to Cluny, for the souls of "avi nostri bonæ memoriæ Aimeradi et patris nostri Ludovici atque Widonis, Giserberti, Ottonis, Wilentii, a
2 CONC vunculorum nostrorum", by charter dated 1 Feb 1083 (O.S.?)[316].  Seigneur de Faucigny.  [1030]/[1060].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' as her first husband, TETBERGA, daughter of ---.  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 4 Sep 1119 by which "Wido…Gebennensis episcopus" donated "ecclesiam de Condominio" for the souls of "…matrie mee Teberge" to 
2 CONC Cluny[317].  She married secondly [as his second wife,] Géraud Comte de Genève.  Her second marriage is confirmed by the undated charter under which "Aymo comes Gebennensis et filius meus Giroldus" founded the priory of Chamonix, 
2 CONC signed by "uterini fratres comitis, Willelmus Fulciniacus et Amedeus…"[318].  
2 CONT
2 CONT    Louis & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00027363&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.geneall.net/F/per_page.php?id=516863
