2 CONT
2 CONT '''Theutberge'''
2 CONT
2 CONT  has been linked on Geni  as  Daughter of Amadeus Count of Savoy, Amadeo, I, Thiburge de Arles, Garnier de Sens, Werner ou Vernaire, Garnier de Loches, Adelaide d'Albon and Teutberge or Thiberge Count of Sens & Troyes (of Provence
2 CONC , d'Arles) however as I can find no such connection I have detached these parents making this record in case a source is found to support any of them.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BURGUNDY%20Kingdom.htm#GuillaumeFaucignydied1124A
2 CONT
2 CONT LOUIS .  His parentage is confirmed by the charter dated 4 Sep 1119 by which his son "Wido…Gebennensis episcopus" donated "ecclesiam de Condominio" for the souls of "patris mei Ludovici et avi mei Ermenradi…" to Cluny[957].  Seign
2 CONC eur de Faucigny.  [1030]/[1060].  m as her first husband, TETBERGA, daughter of ---.  Her marriage is confirmed by the charter dated 4 Sep 1119 by which "Wido…Gebennensis episcopus" donated "ecclesiam de Condominio" for the souls 
2 CONC of "…matrie mee Teberge" to Cluny[958]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  '''She married secondly [as his second wife,] Géraud Comte de Genève'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Her second marriage is confirmed by the undated charter under which "Aymo comes Gebennensis et filius meus Giroldus" founded the priory of Chamonix, signed by "uterini fratres comitis, Willelmus Fulciniacus et Amedeus…"[959].  Lou
2 CONC is & his wife had three children:
2 CONT Guillaume, Guy & Amedee Géraud Comte de Genève & Theutberge had one child: AIMON [I] ([1065/80]-12 May [1125/28]).  "Patris Geraldi et fratris Cononis, comes Aymo successor" donated property to the church of Leman, at the request 
2 CONC of "fratris Burchardi monachi", by undated charter[728].  Comte de Genève
2 CONT
2 CONT There is speculation that Geraud and his second wife first  had CONON (-before 1080).  "Cono Geraldi comitis filius" donated property to the abbey of Ainay, with the consent of "Geraldi comitis patris sui", by charter dated to [10
2 CONC 61][727].  The chronology suggests that Conon must have been considerably older than his brother Aimon [I] and therefore was probably born from his father´s [first] marriage
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/htm/of-gevena.htm#name3818
