1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humbert_de_Gen%C3%A8ve
2 CONT
2 CONT Humbert is the son of the first marriage of Count William I of Geneva and his wife Agnes , daughter of Count Amadeus III of Maurienne and sister of the future Count Humbert III of Maurienne . He seems to have been born before 1174
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Humbert has three children, one daughter and two sons. Pierre married Mathilde''(/?Maud?/)'', the daughter of the English lord Walther de Lacy''(/?Gilbert?/)'',  His wife receives part of his inheritance, following a decisio
2 CONC n of the King of England , Henry III. Peter is also mentioned in the entourage of the king, which receives some royal subsidies. An act allows to place his death before September 1249. A younger son, Ebal, who is found possessed i
2 CONC n Ireland. Alix marries Rodolphe de Grésier, "son of Rodolphe de Faucigny and head of the family of Faucigny-Lucinge"
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://translate.google.com.au/translate?hl=en&sl=fr&u=https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humbert_de_Gen%25C3%25A8ve&prev=search Translated Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/burgkgenev.htm#GuillaumeIGenevadied1196B
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         HUMBERT ([1150/60?]-before 10 May 1225).  "Willelmus…Gebennensis comes" founded the Chartreuse monstery of Pommiers, with the consent of "Humbertus filius meus…B. quoque uxor mea et filius meus Aymo quinquennis", by cha
2 CONC rter dated 1179[78].  "Wilermus Gebennensium et Valdensium comes" confirmed donations by "bonæ memorie predecessoris mei Aymonis [error for Amedei] comitis", with the consent of "Humbertus filius meus", by charter dated 1192, witn
2 CONC essed by "Turumbertus de Lucingio"[79].  Comte de Genève.  "Dominus Humbertus comes, nepos eius" confirmed the donation to Oujon by "Petrus de Ternie" [Ternier] by charter dated to [1195/1207][80].  The donor, and his precise fami
2 CONC ly relationship to Comte Humbert, have not yet been identified.  "Humbertus et Willelmus fratres et comites Gebenn." granted the prior of Saint-Victor the right to fortify the monastery by charter dated 1220[81].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Humbert's wife is not known.  Humbert & his wife had three children: 
