2 CONT Original individual @P2308129441@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@) merged with @P2308130162@ (@MS_NHFETTERLYFAMIL0@)
1 NOTE Marguerite of Geneva (d.1252) was the daughter of William I, Count of Geneva and Beatrice de Faucigny. She was supposed to become the third wife of Philip II of France but was in 1195 while on her way to Paris she was abducted by 
2 CONC Thomas I of Savoy. Thomas then married her himself, claiming that Philip II was already married (the French King had married Ingeborg of Denmark in 1193 but had repudiated her soon thereafter)
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Marguerite and Thomas I of Savoy were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Amadeus IV of Savoy (1197 - 1253) 
2 CONT Umberto (d.1223) 
2 CONT Thomas, Count of Flanders, count in Piedmont 
2 CONT Aimone (d.1237), Lord of Chablais 
2 CONT William of Savoy, Bishop of Valence and Dean of Vienne 
2 CONT Amadeo of Savoy, Bishop of Maurienne 
2 CONT Peter II of Savoy, Earl of Richmond and later disputed count of Savoy 
2 CONT Philip I of Savoy, archbishop of Lyon, later Count Palatine of Burgundy by marriageand disputed count of Savoy in 1268 
2 CONT Boniface of Savoy, Archbishop of Canterbury 
2 CONT Beatrice of Savoy (1205- 4 January 1267), wife of Ramon Berenguer IV, Count of Provence. She was married in 1219 and was mother to four queens consort 
2 CONT Alasia of Savoy (d.1250), abbess of St Pierre, Lyon 
2 CONT Agatha of Savoy (d.1245), abbess of St Pierre, Lyon 
2 CONT Margherita of Savoy (d.1273), wife of Hartmann I of Kyburg 
2 CONT Avita of Savoy (1215-92), wife of Baldwin de Redvers, 7th Earl of Devon and later of Robert Aguillon (d.1286) 
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT Marguerite (Beatrix) of Geneva 
