2 CONT '''Pope Innocent IV''' (Latin: Innocentius IV; c. 1195 – 7 December 1254), born '''Sinibaldo Fieschi''', was head of the Catholic Church and ruler of the Papal States from 25 June 1243 to his death in 1254.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fieschi was born in Genoa and studied at the universities of Parma and Bologna. He was considered in his own day and by posterity as a fine canonist. On the strength of this reputation, he was called to the Roman Curia by [https:/
2 CONC /www.geni.com/people/Cencio-Savelli-papa-Onorio-III/6000000071766422896 Pope Honorius III]. [https://www.geni.com/people/Papa-Gregorio-IX/6000000091079224839 Pope Gregory IX] made him a cardinal and appointed him governor of the M
2 CONC arch of Ancona in 1235. Fieschi was elected pope in 1243 and took the name Innocent IV. As pope, he inherited an ongoing dispute over lands seized by the Holy Roman Emperor, and the following year he traveled to France to escape i
2 CONC mperial plots against him in Rome. He returned to Rome after the death in 1250 of the [https://www.geni.com/people/Federico-II-imperatore-dei-Romani/6000000000424888017 Emperor Frederick II].
2 CONT
