1 OCCU Première propriétaire historiquement attestée du Suaire de Turin
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Joan of Vergy
2 CONT *Death: May 23, 1428
2 CONT *Family: House of Vergy
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne de Vergy married Geoffroi de Charny († 1356) after the death of his first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She is particularly known because of the appearance of the Shroud of Turin in the collegiate church founded by her husband in 1353, at Lirey , in Aube; his coat of arms is present on a sign of pilgrimage found in the depot of Pont
2 CONC  au Change, in Paris. Printed cloth was the subject of ostensions in this collegiate church around 1355, according to an account by the Bishop of Troyes Pierre d'Arcis , in 1389, who relates how his predecessor Henri de Poitiers c
2 CONC aused this cult to cease. The sign of pilgrimage bears her coat of arms and that of her husband and it seems to date from this time of the first ostensions of the object.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1389, his son Geoffroy II de Charny took over the ostensions of the sheet, then called "figure or representation of the Shroud of Christ", despite the prohibition of Pierre d'Arcis who affirms that the Shroud is an image made t
2 CONC o extort money to the faithful. The de Charny family obtained permission from Pope Clement VII , relative of Jeanne's second husband, Aymon de Genève, son of Hugues de Genève , lord of Anthon and member of a younger branch of the 
2 CONC county family of Geneva [ 5 ] .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “The Charny Genealogy.” By Dorothy Crispino
2 CONT <[https://www.shroud.com/pdfs/ssi37part5.pdf PDF]>. Page 19-20
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffroy de Charny and Jeanne de Vergy had two children, Charlotte and Geoffroy II. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1340, Charlotte mar. Bertrand de Chazans, bringing him the seigniory of Missery, just below Mont-Saint-Jean (C 124, A 203).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffroy II mar. Marguerite de Poitiers, dau. of Charles de Poitiers (and niece of Henri de Poitiers who, according to Pierre d'Arcis, his successor as bishop of Troyes, had discovered the artist who painted the Lirey Shroud). The
2 CONC ir children were Marguerite and Henriette, who mar. a Lord of Clermont; and maybe Jeanne. Geoffroy II and his dau. Marguerite, who left no issue, are treated in another section.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sign of the Pilgrimage of Lirey representing the Shroud of Turin (sketch by Arthur Forgeais, 1865)
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000185551266950&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeanne_de_Vergy
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geoffroi_de_Charny
2 CONT *https://gw.geneanet.org/wailly?lang=en&n=de+vergy&oc=1&p=jeanne shows parents as Guillaume III de VERGY †1360/ (Seigneur de Mirebeau et Fontaine Françoise) & Agnès de DURNES 1280-/1356 (Dame de Chateau Neuf de Vuillafans (25))
2 CONT * André Duchesne, Histoire Généalogique de la Maison de Vergy (Paris, 1625), p.387
