1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo_I_di_Monaco /!\
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT -http://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/carlo-grimaldi_(Dizionario-Biografico)/  - Figlio di Raniero (I) e di Margherita Ruffo dei conti di Sinopoli, nacque alla fine del XIII secolo, forse in Calabria. Scarse sono le notizie circa i
2 CONC  suoi primi anni, vissuti al seguito del padre nelle sue peregrinazioni tra Provenza, Francia e Italia meridionale dove probabilmente, presso i familiari della madre, potenti baroni della Calabria Ulteriore, trascorse l'infanzia. 
2 CONC ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Qui il G. morì nello stesso 1357, non si sa se per malattia o in combattimento; egli era però di certo defunto quando, agli inizi di settembre, 
2 CONT *il figlio Raniero (II) scendeva a patti con i Genovesi per la resa di Monaco e di Roccabruna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dal matrimonio con Luchinetta Spinola, figlia di Gherardo, signore di Lucca e di Tortona, il G. ebbe diversi figli, tra i quali vanno ricordati 
2 CONT *Lancillotto 
2 CONT *e Ruffo (che furono entrambi consiglieri e ciambellani della regina Giovanna), 
2 CONT *Giovanni Francesco 
2 CONT *e Carlo che, sposo di Porzia Sanseverino, fu capostipite della linea siciliana della famiglia.
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/provnice.htm#CarloIGrimaldidied1357B<br/>
2 CONT CARLO [I] Grimaldi, son of RANIERO [I] Grimaldi & his first wife --- (-[8 Apr/17 Oct] 1357).  Robert King of Sicily notified payment to “Carolo de Grimaldis militi” for services during the siege of Trapani by charter dated 26 Aug 
2 CONC 1314[153].  Barone di San Demetrio in Calabria: King Robert notified his justiciar in Calabria of rights relating to the “baronia S. Demetrii”, the fief of “Carolus de Grimaldi de Janua miles filius et heres quondam Raynerii de Gr
2 CONC imaldis militis”, by charter dated 7 Apr 1315[154].  A charter dated 24 Oct 1319 records an arbitrated dispute between “Iohannem Baudum militem regium cambellanum comitatus Provincie et Forcalquerii senescallum” and “dominum Morru
2 CONC helem de Auria” concerning “Dulceaqua”, naming “...dnus Carolus et dnus Barnaba de Grimaldis”[155].  He recaptured Monaco in 1331[156].  “Vinciguerra Grimaldis de Janua dominus baronie Sancti Demetrii, parcium Calabrie” renounced 
2 CONC rights in favour of “dominum Karolum de Grimaldis de Janua militem fratrem suum” by charter dated 27 Jan 1334[157].  A charter dated 25 May 1335 records that “in civitate Vintimilii...castrum de Rocha” was captured in the name of 
2 CONC Robert King of Sicily, in presence of “domino Karollo de Grimaldis milite, domino Agamellono de Grimaldis usque nunc potestate civitatis eiusdem”[158].  “Dominus Carolus de Grimaldis miles...Martinus de Grimaldis...Agamelonus de G
2 CONC rimaldis...Vicecomes de Grimaldis...Aimonus de Grimaldis...Manuel de Grimaldis...” agreed with Philippe VI King of France to arm ships to fight the English by charter dated 12 Feb 1338[159].  A charter dated 2 Feb 1341 records a t
2 CONC reaty between “domini Symonis Boccanegre...Januensium ducis...” and “domini Karoli de Grimaldis militis [...Gabrieli de Grimaldis quondam Ghasparis], Antonii de Grimaldis...”, including rights in “terra Monaco castro...terra Roche
2 CONC brune...Castro Francho”[160].  He fought in Brittany 1341-1343: a charter dated 1 Sep 1342 records the participation of “chevalier Charles de Grimauls...[Grimalt]...capitaine des Genevois de Morgue et conseillier du roy de France”
2 CONC  in the war in Brittany, while a charter dated 22 May 1343 records payments to him for his services[161].  Jeanne Queen of Sicily ordered payments to “Carolo de Grimaldis militi et Antonio de Grimaldis” for “manutencionis custodie
2 CONC  castri Monaci” by charter dated 3 Jun 1343[162].  Jeanne Queen of Sicily confirmed the offices of “vicariorum nostrorum comitatuum Provincie e Forcalquerii” granted to “Caroli de Grimaldis de Janua et Antonii de Grimaldis fratrum
2 CONC ” by her grandfather by charter dated 27 Mar 1344[163].  He acquired the Seigneurie de Menton in 1346: “Nobilis vir Manuel Venti de Janua dominus in parte castri de Menthono...Raffi Venti fratris sui et...Arahoni Venti nepotis sui
2 CONC , filii quondam...Andaroni Venti, condominorum...dicti castri Menthoni” granted “castrum de Menthono et territorium ipsius” to “domino Karolo de Grimaldis militis de Janua”, in the presence of “...Nicholoxio de Grimaldis filio dom
2 CONC ini Anthonii de Grimaldi de Janua”, by charter dated 19 Apr 1346[164].   Co-seigneur de Monaco: “Charles Grimaldi chevalier seigneur de Menton et Antoine Grimaldi” acknowledged holding “les biens, terre, château...de Monaco par in
2 CONC divis entre eux et par moitié” by charter dated 29 Jun 1352[165].  “Dominus Petrus Lascharis...comes Ventimilii” sold “castrum villam seu terram Rochebrune...in dyocessi civitatis Ventimilii” to “domini Caroli de Grimaldis militis
2 CONC ” by charter dated 2 Jan 1355[166].  A charter dated 25 Dec 1356 records an alliance between Pisa and “domino Karolo de Grimaldis et eius filio...et pro dominis Agamenone, Richerio, Lanzelocto et Perino de Grimaldis...qui...habita
2 CONC nt in civitatibus Nitie et Vintimidie et in castris et terris Monaci et Mentonis”[167].  “Carolus de Grimaldis milex” leased land “in Turbie loco...ad Crosetum” by charter dated 8 Apr 1357[168].  He is named as deceased in the 17 
2 CONC Oct 1357 charter quoted below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ISABELLA, daughter of --- (-before ).  She is named as mother of Carlo’s son Ranieri [II] in the charter dated 17 Jul 1353, quoted below, which notes “dotem domine Ysabelle quondam matris dicti domini Raynerii”[169].  The 
2 CONC [1534] Libro de la progenie et vita de li ill. signore de Monago names “signora Luchineta, Genovesa” as the wife of “signor Carolo”[170].  Père Anselme, following Venasque[171], names “Luchinette Spinola fille de Gerard de Spinola
2 CONC  seigneur de Dertonne” as the wife of Carlo Grimaldi and mother of his son Ranieri [II][172].  All these indications seem to be disproved by the 17 Jul 1353 charter quoted above. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Carlo & his wife had seven children: 
