2 CONT - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MONFERRATO,%20SALUZZO,%20SAVONA.htm#ManfredoISaluzzodied1175
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         MANFREDO (-[4 Jun 1175/Mar 1176], bur Staffarda).  "Bonifacius marchio filius Teutonis…marchio…cum Alice cometissa filia qd. d. Petri marchio atque Theotone, Petro, Magnifredo, Hugone et Willielmo filiis eorum" donated 
2 CONC property to "monasterio sancti Petri…in…villa Saviliani" by charter dated 21 Dec 1099[444].  Marchese di Saluzzo. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT Manfred I (died 1175) was the first margrave of Saluzzo in the last year of his life alone, being an old man when the Emperor Frederick I appointed him margrave. He was the eldest son of Boniface del Vasto, the margrave of Western
2 CONC  Liguria, of a noble stock which had ruled the region between Savona and Ventimiglia for generations. Boniface received the county of Saluzzo in feudum directly from its suzerain, Ulric Manfred, margrave of Turin, and gave it to h
2 CONC is son. The county comprised the land between the Alps, the Po River, and the Stura. Manfred transmitted the margravate to his son by Eleanor, Manfred II, and the dynasty which reigned until the Renaissance was born.
