2 CONT
2 CONT '''ANSELMO del Vasto''', son of BONIFAZIO Marchese del Vasto & his [first/second] wife [Alix de Savoie/Agnès de Vermandois] (-after 1140).  "Bonifacius marchio" appointed "filiis suos Maginfredum et Wilielmum adque Ugonem necnon A
2 CONC nselmum…et Anricum et Bonefacium minorem atque Odonem" as his heirs but disinherited "Bonifacium…incixie nominatum" by charter dated 1125[873].  That he may have been born from the first marriage of his father is suggested by the 
2 CONC charter dated 1196 under which his son "Bonifacius marchio de Cravexana" confirmed a donation to the monastery of San Stefano by "comitissa Adalasia avia mea"[874].  However, this charter could also refer to Bonifazio´s maternal g
2 CONC randmother, mother of Anselmo´s wife who is not otherwise known.  "Marchiones filii domni Bonefatii…Manfredus, Wilielmus, Ugo, Anselmus, Enricus, Oddo Bouarius" donated property to the monastery of Staffarda by charter dated 9 Dec
2 CONC  1138[875].  A charter dated 1140 records the agreement between the people of Genoa and "marchiones filios Bonefacii…Manfredum et Hugonem et Anselmum et Henricum et Ottonem", promising not to make war secretly with "Oberto comite 
2 CONC Vintimillii" with the permission of Genoa[876].  Marchese di Ceva: a charter dated 22 Dec 1142 records the division of territories agreed between "Marchiones de Vasto…Mainfredum, Willielmum, Hugonem, Anselmum, Heinricum, Bonifaciu
2 CONC m et Oddonem filios quondam Bonifacii marchionis", under which Anselmo took "marchionatus Ceve"[877]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Anselmo's wife is not known.  Her son "Bonifacius marchio de Cravexana" confirmed a donation to the monastery of San Stefano by "comitissa Adalasia avia mea"[878].  As noted above, it is not known whether
2 CONC  this document refers to Bonifazio´s maternal or paternal grandmother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Anselmo & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT # GUGLIELMO [I] (-after 10 Nov 1204). Marchese di Ceva....
2 CONT # BONIFAZIO (-after 27 Sep 1223).... Marchese di Clavesana...
2 CONT
2 CONT ------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother dispute:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boniface_del_Vasto
2 CONT
2 CONT Boniface is sometimes said to have married Alice of Savoy, the daughter of Peter of Savoy.[3] This is unlikely, however, since Boniface and Alice were first-cousins-once-removed (Boniface's mother Bertha and Alice's grandmother Ad
2 CONC elaide were sisters), and thus far too closely related to be permitted to marry according to canon law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Boniface married Agnes, daughter of Hugh, Count of Vermandois.[4]
2 CONT
