2 CONT '''BONIFAZIO di Ceva''', son of ANSELMO del Vasto Marchese di Ceva e Clavesana & his wife --- (-after 27 Sep 1223).  A charter dated Oct 1198 records an agreement between Bonifazio Bishop of Asti and "Wiermus de Ceva", who confirm
2 CONC s that "dominum Bonefacium fratrem et nepotes suos et dominum Othonem et Henricum de Carreto" will respect it[935].  Marchese di Clavesana.  "Bonifacius marchio de Cravexana" confirmed a donation to the monastery of San Stefano by
2 CONC  "comitissa Adalasia avia mea" by charter dated 1196[936].  "Dominus Oto de Carreto marchio et Henricus marchio frater eius et Guillelmus dominus de Ceua et Bonifacius marchio de Crauesana frater eius" donated property to the mona
2 CONC stery of Santa Maria di Casanova by charter dated 10 Nov 1204[937].  "Bonifacius filius Anselmi, marchesus Clavesanæ" sold "villam Bibiæ" to "Mainfredo II marcheso Salutiarum" by charter dated 27 Nov 1205[938].  Marchese di Claves
2 CONC ana.  The Annals of Ogerio Panis record that "Conrado et Opitione marchionibus Malaspine, Ottone atque Enrico marchionibus de Carretto, Bonifatio marchione Crauexane, filio Wilielmi marchionis de Ceua" attacked Ventimiglia in 1219
2 CONC [939].  "Dominus Bonifacius Marchio Cravexanæ" donated property by way of testament made "in infirmitate sua" to "ecclesiæ Sanctæ Mariæ de Casulis" by charter dated Mar 1221[940].  Manfredo III Marchese di Saluzzo invested "dominu
2 CONC m Guillelmum marchionem de Busca" with his fee in return for allegiance by charter dated 27 Sep 1223, witnessed by "Dominus Bonifacius marchio de Ceva, Gratapalea, Guillelmus de Verçolio…"[941]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name of Bonifazio´s wife is not known.  Bonifazio & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         BONIFAZIO "Taliaferio" (-after 3 Jul 1237).  Marchese di Clavesana.   
2 CONT * 2.         OTTONE (-[1 Jul 1228/16 Sep 1233]).  A charter dated 10 Oct 1226 records an arbitration between the archdeacon of Alba and "dominum Octonem marchionem Cravexane" regarding disputes involving Ormea and Teco[1033].  m a
2 CONC s her [second/third] husband, MABILIA, widow firstly of FULCO di Castro and secondly of BONIFAZIO di Volta, daughter of -- (-[16 Jun 1248/14 Mar 1251]). Ottone & his wife had six children:  … 
2 CONT * 3.         BERTA di Clavesana (-after 1224).   … m (before 9 Aug 1202) as his second wife, GUGLIELMO di Monferrato, son of BONIFAZIO Marchese di Monferrato & his first wife Elena di Busca ([1180]-17 Sep 1225).  He succeeded his 
2 CONC father in 1207 as GUGLIELMO VI Marchese di Monferrato.  
