2 CONC  Sicile…Constance"[564].  The Historia Sicula of Bartolomeo di Neocastro names "Alfonsus, Elisabeth regina Portugalli…Rex Iacobus, Dominus Fridericus, domina Violanta et dominus Petrus" as the children of "Petro regi Aragonum" and
2 CONC  his wife[565].  The Chronicle of Ramon Muntaner records the death of "l´infant Pierre…ainsi que Raimond d´Anglesola" at the siege of León and their burial in adjacent graves in Aragon[566].  m (28 Aug 1291) GUILLELMA de Béarn, da
2 CONC ughter of GASTON [VII] de Moncada Vicomte de Béarn & his first wife Mathe [Amata] de Marsan [Mastas] Ctss de Bigorre ([1245/55]-1309).  The Chronicle of Ramon Muntaner records the marriage of "l´infant Pierre" and "madame Guillelm
2 CONC ine de Muncada, fille de Gaston de Béarn", dated to 1295[567].  She had previously been betrothed to Alfonso Manuel, and later to the latter's first cousin the future Sancho IV King of Castile.  Pedro had two illegitimate children
2 CONC  by unknown mistresses: 
