2 CONT ['''AGATHE de Savoie''' (-after 1279).  Guichenon names Agathe as daughter of Comte Thomas I and his wife, stating that she was nun and later abbess of Saint-Pierre, Lyon in  1279, referring to "Titre de l´abbaye de Saint-Pierre d
2 CONC e Lyon" with no precise citation reference[461].  She is not mentioned in the 11 Oct 1264 testament of her supposed brother Boniface Archbishop of Canterbury (which refers to his "sister the Ctss of Provence" and his "other sister
2 CONC  the Ctss of Quibourc")[462], although this is not conclusive to dismiss her affiliation.  One possibility is that Agathe was the illegitimate daughter of Comte Thomas I.] 
