2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Maude or Matilda de Percy de Neville
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud de Percy was born circa 1335 at Alnwick Castle, Northumberland, England. She was the daughter of Sir Henry Percy, 2nd Lord Percy and Idoine de Clifford. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Sir John de Neville, 3rd Baron Neville, son of Ralph de Neville, 2nd Lord Neville and Alice Audley, in July 1357 in a Alnwick, Northumberland, England. They had seven children:
2 CONT * Ralph Neville, 1st Earl of Westmorland
2 CONT * Thomas Neville, 5th Baron Furnivall
2 CONT * Idione Neville
2 CONT * Alice Neville, wife of William Deincourt, 3rd Baron Deincourt
2 CONT * Maud Neville
2 CONT * Elizabeth de Neville, a nun
2 CONT * Eleanor Neville, wife of Ralph de Lumley, 1st Baron Lumley
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud died in 1379 at Raby Castle, Durham, England. 
