1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Here is what Stirnet says on the subject:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Boteler of Wemme, 2nd Lord (b 08.09.1298, d 12.1361)
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Margaret FitzAlan (dau of Richard FitzAlan, 7th Earl of Arundel)
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) We are following TCP (Boteler of Wem) and BE1883 in showing this William as married only once, to Margaret FitzAlan. Visitation shows the same but, as it shows William as son of the Ralph who married Maude Pantulf, thereby mis
2 CONC sing out 2 generations, it loses some credibility. Visitation shows this William as father of another William (m. Ella Handslagh or Hansacre) who had 2 sons: William who married Johanna Sudeley and Ralph, who married _ Hanlow, fat
2 CONC her of the heiress Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) BE1883 (Boteler) identifies the following William's wife as Joane Sudeley, dau of John, Lord Sudeley, but does not report having a son by her, only his dau/heiress Elizabeth. BE1883 (Sudeley) identifies Joan's husband as "Will
2 CONC iam Boteler, of Wemme", showing them as having a son Thomas who inherited Sudeley Castle. TCP (Boteler of Wem) identifies (the following) William's wife merely as "Elizabeth" and confirms that they dspm.
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) It appears that some sites identify Joan Sudeley as second wife of this William (2nd Lord), possibly in an attempt to explain why the barony of Wemme did not pass to Thomas, son of the William who married Joane Sudeley. Joan's
2 CONC  husband is described in TCP (Sudeley) as "William le Botiler (Boteler), knight" which refers by note to Dugdale's 'Baronage' (vol i) where this William is shown as having had 2 sons both called William, the younger married to Joa
2 CONC n Sudeley. We are suspicious about this and provisionally continue to show this 2nd William and his descendants on Sudeley1.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan de Sudeley was the daughter of John de Sudeley, 2nd Lord Sudeley and Eleanor de Scales.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William le Botiler, son of William le Botiler, 1st Lord le Botiller and Beatrice (?), before 1355.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died before August 1367.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      From before 1355, her married name became le Botiler.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Joan de Sudeley and William le Botiler
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Thomas le Botiler, 4th Lord Sudeley1
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. [S2] Peter W. Hammond, editor, The Complete Peerage or a History of the House of Lords and All its Members From the Earliest Times, Volume XIV: Addenda & Corrigenda (Stroud, Gloucestershire, U.K.: Sutton Publishing, 1998), p
2 CONC age 101. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage, Volume XIV.
