2 CONT      Thomas le Botiler, 4th Lord Sudeley is the son of William le Botiler and Joan de Sudeley.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      Thomas le Botiler, 4th Lord Sudeley succeeded to the title of 4th Lord Sudeley in 1379.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S2] Peter W. Hammond, editor, The Complete Peerage or a History of the House of Lords and All its Members From the Earliest Times, Volume XIV: Addenda & Corrigenda (Stroud, Gloucestershire, U.K.: Sutton Publishing, 1998), page 10
2 CONC 1. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage, Volume XIV.
2 CONT
2 CONT Complete Peerage, 12 (1) (1953): 418 identifies the wife of Sir Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT le Boteler, 4th Lord Sudeley (and mother of his children), simply as
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice:
2 CONT
2 CONT "He married, on or before 18 July 1385, Alice."
2 CONT
2 CONT The Coll. Top. et Gen. account reads as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT "The wife of this Thomas Boteler was Alicia, daughter of Sir John
2 CONT
2 CONT Beauchamp of Powyke, Knt., by whom he had issue four sons, John,
2 CONT
2 CONT William, Thomas, and Ralph, and four daughters, Elizabeth, Jane,
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, and Eleanor. All of the sons except Ralph died issueless,
2 CONT
2 CONT and two of the daughters, Margaret and Eleanor, died unmarried."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
