2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p804.htm#i24152 http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Thomas-Boteler-4th-Baron-Sudeley/6000000006444385831?through=6000000007151199993
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas le Boteler bio 4th baron, de jure. JP & MP for Glos. Nephew and ultimately sole heir of John Sudeley, 3rd Lord Sudeley, on or before 18 July 1385 he married Alice Beauchamp and, by November 1388, was knighted. From 1394 til
2 CONC l 1398 he was Justice of the Peace for Gloucestershire, then in 1397 Knight of the Shire of Gloucester.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1390 he made a pilgrimage to the Holy Land, but, while at the Holy Sepulchre and other sacred places, he ate and drank with the Saracens for which, by June 1391, he was excommunicated by Pope Boniface IX. In March 1392 he was g
2 CONC ranted absolution and released from excommunication, having paid a sum to the papal collector equivalent to the expenses of the uncompleted portion of his pilgrimage. (Genealogics)
