2 CONT **compiled by JOHN LUCHER DALTON 1889
2 CONT *   A copy was obtained from Voyla Dalton Smith, the daughter of John Luther Dalton and a copy of the Dalton pedigree chart sent to Sarah Cedenia Dalton of Parowan, Utah, by John Luther Dalton. 
2 CONT *   In a letter sent to me, dated March 19, 1960, Mrs. Voyla Dalton Smith has this to say, "Father left on a mission to England the 28th of April 1863 and re- turned 1866. He also made a subsequent trip to England for genealogical
2 CONC  research in 1888 and compiled his findings in 1889. Father never put down the source of his information as I have indicated but Mother said that he searched histories, deeds, wills, cemetery records and etc." 
2 CONT *— 1 —    
2 CONT *   LeSieur or Sire de Dalton came from Normany, France, in 1135 A.D. with King Henry II of England. 
2 CONT *   The eldest son John was granted on the death of his father, the Manors of Dalton and Byspham in Lancashire, England. He executed a deed in favor of his eldest son John 1193 A.D. He had two sons. 
2 CONT *— 2 — 
2 CONT *   John Dalton or Doldon was given a deed 1193 A.D. Lancashire, England. Simon de Dalton was mentioned in a deed 1190 A.D. Lancashire, England. 
2 CONT *   *Note — In the Sarah Cedenia Dalton copy "The eldest son John executed a deed in favor of his eldest son third John 1193 A.D." 
2 CONT *— 3 — 
2 CONT *   (1) Sir Richard, eldest son of John, was a crusader in the Holy Land 1187 A.D. He killed several Saracens. From this the family takes the green griffin in its crest. He was buried at Dalton with his legs crossed. 
2 CONT *   (2) His brother was John Dalton or second John. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/johndaltonbookof00dalt#page/26/mode/1up
2 CONT *— 4 — 
2 CONT *   Sir Richard, eldest son of Sir Richard (3), married Miss Lawrence in 1277, Lancashire, England. His signature to a deed 1282 A.D. is still extant. 
2 CONT *— 5 — 
2 CONT *   His eldest son Sir Robert, married the daughter of Sir Thomas Latymer or Latham. 
2 CONT *— 6 — 
2 CONT *'''   His son Sir John, married Alice Hussey 1327 A.D.''', daughter of Sir Henry Hussey of Lancashire. Received lands in 1327. 
2 CONT *— 7 —
2 CONT *   His '''eldest son''', Sir John, bore arms as a Knight in 1389, and was given a deed 1359. He married Miss Pilkington, daughter of Sir Richard Pilkington. 
2 CONT *— 8 — 
2 CONT *   His son, Robert Dalton, married Margaret Holker, 1444, Lancashire, England. 
2 CONT *— 9 — 
2 CONT *   Richard Dalton married Miss Hesie or Heine (Fleming) 
2 CONT *— 10 — 
2 CONT *   His son Roger Dalton of Lancashire, married his second cousin Margaret Stanley. 
2 CONT *— 11 — 
2 CONT *   Their son Richard, married Jane Whitaker 
2 CONT *— 12 — 
2 CONT *   Roger Dalton married twice, first Miss Radcliff of Wymerly 
2 CONT *— 13 — 
2 CONT *   Their son William, 1513, Byspham, Lancashire, also married twice. He had no children by his first wife, and his second wife was Jane Townley or Towerly. By her he had three sons. 
2 CONT *— 14 — 
2 CONT *   1 -Robert Dalton, married Ann Kitchin and he died without male issue. 
2 CONT *   2-Thomas Dalton, married Ann Molyneux. Thomas inherited Thurnham and other properties and his descendants in the female line have lived at Thurnham Hall up till about thirty years ago. 
2 CONT *   3 -Roger Dalton (Our Line) married Mary Ward or Warer of Lancashire. 
2 CONT *— 15 — 
2 CONT *   Walter Dalton, born 1552, died 1619, Whitney, Oxfordshire, England. He married Margaret of Lancashire and had issue. 
2 CONT *— 16 — 
2 CONT *   1 -Walter Dalton (Our Line) born 1582, Whitney, Oxford and died 1650. He married Elizabeth of Curbridge, Oxford and had issue ( 17) . 
2 CONT *   2-Edward Dalton, born 1590, Whitney, Oxford, England. He went to Ireland, then afterward to America. 
2 CONT *— 17 — 
2 CONT *   1-Walter Dalton (Our ancestor) born 1603, Whitney, Oxford, England. He died 1666. Married Jane Needham. 
2 CONT *   2-Charles Dalton, born 1605, Whitney, Oxford, England died 23 Oct. 1707. 
2 CONT *   3 -Elizabeth Dalton, born 1609, Whitney, Oxford, England — died young. 
2 CONT *   4-Thomas Dalton, born 1611, Whitney, Oxford England — died young. 
2 CONT *   5-William Dalton, born 1614, Whitney, Oxford, England — died young. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/johndaltonbookof00dalt#page/27/mode/1up 
2 CONT *   6-Andrew Dalton, born 1616, Whitney, Oxford, England. He died in 1721. The last of his descendants as far as could be traced was William, who died 1850. 
2 CONT *   7-Johanna 
2 CONT *   Walter Dalton, born 1603, the eldest son of Walter (Our Ancestor) married Jane Needham and left issue. After the battle of Worchester he settled in South Wales about 1651. Walter Dalton died 1666 and Jane Needham died May 1, 1
2 CONC 714. Children: 
2 CONT *— 18 — 
2 CONT *   1 -Charles Dalton, born 1639, Whitney, Oxford, England, died 23 Oct. 1707. Married Jane Shedd or Shead. They had nine children, none of the sons left issue. 
2 CONT *   2-Thomas Dalton, born 1643, Whitney, Oxford, England — died young. 
2 CONT *   3-Ormand Dalton, born 1645, Whitney, Oxford, England — died young. 
2 CONT *   4- Walter Dalton, born 1648, Whitney, Oxford, England — died young. 
2 CONT *   5-James Dalton (Our Line), born 1650, Whitney, Oxford, England died May 15, 1721 — He married Joyce Vaughn, 1677. She was the daughter of Rowland Vaughn. She was born 1647 Pembrey, Carmarthanshire, Wales, and died March 14, 17
2 CONC 31. 
2 CONT *   6-Johanna, born 1653 — Married James Butler. 
2 CONT *   James Dalton, born 1650, married Joyce Vaughn, 1677. They left issue. 
2 CONT * .... etc. ______________
2 CONT *	'Dalton01'
2 CONT *Sir Richard Dalton of Bypsam, Lancashire
