2 CONT England Kings https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLAND,%20Kings%201066-1603.htm#E...
2 CONT 6. ELEANOR ([1318]–Arundel Castle, Sussex 11 Jan 1372, bur Lewes Priory, Sussex). While her first husband was still alive, she lived with her future second husband who had his first marriage[1043] annulled in order to marry her. T
2 CONC he will of "Richard Earl of Arundel and Surrey", dated 5 Dec 1375, chose burial “in...the priory of Lewes near to the tomb of Eleanor of Lancaster my wife”[1044]. m firstly (before Jun 1337) JOHN de Beaumont, son of HENRY de Beaum
2 CONC ont[-de Brienne] Lord Beaumont Earl of Buchan [Constable of England] & his wife Alice Comyn Ctss of Buchan (–[10/25] May 1342). He succeeded his father in 1340 as Lord Beaumont. m secondly (Ditton Church, Stoke Poges, Buckinghamsh
2 CONC ire 5 Feb 1345, Papal dispensation 4 Mar 1345) as his second wife, RICHARD Fitzalan Earl of Arundel "Copped hat", son of EDMUND Fitzalan Earl of Arundel & his wife Alice de Warenne ([1313]–Arundel 24 Jan 1376, bur Lewes Priory, Su
2 CONC ssex).
2 CONT
2 CONT English Lords A–C – John de Beaumont: https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#JohnB...
2 CONT England Earls Created 1138-1142 – Richard FitzAlan: https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm...
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT "Eleanor of Lancaster, Countess of Arundel (sometimes called Eleanor Plantagenet; 11 September 1311-1318 – 11 January 1372) was the fifth daughter of Henry, 3rd Earl of Lancaster and Maud Chaworth."
2 CONT
