2 CONT Thomas Arundel (1353-1414). Archbishop of Canterbury in 1397 and from 1399 until his death in 1414. He persecuted the Lollards, a group calling for reform of the Catholic Church by promoting a lay priesthood and translations of th
2 CONC e Bible. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2005/2006, BBC History Magazine chose Thomas Arundel as the 15th century's entry for their Ten Worst Britons poll. On the final list of 10 Worst Britons, he tied for 9th place with Hugh Despenser, The Younger.
2 CONT
