1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Joan Le Strange
2 CONT ''Last updated 27 July 2025''
2 CONT * Born: ABT 1356
2 CONT * Died: BEF Nov 1399, Basing, Hampshire, England
2 CONT * Notes: not sure if she was the daughter or the sister of Roger, sixth Baron of Knockyn.
2 CONT * Father: Roger Le STRANGE (6º B. Strange of Knockin)
2 CONT * Mother: Alaive FITZALAN (B. Strange of Knockin)
2 CONT * Married: Thomas De POYNINGS (1º B. St. John of Basing) 1372, Basing, Hampshire, England.  His first wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Luke De POYNINGS
2 CONT * 2. Hugh De POYNINGS (Sir Knight)
2 CONT * 3. Isabel De POYNINGS (b. 1385 - d. AFT 1428)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/STRANGE.htm#Joan Le STRANGE2
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Poynings family
2 CONT
2 CONT From Sussex Archaeological Society. Sussex archaeological collections relating to the history and antiquities of the county. (1863) “Poynings Pedigree.” Page 17. < Archive.Org >; (document attached)
2 CONT
2 CONT L. P., Baron St. John = Isabella
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas Poynings, de St. John, chivaler; aet. 36 and upw. at death of his mother; ob. 7 March, 1429; bu. at Boxgrove.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Joan, d. of Roger, Lord Strange; ob. 1398. 1st wife.
2 CONT * Phillippa, d. of Edm. Mortimer, 3rd Earl of March, w° of John, Earl of Pembroke and Rich., 14th Earl of Arundel; ob. 26 Sep., 1400; bu. at Boxgrove. 2d wife.
2 CONT * Margaret, 2d d. and co-h. of Sir Nigel Loring, w° of Sir Thomas Pevre, of Bedford. 3d wife.
2 CONT * Maude, extrix. of her husb., re-m. Hugh Halsham ; ob. 3d June, 1453. (Inq. p. in.) 4th wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister: Johanna, m. Henry de Ferrers, 4th Baron Ferrers, of Groby
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with 1st wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Margaret, m. 1. Sir John de Braose, of Wiston. He ob. 29 Nov., 1426. S. P. (Suss. Arch. Coll. V. p. 6). 2 Wickham. (Inq. 5 H. VI.)
2 CONT # Lucas Poynings, ob. v. p. S.P.
2 CONT # Isabel
2 CONT # Sir Hugh Poynings, ob. v. p. Oct., 1426 = 1) Elizabeth, d and h. of Martin Ferrers, of Bere Ferrers, 1st wife. 2) Eleanor, d. of John, Lord Welles. 2d wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/POYNINGS.htm#Thomas%20De%20POYNINGS%20(1º%20B.%20St.%20John%20of%20Basing) Accessed 27 July 2025
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas De POYNINGS (1º B. St. John of Basing)
2 CONT Born: 1350, Basing, Hampshire, England
2 CONT Died: 7 Mar 1429, Basing, Hampshire, England
2 CONT Father: Luke De POYNINGS
2 CONT Mother: Isabel St. JOHN
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1: Joan Le STRANGE 1372, Basing, Hampshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Luke De POYNINGS
2 CONT 2. Hugh De POYNINGS (Sir Knight)
2 CONT 3. Isabel De POYNINGS (b. 1385 - d. AFT 1428)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 2: Philippa De MORTIMER (C. Pembroke / C. Arundel) (d. 24 Sep 1401) (dau. of Edmund Mortimer, 3º E. March, and Phillippa Plantagenet) (w.1 of John Hastings, 3° E. Pembroke - w.2 of Richard Fitzalan, 6º E. Arundel) Nov 1399
2 CONC , Basing, Hampshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 3: Margaret LORING (dau. of Nigel Loring and Margaret Beaupel) (w. of Thomas Peyvre) ABT 1400
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 4: Maud De MAULEY (d. 3 Jun 1453) (m.2 Hugh Halsham) Apr 1415, Basing, Hampshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT THE TIMES 
2 CONT
2 CONT Monarchs 
2 CONT Edward I 1272-1307 
2 CONT Edward II 1307-1327 
2 CONT Edward III 1327-1377
2 CONT
2 CONT EVENTS 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Edward expels all Jews from England 1290 
2 CONT Marco Polo publishes his tales of China.1295 
2 CONT Edward I of England invades Scotland.1296 
2 CONT Robert the Bruce restores Scotland's de facto independence at the Battle of Bannockburn.1314 
2 CONT Famine stalks the land 1315-16 
2 CONT The Hundred Years War between England and France begins 1337 
2 CONT English win naval battle of Sluys against the French 1340 
2 CONT The battle of Crecy. English longbow men defeat the French army.1346 
2 CONT The Black Death ravages Europe for the first of many times. An estimated 20% - 40% of the population is thought to have perished within the first year.1347 
2 CONT The battle of Poitiers. English defeat the French 1356
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
