1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT Lucy Lestrange is the daughter of Roger Lestrange, 5th Lord Strange (of Knokyn) and Lady Aline Fitzalan.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William de Willoughby, 5th Baron Willoughby de Eresby, son of Robert de Willoughby, 4th Baron Willoughby de Eresby and Alice Skipwith, before 23 April 1383.1  Her married name became Willoughby.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lucy Lestrange and William de Willoughby, 5th Baron Willoughby de Eresby
2 CONT
2 CONT *Marjery Willoughby+2 d. b 22 Oct 1452
2 CONT *Sir Thomas Willoughby+
2 CONT *Elizabeth Willoughby+ b. c 1384, d. b 12 Nov 1428
2 CONT *Robert de Willoughby, 6th Baron Willoughby de Eresby+ b. c 1385, d. 25 Jul 1452
2 CONT
2 CONT ——
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy le Strange was born circa 1364 at of Knockin, Shropshire, England.3 She and Sir William Willoughby, 5th Lord Willoughby obtained a marriage license on 3 January 1383 at Middle, Shropshire, England; They had 2 sons (Sir Robert
2 CONC , 6th Lord Willoughby, Comte de Vendôme & Beaumont-sur-Oise; & Sir Thomas) and 3 daughters (Elizabeth, wife of Sir Henry, 5th Lord Beaumont; Margery, wife of Sir William, 4th Lord FitzHugh; & Margaret, wife of Sir Thomas Skipwith,
2 CONC  & of Sir William Oldhall).14,2,15,4,5,6,7,8,9,10,11 Lucy le Strange died between 28 April 1398 and 9 August 1404; Buried at Spilsby, Lincolnshire.3,7,11
2 CONT
