2 CONT *RICHARD FitzAlan, son of EDMUND FitzAlan Earl of Arundel & his wife Alice de Warenne ([1313]-Arundel 24 Jan 1376, bur Lewes Priory, Sussex).  His father's assets having been forfeited following his execution in 1326 (for supporti
2 CONC ng King Edward II against the Queen and Mortimer), Richard FitzAlan's inheritance was restored in 1330 and he succeeded as Earl of Arundel, known as "Copped Hat".  He succeeded in 1347 to the estates of the Warenne family, on the 
2 CONC death of his uncle John de Warenne 8th Earl of Surrey, although he only assumed the title Earl of Surrey after the death of the 8th Earl's widow Joan in 1361[102].  The History of the foundation of Walden abbey records the death “
2 CONC 1375 IX Kal Feb” of “Ricardus comes Arundell”[103].  
2 CONT *m firstly (1321, annulled 1344) ISABEL Le Despencer, daughter of Sir HUGH Le Despencer the younger, Lord Le Despencer & his wife Eleanor de Clare of Gloucester ([1312]-).  The Chronicle of Lanercost records that "comes Arundeliæ"
2 CONC  married "filiam domini Hugonis, junioris"[104].  
2 CONT *m secondly (Ditton Church, Stoke Poges, Bucks 5 Feb 1345, Papal dispensation 4 Mar 1345) as her second husband, ELEANOR of Lancaster, widow of JOHN de Beaumont, daughter of HENRY Earl of Lancaster & his wife Matilda Chaworth ([13
2 CONC 18]-Arundel Castle, Sussex 11 Jan 1372, bur Lewes Priory, Sussex).  While her first husband was still alive, and before Earl Richard's annulment of his first marriage, she lived with her future second husband.  
2 CONT *Earl Richard & his first wife had two children (bastardised in 1344 on the annulment of their parents´ marriage[105]):
2 CONT **1.         EDMUND de Arundel ([1327]-after 1377).  m (before Jul 1349) SIBYL de Montagu, daughter WILLIAM de Montagu Earl of Salisbury & his wife Katharine de Grandison .  Edmund & his wife had two children:  ......
2 CONT **'''2.         MARY [Isabel]''' (-29 Aug 1396).  '''m JOHN Lestrange 4th Lord Strange (of Blackmere), son of''' JOHN Lestrange Lord Strange (of Blackmere) & his wife Ankaret Boteler of Wem, Shropshire (Whitchurch [Easter] 1332-12
2 CONC  May 1361).  
2 CONT *From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm _____________
