1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==John de Bohun, 5th Earl of Hereford==
2 CONT '''John de Bohun, 5th Earl of Hereford (23 November 1306 – 20 January 1336) was born in St Clement's, Oxford''' to Humphrey de Bohun, 4th Earl of Hereford and Elizabeth of Rhuddlan, a daughter of Edward I of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his father's death at the Battle of Boroughbridge, the family lands were forfeited. '''It was not until after the fall of the Despensers that John was permitted to succeed to his inherited position as Earl of Hereford and Es
2 CONC sex and hereditary Constable of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He married firstly, in 1325, to Alice FitzAlan''' (1314-1385/86), daughter of Edmund FitzAlan, 9th Earl of Arundel, '''and secondly to Margaret Basset''' (died 1355).[citation needed] '''After the marriage, it was discovered th
2 CONC at the couple were related to the fourth degree of consanguinity and they were forced to live apart. An appeal to the Pope resulted on 19 February 1331 in a papal commission to the bishops of Lichfield and London to hold an enquir
2 CONC y into the case.[1] However, Roger Northburgh, the Bishop of Coventry and Lichfield, failed to act and the case was still pending when the Pope issued a further demand for an enquiry in 1334. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He did not play much of a public role, despite his high titles and offices, most likely because he had some sort of incapacity.[3] His younger brothers were often deputed to fulfill his duties as Constable. He died at Kirkby Th
2 CONC ore, Westmorland and was interred in Stratford Langthorne Abbey, London.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_de_Bohun,_5th_Earl_of_Hereford
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________
2 CONT *'''Sir John de Bohun, 9th Earl of Hereford & Essex, Constable of England1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8
2 CONT *'''M, #41481, b. 23 November 1306, d. 20 January 1336
2 CONT *Father	Sir Humphrey VIII de Bohun, 8th Earl Hereford & 9th Earl Essex, Constable of England1,9,10,11 b. c 1276, d. 16 Mar 1322
2 CONT *Mother	Elizabeth Plantagenet9,10,11 b. 7 Aug 1282, d. 5 May 1316
2 CONT *'''     Sir John de Bohun, 9th Earl of Hereford & Essex, Constable of England was born on 23 November 1306 at St. Clements, London, Middlesex, England.1,12,9,4,6 He and Alice FitzAlan obtained a marriage license on 22 February 13
2 CONC 25; Date of Dispensation, being related in the 4th degree of kindred; no issue.3,4,5,6,7 Sir John de Bohun, 9th Earl of Hereford & Essex, Constable of England married Margaret Basset''', daughter of Sir Ralph Basset, 2nd Lord Bass
2 CONC et of Drayton, Steward of the Duchy of Aquitaine, Constable of Dover Castle, Seneschal of Gascony and Joan Grey, '''on 19 February 1331; Date of Dispensation, being related in the 4th degree of kindred. No issue.4,6,8 Sir John de 
2 CONC Bohun, 9th Earl of Hereford & Essex, Constable of England died on 20 January 1336 at Kirkby-Thore, Westmoreland, England, at age 29; d.s.p; buried at Stratford Abbey, near London.13,3,4,6
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Alice FitzAlan d. 1326
2 CONT *'''Family 2     Margaret Basset b. c 1310, d. a 1 Dec 1347
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S11588] Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 32.
2 CONT *[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VI, p. 470-472.
2 CONT *[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 122.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 241.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 183.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 421.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 604.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. V, p. 7.
2 CONT *[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 121-122.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 239.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 419.
2 CONT *[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VI, p. 470.
2 CONT *[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VI, p. 471.
