2 CONT Margaret Marshall Plantagenet, Duchess of Norfolk1
2 CONT
2 CONT  b. circa 1321, d. 24 March 1399/0
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Marshall Plantagenet, Duchess of Norfolk was born circa 1321.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She was the daughter of Thomas of Brotherton, Earl of Norfolk and Alice Hayles.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 She married, firstly, John de Segrave, 4th Baron of Segrave after 3 March 1327.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Walter de Mauny, 1st Lord Mauny circa 30 May 1354.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She died on 24 March 1399/0.1 She was buried at Grey Friars Church, Greenwich, London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT From after 3 March 1327, her married name became Segrave. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She succeeded to the title of Countess of Norfolk in September 1338.
2 CONT
2 CONT  From circa 30 May 1354, her married name became de Mauny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She gained the title of Duchess of Norfolk on 29 September 1397.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Marshall Plantagenet, Duchess of Norfolk and John de Segrave, 4th Baron of Segrave
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Anne de Segrave1 d. c 1377
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Elizabeth de Segrave+3 b. 25 Oct 1338, d. b 1368
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Marshall Plantagenet, Duchess of Norfolk and Walter de Mauny, 1st Lord Mauny
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Anne de Mauny+1 b. 1354, d. 3 Apr 1384
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Thomas de Mauny1 b. b 1372, d. b 1372
