2 CONT Anne Hastings, Countess of Pembroke
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Hastings, Countess of Pembroke and 2nd Baroness Manny (24 July 1355 – 3 April 1384) was the daughter of Walter Manny, 1st Baron Manny and Margaret, Duchess of Norfolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT In July 1368, she married John Hastings, 2nd Earl of Pembroke. They had one son, John Hastings, 3rd Earl of Pembroke. Her husband and father both died in 1375, and she became suo jure Baroness Manny (her one brother having died in
2 CONC  his youth).
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly before her death in 1384, she was invested as a Lady of the Garter
2 CONT
2 CONT =================
2 CONT
2 CONT MARGARET ([1320/22]-24 Mar 1399, bur Charterhouse, Smithfield, London or Greyfriars Church, Newgate, London).  She succeeded her father in 1338[793] as Countess of Norfolk, suo iure.  She was created Duchess of Norfolk for life 29
2 CONC  Sep 1397.  m firstly (after 3 Mar 1327, probably [1337/38]) JOHN de Segrave Lord Segrave, son of STEPHEN de Segrave Lord Segrave & his wife Alice FitzAlan of Arundel ([1315]-1 Apr 1353).  He succeeded his father in 1325 as Lord S
2 CONC egrave.  m secondly (shortly before 30 May 1354) WALTER de Mauny, son of JEAN "le Borgne" de Mauny [Magny] Seigneur de Magny[-en-Hainaut] & his wife Jeanne de Jenlain ([1310]-London 8 or 15 Jan 1372, bur Charterhouse, Smithfield, 
2 CONC London).  He came to England as a page of Philippa de Hainaut, on her marriage to King Edward III.  He served the King in campaigns in Flanders, Brittany, Scotland, Gascony, and at the capture of Calais in Aug 1347.  Summoned to P
2 CONC arliament from 1347 as Lord Mauny.  Appointed Admiral of the Fleet from the Thames to Berwick Mar 1348.  He was one of the guarantors of the Treaty of Brétigny 8 May 1360, and an arbitrator on the claims to the duchy of Brittany. 
2 CONC  Ctss Margaret & her first husband had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT -        see Part D, below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ctss Margaret & her second husband had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ANNE de Mauny (24 Jul 1355-3 Apr 1384).  She succeeded her father in 1372 as Baroness Mauny.  m ([Jul or after] 1368) as his second wife, JOHN Hastings Earl of Pembroke, son of LAURENCE de Hastings Earl of Pembroke & hi
2 CONC s wife Anne de Mortimer (Sutton Valence 29 Aug 1347-1375). 
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         THOMAS de Mauny (-died aged 5). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Hastings, Countess of Pembroke
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Hastings, Countess of Pembroke and 2nd Baroness Manny (24 July 1355 – 3 April 1384) was the daughter of Walter Manny, 1st Baron Manny and Margaret, Duchess of Norfolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT In July 1368, she married John Hastings, 2nd Earl of Pembroke. They had one son, John Hastings, 3rd Earl of Pembroke. Her husband and father both died in 1375, and she became suo jure Baroness Manny (her one brother having died in
2 CONC  his youth).
2 CONT
2 CONT Shortly before her death in 1384, she was invested as a Lady of the Garter.
2 CONT --------------------
