2 CONT iii)        ENRICHETTO (-before 20 Mar 1385).  Signor di Calizzano.  He is named as deceased in the 20 Mar 1385 charter quoted below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' --- Adorno, from Genoa.  Enrichetto & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(a)       GIORGINO (-17 Nov 1428).  A charter dated 20 Mar 1385 records a dispute between the commune of Genoa and “dominos Lazarinum et Karolum marchiones de Carreto natos quondam domini Georgiii...et vice Georgini nepotis ipsor
2 CONC um nati quondam domini Enriceti...” concerning their fiefs, and a settlement agreed “...cum filiis et heredibus quondam Enriceti marchionis de Carreto fratris ipsorum dominorum Lazarini et Carolli...” by charter dated 13 Jan 1385[
2 CONC 1253].  “Domini Georgini filii quondam domini Enriceti marchionis de Carreto de Finario” swore allegiance to Charles VI King of France by charter dated 27 Jan 1402[1254].  Signor di Calizzano, Santa Giulia e Sassello.  '''m''' ISA
2 CONC BELLA, daughter of [--- Conte Valperga di Caluso].  Giorgino & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT **(1)       BATTISTINO (-young after 1428). 
2 CONT
2 CONT **(2)       COSIMO (-young after 1428). 
2 CONT
2 CONT **(3)       GIOVANNI (-young after 1428). 
2 CONT
2 CONT **(4)       ENRICHETTO (-young after 1428). 
2 CONT
2 CONT **(5)       DEIFEBO (-young after 1428). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *(b)       PIETRO (-1425).  Abbot of San Martino della Gallinara, near Albenga.   
2 CONT
2 CONT *(c)       GALEOTTO (-1396). 
