2 CONT
2 CONT a)       ''' HERZLAUDE von Rappoltstein''' (-before 18 Jun 1400).  The late 15th century Chronicle of Peter von Andlau names “Hertzelande” as the only child of Ulrich and his first wife “Hertzelande grefin von Fürstenberg”, record
2 CONC ing that she married “ein grofen von Sarwer”[1141].  “Graf Rudolf von Habspurg herre ze Loffenberg” promised payments to “grafe Hansen unsern sun” when he married “Ulrichen herren zu Rappoltstein...Herczeladen...tohter” by charter
2 CONC  dated 9 Dec 1372[1142].  This betrothal did not proceed as shown by the 4 Jul 1378 charter under which [her uncle] Bruno Herr von Rappoltstein confirmed that he had not permitted the marriage to proceed, which resulted in legal p
2 CONC roceedings in Nürnberg as shown by a charter dated 25 Aug 1379[1143].  “Ulrich herre zu Rapoltzstein und ze Hohennag” donated property to Kloster Päris for masses on his anniversary, with the consent of “Brune herre zu der Hohen R
2 CONC apoltzstein, Hug von Rapoltzstein tumherre und portener der styft zu Straßburg gebrudere und Hertzelaude des vorgenanten hern Ulriches...tochter”, by charter dated 11 Jul 1377[1144].  Frau von Rappoltstein und Hohenack: “Brune her
2 CONC re zu der Hohen Rapoltzstein und...Hertzelaude frowe zu Rapoltzstein und ze Hohennag, hern Ulriches seligen tochter...” issued a charter dated 5 Sep 1377 in favour of “Cuntz von Halstat”[1145].  “Heinrich graff zu Sarwerde und...H
2 CONC erczelauden frowe zu Rapolczstein und zu Hohennag”, with the agreement of “mins vatters hern Johanses grafen zu Sarwerde”, granted half his county to his wife as dower, and “Brune herre zu der Hohen Rapolczstein” confirmed his nie
2 CONC ce Herzlaude’s agreement to sell her share in Rappoltstein to him, by charter dated 4 Jul 1378, amended by a further charter dated 15 Aug 1378[1146].  The couple’s marriage was declared valid, despite Herzlaude’s previous betrotha
2 CONC l, by a Papal representative by charter dated 7 Aug 1393[1147].  “Hertzelauden grefin von Sarwerden frowe zu Ropsteyn und zu Hohenag” confirmed donations to Kloster Alspach made by “myns...herren seligen her Heinrichs wilent greff
2 CONC en zu Sarwerde...”, by charter dated 4 Jun 1398[1148].  Her second marriage is indicated by the charter dated 6 Sep 1398 under which “Johanns von Lupffen landtgrave zue Stuelingen” granted “die landtgraffschafft zu Stuelingen” to 
2 CONC “unser...hausfrawen fraw Hertzelauden frawen zu Rapolstein undt zue Hohennagkh” as dower by charter dated 4 Jun 1398[1149].  Leopold IV Duke of Austria settled a dispute between “unserm...ohain Hansen von Lupfen lantgrafen zu Stul
2 CONC ingen” and “Smahsman und Ulrichen gebrudere herren zu Rappolczstein” concerning the inheritance of “Herzelauden von Rappolczstein” by charter dated 18 Jun 1400[1150].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' (9 Dec 1372, terminated) to JOHANN [IV] von Habsburg, son of RUDOLF [IV von Habsburg Graf von Laufenburg & his wife Elisabeth von Mentone (-18 May 1408).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (before 4 Jul 1378) HEINRICH Graf von Saarwerden, son of JOHANN Graf von Saarwerden & his wife --- (-18 Jul 1397).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' thirdly (contract 6 Sep 1398) JOHANN von Lupfen Landgraf von Stühlingen, son of ---.    
