2 CONT     * Jeanne of Savoy (unknown - 1460; married Giangiacomo Paleologo, marquis of Montferrat.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Amadeus' death in 1391, a regency dispute over their son Amadeus VIII ensued after her husband passed over Bonne in favor of his mother Bonne of Bourbon. This conflict would only be resolved by an agreement, signed on 8 May 
2 CONC 1393.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Second marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Her second marriage was to Bernard VII of Armagnac. Their marriage contract is dated on 2 December 1393.[2] They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * John IV of Armagnac (1396 - 1450); married (1) Blanche of Brittany (2) Isabella d' Évreux
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Marie (1397), died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bonne d'Armagnac (1399 - 1415); married Charles, Duke of Orléans.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Bernard d'Armagnac, Count of Pardiac (1400 - 1462); married Eleanor of Bourbon-La Marche.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne of Armagnac (1402 - before 1473); married Charles II of Albret.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Jeanne (1403), died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Béatrix (1406), died young.
2 CONT
