1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amadeus_VIII,_Duke_of_Savoy ''[45 languages]''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Amadeus VIII''' (4 September 1383 – 7 January 1451), nicknamed '''the Peaceful''', was Count of Savoy from 1391 to 1416 and Duke of Savoy from 1416 to 1440. He was the first to hold the ducal title, granted by Emperor [https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/people/Re-Sigismondo-di-Lussemburgo/6000000001500854063 Sigismund]. Known for his diplomatic temperament and administrative reforms, he strengthened the state's institutions and fostered internal peace.
2 CONT He also claimed the papacy from 1439 to 1449 as '''Antipope Felix V''',[a] in opposition to Popes [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-Eugene-IV/6000000010293952225 Eugene IV] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Pope-Nicholas-V/60000000
2 CONC 22945004064 Nicholas V], becoming the last historical antipope recognised by a significant portion of the Catholic clergy.
2 CONT {{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vigiles_du_roi_Charles_VII_17_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Vigiles_du_roi_Charles_VII_17_%28cropped%29.jpg|right|140px}}
2 CONT
