1 OCCU Herzogin von Savoyen ( 1417 - 1422)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Mary of Burgundy (French: Marie de Bourgogne; 1386–1428) was a Duchess consort of Savoy by her marriage to Duke Amadeus VIII of Savoy, who was later known as Antipope Felix V.
2 CONT Life
2 CONT '''Mary was born in 1386, most likely in September, in Dijon, France.[1] She was the eighth of the nine children''' of Philip the Bold, Duke of Burgundy, and his wife Margaret III, Countess of Flanders.[2]
2 CONT '''From her birth, Mary's father intended her to marry Amadeus VIII of Savoy''', son of Amadeus VII, Count of Savoy and Bonne of Berry. '''Their marriage was contracted in the year of her birth, on 11 November 1386 in Sluis, Zeela
2 CONC nd; they married by proxy 30 October 1393 in Chalon-sur-Saône and in person at Arras in May 1401, when Mary was around 15 years old.[3] However, she did not arrive in Savoy until she was 17, in September 1403.'''[4]
2 CONT '''In 1416, Sigismund, then King of the Romans elevated Amadeus from Count to Duke of Savoy. Mary duly became Duchess. From then onwards Dukes ruled over Savoy.'''
2 CONT '''The couple were married for thirty-six years before Mary died in the beginning of October 1428[a] at Chateau of Thonon-les-Bains.[2] She is buried in the Abbey of Hautecombe.'''
2 CONT '''Issue'''
2 CONT '''Mary and Amadeus had nine children, only four of whom lived to mature adulthood.'''
2 CONT 1. Margaret of Savoy (13 May 1405 – 1418).
2 CONT 2. Anthony of Savoy (September 1407 – bef. 12 December 1407).
2 CONT 3. Anthony of Savoy (1408 – aft. 10 October 1408).
2 CONT 4. Marie of Savoy (end January 1411 – 22 February 1469), married Filippo Maria Visconti, duke of Milan.
2 CONT 5. Amadeus of Savoy (26 Mar 1412 – 17 August 1431), Prince of Piemonte, Amadeus' heir apparent until his premature death.
2 CONT 6. Louis of Savoy (24 February 1413 – 29 January 1465), Duke of Savoy, he married Anne of Cyprus in 1432 and had issue.[5]
2 CONT 7. Bonne of Savoy (September 1415 – 25 September 1430), betrothed at the age of 11 to Francis I, Duke of Brittany, she died at 15 before the marriage could take place.[6]
2 CONT 8. Margaret of Savoy (7 August 1420 – 30 September 1479), married firstly Louis III of Anjou, titular king of Naples, and had no issue; secondly Louis IV, Count Palatine of the Rhine and had issue; and thirdly Ulrich V, Count of W
2 CONC ürttemberg and had issue.
2 CONT 9. Philip of Savoy (1422 – 3 March 1444), Count of Genève.
2 CONT Ancestry
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_of_Burgundy,_Duchess_of_Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________________
2 CONT ==Mary of Burgundy1
