1 OCCU Count of Nevers and Rethel, seigneur de Saint-Valery, Comte de Nevers, chambrier de France
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_II,_Count_of_Nevers
2 CONT
2 CONT Phillip II, Count of Nevers (October 1389, Villaines-en-Duesmois – 25 October 1415, Agincourt) was the youngest son of Philip the Bold and Margaret III of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his brothers, John the Fearless and Anthony, Duke of Brabant, as Count of Nevers and Rethel respectively after each of them acceded to their duchies.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in Soissons on 9 April 1409 Isabelle de Coucy (d. 1411), daughter of Enguerrand VII de Coucy. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT  1.Philip (1410 – 1411/aft. 1415)
2 CONT
2 CONT  2.Margaret (1411–1411/12)
2 CONT
2 CONT He married again, in Beaumont-en-Artois on 20 June 1413, Bonne of Artois, daughter of Philip of Artois, Count of Eu. They had two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT  1.Charles I, Count of Nevers (1414–1464)
2 CONT
2 CONT  2.John II, Count of Nevers (bef. 1415 – 1491)
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had four illegitimate children by various mistresses.
2 CONT
2 CONT In spite of his elder brother John's ambivalent position and ultimate refusal to come to the aid of the royal army in the face of the English invasion of Henry V in 1415, Philip was with the French army at the Battle of Agincourt,
2 CONC  and both he and his brother Anthony were killed in the battle. He was succeeded by his son Charles.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Stamboom nr. :  837.012.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generatie :  20.
