2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_III,_Duke_of_Bar
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward III of Bar (late June 1377 - 25 October 1415, Agincourt) was made marquis of Pont-à-Mousson by his father Robert I of Bar in 1399 (his mother was Mary of France, daughter of John II of France) and held it until his death. H
2 CONC e then became heir to the duchy of Bar following the death of his elder brothers Henry and Philippe at or soon after the battle of Nicopolis in 1396.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1405, Charles VI of France charged him with defending the Boulonnais, then threatened by the English. At the end of 1406 he participated in the Guyenne campaign under the orders of Louis of Orleans, but dysentry decimated the F
2 CONC rench forces. After Louis's assassination in 1407, Edward joined John the Fearless and rallied the Burgundians. Succeeding his father on 12 April 1411, Edward was killed at the battle of Agincourt and succeeded by his brother (he 
2 CONC never married, though he left several illegitimate children).
