2 CONT Marie of Cleves (19 September 1426 - 23 August 1487) was born in Prussia to Adolph I of Cleves and Marie of Burgundy.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 November 1440 at the age of fourteen she married Charles of Valois, Duke of Orléans[1] they had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie d' Orléans (19 December 1457 – 1493). She married Jean of Foix, Count of Étampes in 1476.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis XII of France (1462–1515)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne d' Orléans (1464–1491), Abbess of Fontevrault and Poitiers.
