2 CONT RICHARD (EARL OF ARUNDEL) BUT DID NOT MARRY HER; CHIEF GUARDIAN OF THE TRUCE
2 CONT WITH SCOTLAND; MARSHAL OF ENGLAND 1373-76 (WHEN JOHN OF GAUNT WAS OUT OF
2 CONT POWER); APPOINTED TO THE KING'S COUNCIL 1376; APPOINTED TO THE COUNCIL OF
2 CONT REGENCY ON THE ACCESSION OF RICHARD II 6/1377, AND CARRIED THE SPURS AT THE
2 CONT CORONATION; KNOWN AS "THE GOOD"
1 NOTE 3rd Earl of March. [GADD.GED]
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. Plantagenet Ancestry, Eng. 116, p. 2, 72-73, 96
2 CONT     2. The Complete Peerage, G.E.C., Eng. V, v. 8, p. 445-48, v. 9, p. 285
2 CONT     3. The Royal Dau of Eng., Eng. 120, v. 1, p. 241, 275, 278, 233
2 CONT     4. Dict. of Nat'l Biog., Eng. Pub. A, v. 39, p. 119-20
2 CONT     5. Montgomery Collections, Montg. Pub. A, v. 23, p. 347, v. 25, p. 9-10
2 CONT     6. Antiq. of Shropshire, Shrops 5, v. 4, p. 193
2 CONT     7. Shropshire Arch. Soc. Pub. A 1s, v. 2, p. 45
2 CONT     8. Archaeological Cambrensis, Wales Pub. A4s, v. 5, p. 103
2 CONT     9. Worcester Inquisitions Post Mortem, Worc. 10, pt 2
2 CONT !RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT     1. There appears to be two dates of marriage given for the above couple, oneas shown above and the other in 1368. The above husband may have had another son by the name of John, but if so, he must have been illegitimately born
2 CONC ; thus his sealing to the above couple on 11 Feb 1958 would be erroneous.
