1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Philippa de Mortimer: http://thepeerage.com/p10691.htm#i106902
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa de Mortimer [1]
2 CONT *F, #106902, 
2 CONT *b. 21 November 1375, 
2 CONT *d. 24 September 1401
2 CONT *Last Edited=22 May 2004
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.16%
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippa de Mortimer was born on 21 November 1375 at Ludlow Castle, Ludlow, Shropshire, England.[1] She was the daughter of Edmund de Mortimer, 3rd Earl of March and Philippa Plantagenet, Countess of Ulster.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, John de Hastings, 3rd Earl of Pembroke, son of John de Hastings, 2nd Earl of Pembroke and Anne de Mauny, circa 1385.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Richard FitzAlan, 11th Earl of Arundel, son of Richard FitzAlan, 10th Earl of Arundel and Lady Eleanor Plantagenet, on 15 August 1390, without Royal license (for which he was fined 500 marks).[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT \She married, thirdly, Thomas Poynings, 5th Lord St. John of Basing from April 1398 to 24 November 1399.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 24 September 1401 at age 25 at Halnaker, Sussex, England.[3],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried at Boxgrove Priory, Lewes, Sussex, England.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT From circa 1385, her married name became Hastings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 15 August 1390, her married name became Fitzalan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 24 November 1399, her married name became Poynings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Philippa de Mortimer and Richard FitzAlan, 11th Earl of Arundel
2 CONT *1. John FitzAlan [3] b. c 1394, d. a 1397
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 97. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 245. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *3. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family, page 98.
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================
