2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hainaut-43
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/fedegrifo?n=de+hainaut+comte+de+hainaut+et+hollande+comte+de+hainaut+et+hollande+comte+de+hainaut+et+hollande+comte+de+hainaut+et+hollande+comte+de+hainaut+et+hollande&oc=&p=guillaume
2 CONT
2 CONT ===William Avesnes who was known as 
2 CONT William I Avesnes the Count of Hainaut
2 CONT William II Avesnes the Count of Zeeland 
2 CONT William III Avesnes Count of Holland===
2 CONT
2 CONT William, born c. 1286, was the son of John II Count of Hainaut and his wife Philippa the daughter of Henry V Count of Luxembourg. William was the brother of John of Beaumont and Alice of Hainault.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was originally not expected to become count. After the deaths of his elder brothers, John (killed at Kortrijk in 1302) and Henry (d. 1303), he became heir apparent to his father's counties.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prior to becoming count, he was defeated by Guy of Namur at the battle on the island of Duiveland in 1304. Guy and John II Duke of Brabant then conquered most of Zeeland and Holland, but these territories were recovered again when
2 CONC  William became the new count in the same year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William continued the war with Flanders until the Peace of Paris in 1323, during which the Count of Flanders renounced all claims on Zeeland. 
2 CONT William, in turn, gained all of Zeeland but agreed to renounce all claims on Imperial Flanders. 
2 CONT William had occupied most of the Bishopric of Utrecht and tried to conquer Friesland but was repelled by Hessel Martena. 
2 CONT At the death of his uncle, Guy d'Avesnes Bishop of Utrecht, William took his fief of Amsterdam and annexed it to Holland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many of his daughters married with important rulers of Europe; King Edward III of England and Holy Roman Emperor Louis IV were married to his daughters, while he was married to the sister of the King Philip VI of France. With thes
2 CONC e important alliances William gained considerable influence and respect, which he used to advance the interests of his counties.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 19 May 1305 William married Joan of Valois, sister of the future king Philip VI of France, and had the following children:
2 CONT William II Count of Hainaut (1307–1345)
2 CONT John (died 1316)
2 CONT Margaret II Countess of Hainault Holy Roman Empress (1311–1356), married Louis IV Holy Roman Emperor
2 CONT Philippa of Hainault Queen-Consort of England (c.1313–1369), married King Edward III of England
2 CONT Agnes (d. 1327)
2 CONT Joanna of Hainaut Duchess-Consort of Julich (1315–1374), married William V Duke of Jülich
2 CONT Isabelle of Hainaut (1323–1361), married Robert of Namur
2 CONT Louis (1325–1328)[1]
2 CONT Jan Aelman (1320–1389) Illegitimate son and Knight
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Killed by the Frisians along with Count Willem of Hainaut, Holland and Zeeland, and Lord of Friesland: Lord Jan van Montfoort, Lord Roelof van Montfoort, Lord Willem van Montfoort, with many of their kin, friends and subordinates.
2 CONC  Pray for all their souls. This was portrayed in the year 1608; portrayed for the third time in 1770)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bron: http://www.kareldegrote.nl/Reeksen/ToonReeks.php?Reeks=3 Bij de reeks persoon nummer 19 staat duidelijk dat Willem III van Holland bij de concubine NN De Moor een zoon genaamd Jan Aelman heeft. Dat is ook te vinden op een tw
2 CONC eede bron: Wikipedia Willem III van Holland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume V (III), Comte de Hainaut, Hollande et Zélande was born in 1280.2 He married Jeanne de Valois, daughter of Charles I de France, Comte de Valois and Marguerite d'Anjou, in 1305.2 He died on 7 June 1337. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume V (III), Comte de Hainaut, Hollande et Zélande also went by the nick-name of Guillaume 'le Bon' (or in English, 'the Good').3 He was the son of Jean II, Comte de Hainaut et Hollande and Philippa de Luxembourg. He gained 
2 CONC the title of Comte de Zélande in 1304. He gained the title of Comte de Hainaut in 1304.1 He succeeded to the title of Comte de Hollande in 1304.3 <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Guillaume V (III), Comte de Hainaut, Hollande et Zélande and Jeanne de Valois'''
2 CONT
2 CONT #Jeanne de Hainaut+1 d. 1374
2 CONT #Marguerite, Comtesse de Hainaut et Hollande+4 b. 1311, d. c 1356
2 CONT #Philippe de Hainaut+3 b. 24 Jun 1311, d. 15 Aug 1369
2 CONT # Guillaume VI (IV), Comte de Hainaut et Hollande b. c 1317, d. c 1345
2 CONT #Isabella de Hainaut b. c 1323, d. 1361
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 88. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *[S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 65. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT *[S45] Marcellus Donald R. von Redlich, Pedigrees of Some of the Emperor Charlemagne's Descendants, volume I (1941; reprint, Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.A.: Genealogical Publishing Company, 2002), page 64. Hereinafter cited as Pedigr
2 CONC ees of Emperor Charlemagne, I.
2 CONT *[S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 91. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
