1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Margaret II, Countess of Hainault==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret II of Avesnes (1311 – June 23, 1356) was Countess of Hainaut and Countess of Holland (as Margaret I) from 1345 to 1356. Margaret was the daughter''' of William I, Count of Hainaut and his wife, Jeanne of Valois. '''On 
2 CONC 26 February 1324 in Cologne she married Emperor Louis IV the Bavarian.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She succeeded in 1345 her brother''' William IV following his death in battle: '''The emperor was conferring Hainaut, Holland, Zeeland and Friesland upon his wife, and shortly later also upon their son''' William V. '''The here
2 CONC ditary titles of Margaret's sisters''', including Philippa of Hainaut who was Queen consort of Edward III of England, were ignored. Due to the dangerous hostility of the House of Luxemburg Louis had increased his power base ruthle
2 CONC ssly. '''Margaret then returned to Holland in 1346 to secure her position of power but did not manage to prevent the coronation of the Luxemburg Charles IV as anti-king in Aix-la-Chapelle by force.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''When Louis IV died''' on October 11, 1347, he was succeeded by his six sons. In 1349 the brothers decided to partition their possessions; Louis V, Duke of Bavaria kept Brandenburg and Tyrol, he and his younger brothers Louis VI
2 CONC  the Roman and Otto V the Bavarian received Upper Bavaria. Stephen II, William and Albert received Lower Bavaria, Holland and Hainaut. Louis V and Stephen were no sons of '''Margaret and her youngest sons''' Albert and Otto were s
2 CONC till minors. Louis VI released Holland and Hainaut for his brothers William and Albert in 1349 since he expected the Polish crown by his marriage with Cunigunde of Poland. In 1353 also Stephen released Holland and Hainault to his 
2 CONC brother William.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Also Margaret had resigned her sovereignty in favour of her son''' William. '''In 1350, the nobles of Holland asked Margaret to return to Holland again. She then battled for the power in Holland and Hainaut for some years with 
2 CONC her son''' William who had refussed to pay her alimony. The Cod league was formed in May 23, 1350 by a number of supporters of William. On September 5 of the same year, the Hook league was formed. Soon afterward, these factions cl
2 CONC ashed, and a civil war began.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward III of England, '''Margaret's brother-in-law through her sister''' Philippa of Hainault, '''came to her aid, winning a naval engagement off Veere in 1351; a few weeks later the Hooks and their English allies were defeated''
2 CONC ' by William and the Cods at Vlaardingen, '''an overthrow which ruined Margaret's cause'''. Edward III shortly afterwards changed sides, and '''the empress saw herself compelled (1354) to come to an understanding with her son''', 
2 CONC he being recognized as count of Holland and Zeeland, '''she of Hainaut. Margaret died two years later''', leaving William, in possession of the entire Holland-Hainaut inheritance (July 1356). William was married to Matilda ("Maud"
2 CONC  in the English style) of Lancaster, sister to Blanche of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1324 she married Louis IV, Holy Roman Emperor. Their children were:
2 CONT * 1. Margarete (1325–1374), married: 1. in 1351 in Buda Stephen, Duke of Slavonia (d. 1354), son of the King Charles I of Hungary, and had issue; 2. 1357/58 Gerlach von Hohenlohe. 
2 CONT * 2. Anna (c. 1326 – June 3, 1361, Fontenelles) married John I of Lower Bavaria (d. 1340) 
2 CONT * 3. Louis VI the Roman (1328–1365), duke of Upper Bavaria, elector of Brandenburg. No issue.
2 CONT * 4. Elisabeth (1329 – August 2, 1402, Stuttgart), married with: 1. Cangrande II della Scala, Lord of Verona (d. 1359) in Verona on November 22, 1350. No issue; 2. Count Ulrich of Württemberg (d. 1388) in 1362. No issue.
2 CONT * 5. William V of Holland (1330–1389), as William I duke of Lower Bavaria, as Wiliam V count of Hainaut and Holland. He married Maud of Lancaster but their only daughter died young 
2 CONT * 6. Agnes (Munich, 1335 – November 11, 1352, Munich) She became a nun, due to ill health and died young
2 CONT * 7. Albert I of Holland (1336–1404), duke of Lower Bavaria, count of Hainaut and Holland 
2 CONT * 8. Otto V the Bavarian (1340–1379), duke of Upper Bavaria, elector of Brandenburg 
2 CONT * 9. Beatrix of Bavaria (1344 – December 25, 1359), married bef. October 25, 1356 Eric XII of Sweden 
2 CONT * 10. Louis (October 1347 – 1348) 
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_II,_Countess_of_Hainault
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Margarethe I. (Holland)
2 CONT
2 CONT aus Wikipedia, der freien Enzyklopädie
