2 TITL Thomas Holland | European Royal History 
1 NOTE
2 CONT if you have questions e-mail me at kathleen@wwdb.org
1 NOTE Her marriage to William de Montacute was bigamous. It was anulled by the Pope
2 CONT and she was ordered to return to Thomas Holland.
2 CONT Baroness Wake. The Complete Peerage vol.VII,pp.150-154
1 NOTE !RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT     Joan md (2) before 15 Oct 1348, William de Montacute, Earl of Salisbury, from whom she was divorced by Papal Bull 13 Nov 1349 and ordered to return to her lawful husband, sir Thomas de Holand, later created Earl of Kent; md (3
2 CONC ) 10 Oct 1361, Edward "The Black Prince", Prince of England.
1 NOTE _P_CCINFO 1-20792
1 NOTE !RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT     Joan md (2) before 15 Oct 1348, William de Montacute, Earl of Salisbury, from whom she was divorced by Papal Bull 13 Nov 1349 and ordered to return to her lawful husband, sir Thomas de Holand, later created Earl of Kent; md (3
2 CONC ) 10 Oct 1361, Edward "The Black Prince", Prince of England.
1 NOTE Married on or before 1339
1 NOTE There was a bit of a problem she was far too related to Edward, but the marriage was sanctioned anyway.
2 CONT Another problem lay within the fact that she had been married previously and was still married when she bethrothed the King Edward the Black Prince. The marriage was anulled in any case.
1 NOTE "THE FAIR MAID OF KENT""OF WOODSTOCK"; 1ST PRINCESS OF WALES
1 NOTE Joan, "The Fair Maid of Kent" (1328-85), was the daughter of Edmund of Woodstock, son of Edward I. She appears to have formed a liaison with the Earl of Salisbury, and then to have married Sir Thomas Holland. She became Countess o
2 CONC f Kent (1352), and on Holland�s death, married the Black Prince (1361), and became the mother of Richard II. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
1 NOTE Joan (of KENT) PLANTAGENET Countess [Parents] was born 29 Sep 1328. She died 8 Aug 1385 in Wallingford Castle, Berkshire, England and was buried in Greyfriars Church, Stamford, Lincoln. Joan married Thomas HOLLAND Earl of Kent on 
2 CONC 1348.
1 NOTE !RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT     Joan md (2) before 15 Oct 1348, William de Montacute, Earl of Salisbury, from whom she was divorced by Papal Bull 13 Nov 1349 and ordered to return to her lawful husband, sir Thomas de Holand, later created Earl of Kent; md (3
2 CONC ) 10 Oct 1361, Edward "The Black Prince", Prince of England.
