2 CONT '''Mother'''	Isabel Plantagenet2,3,4 b. 16 Jun 1332, d. 5 Oct 1382
2 CONT '''     Philippe de Coucy was born circa 1368 at Eltham, Kent, England.2 She married Sir Robert de Vere, 9th Earl of Oxford, Duke of Ireland, Marquess of Dublin, Chamberlain of England, Sheriff of Rutland, Chief Justice of Chester
2 CONC  & North Wales''', son of Sir Thomas de Vere, 8th Earl of Oxford, Chamberlain of England and Maud de Ufford, '''circa 5 October 1376; They had no issue.5,2,3,4 Philippe de Coucy and Sir Robert de Vere, 9th Earl of Oxford, Duke of 
2 CONC Ireland, Marquess of Dublin, Chamberlain of England, Sheriff of Rutland, Chief Justice of Chester & North Wales were divorced in 1387; However, the Pope declared the divorce null and void in 1389.1,2,4 Philippe de Coucy died on 24
2 CONC  September 1411.'''6,2,4
2 CONT '''Family'''
