1 NOTE At the age of 4, Phillipa de Coucy, daughter of Enguerrand VII and Isabelle of England, and granddaughter of King Edward III, was betrothed to Robert de Vere, 9th Earl of Oxford, then aged 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the separation of her parents, Enguerrand de Coucy and Isabella of England, Phillipa de Coucy then inherited the de Coucy lands in England after her mother, Isabella died in 1379.  This included the Duchess of Bedford ti
2 CONC tle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Phillipa de Coucy, now the widowed Countess of Oxford, accompanied her English uncles to  a parlay with the King of France in 1392.  She had not been to her homeland since she and her mother had moved to England in 1371.
