2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_II,_Count_of_Flanders     (Very interesting read!!)
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis II of Flanders (Dutch: Lodewijk van Male; French: Louis II de Flandre) (25 October 1330, Male – 30 January 1384, Lille), also known as Louis of Male, a member of the House of Dampierre, was Count of Flanders, Nevers and Reth
2 CONC el from 1346 as well as Count of Artois and Burgundy from 1382 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT The main line of the House of Dampierre, originally only counts of Flanders, had through a clever marriage policy managed to inherit the counties of Nevers (1280) and Rethel (1328). Through Louis' mother, a daughter of King Philip
2 CONC  V of France, the counties of Artois and Burgundy (the "Franche Comté") were added to this (1382).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00013574&tree=LEO
2 CONT
