2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Katherine of Lancaster (also known as Katherine Plantagenet and as Queen Catalina of Castile and Leon) (1372-1418) – was the daughter of John of Gaunt, 1st Duke of Lancaster, and his second wife, Constance of Castile who was the d
2 CONC aughter and rightful heir of Pedro I of Castille, who died at the hands of his half brother Enrique II. She was born in Hertford Castle, her father's chief country home.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Enrique III of Castile in 1393 at Burgos. As her mother was daughter of Pedro of Castile, and had been a claimant to the Castilian throne herself, the marriage helped to restore a semblance of legitimacy to the Trastam
2 CONC ara line.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria of Castile (1401-1458), who married Alfonso V "the Magnanimous", King of Aragon and Naples, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina of Castile (1403-1439), who wed Enrique of Aragón, Duque de Villena, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan II (1405-1454), who succeeded his father as King of Castile. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Enrique III died in 1406 and according to his will, his widow Catherine and his brother Ferdinand I of Aragon served as co-regents during the minority of Juan II. He ordered Mudejars (peasants, carpenters, seaman, and shipbuilders
2 CONC ) to wear a symbol; a blue moon on their clothing. They were not allowed to leave their home. They were not allowed to work or trade, as well as the Jewish, with Christians. They were under the mercy of the Christians. This was an
2 CONC  attempt by Juan II to suppress religious minority and with the attempts of Queen Catalina, this attempt only lasted until her death and tensions between the regents led to a division of rule and in 1418 tolerance returned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Queen Catherine died at Valladolid of a stroke, possibly precipitated by her great obesity, leaving her thirteen year-old son at the mercy of self-interested courtiers. She is the namesake of her great granddaughter Katherine of A
2 CONC ragon, first of the six wives of Henry VIII of England.
2 CONT
