2 CONT *'''Henry de Beaufort1
2 CONT *'''M, #101972, b. circa 1375, d. 11 April 1447
2 CONT *Last Edited=29 Dec 2009
2 CONT *'''     Henry de Beaufort was born circa 1375 at Château de Beaufort, Montmorency-Beaufort, Champagne, France.1,2,3 He was the son of John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster and Katherine Roët. He died on 11 April 1447 at Wolvesey Palac
2 CONC e, Winchester, Hampshire, England.1 He was buried at Winchester Cathedral, Winchester, Hampshire, England.1
2 CONT *'''     He held the office of Dean of Wells Cathedral in 1397.1 In February 1397 Parliament legitimised his birth, even though he was born before his parent's marriage. He was provided to the See of Lincoln on 27 February 1398.1 
2 CONC He held the office of Bishop of Lincoln on 14 July 1398.1 He held the office of Bishop of Winchester on 19 November 1404.1 He held the office of Cardinal-Priest of St. Eusebius on 24 May 1426.1 He has an extensive biographical ent
2 CONC ry in the Dictionary of National Biography.4
2 CONT *'''Child of Henry de Beaufort and Alice FitzAlan
2 CONT **Joan Beaufort+5 b. c 1402, d. c 1453
2 CONT *Citations
