2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Stirnet's "CZmisc16" page (link below):
2 CONT
2 CONT >Wright reports that <this> William had 4 daughters (including Alice, wife of Sir John Tyrell of Heron) who were his co-heiresses and was succeeded by the line of Tyrells which appears to be the one shown here. However, ''Visitati
2 CONC on'' does not show any daughters in this generation but continues with a son, Thomas, father of Richard father (by dau/coheir of Sir John Wattevile) of Sir William who had 4 wives of whom Mary, dau/heir of Sir John Hawkwood, was m
2 CONC other of 4 daughters including Elianor who m. John Tirrell of Heron, Treasurer of the Household of King Henry 6. ''BEB1841'' ('Tyrrell of Springfield') identifies the wife of Treasurer Sir John Tyrrell as Alice, dau/coheir of Sir 
2 CONC William, Coggeshall of Little Stamford Hall, Essex. '''We presume that''' ''Visitation'' has inserted too many generations but identify the 4 daughters of this William as those shown by ''Visitation'' as some generations later (ex
2 CONC cept that ''Visitation'' names Lady Tyrell as Elianor rather than Alice). ''Visitation'' names the mother of those daughters as Mary Hawkwood but ''BEB1841'', supported by 'The Genealogical Magazine' (vol 3, 1899-1900, 'Hawkwood-J
2 CONC osselyn Pedigree', p103), names her ... <Antiocha Hawkwood.>
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
