2 CONT
2 CONT Commentary from an unidentified Geni member:
2 CONT
2 CONT >The aforementioned History of Parliament bio is a bit diplomatic. The "White Company" of mercenaries terrified Europe, even extorting a huge ransom from the Pope. They frequently decided that they would call themselves knights, a
2 CONC lthough no-one with the authority to knight them had done so. (Reading between the lines, this appears to have been the case with "Sir" William. The practice of systematically recording who had been properly knighted dates from th
2 CONC is time, to distinguish real knights from self-promoted mercenaries. Real knights were forbidden from going abroad to fight without the King's licence; "Sir" William was in Italy while England was at war with France, and absented 
2 CONC himself from all the major battles of the Hundred Years War including Agincourt. Of course if you came back rich enough from your mercenary campaigns, all might be forgiven, though you might not be considered very reliable (as he 
2 CONC clearly was not).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes for Sir William de Coggeshall
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke says he was of Little Stamford Hall, Essex.
2 CONT
2 CONT G F Beaumont says he was of Codham Hall, Wethersfield but lived at Coggeshall for some of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Stonor Saunders in her biography of him says he spent most of his life as an adventurer in Italy, holding various towns and princes to serious ransom.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1388 Calendar of Patent Rolls 12 Richard II Part I
2 CONT July 10 Westminster. Commission to William Rykhill and John Casy to enquire and certify touching the following circumstances: Ricards, late the wife of Thomas Fychet, knight, whom William Coggeshale has married, being lately seise
2 CONC d of a third part of the manors of Tremertheret, Trenant, Leskyret, Manely, Seintcleere and certain lands in Canlese and Treworra, Co Cornwall, as dower in right of William Hywyssh, her former husband, the said Thomas, while he wa
2 CONC s her husband, demised the third aforesaid to Robert Tresilian for life, at the yearly rent of 40 marks, the said Robert having no othere estate therein and having no certainty as to the time of death of the said Thomas, who died 
2 CONC in Spain, kept the said third until he was convicted in the last Parliament of treason, for which reason the premises are now in the king's hand. By K.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
