2 CONT * https://stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4rz/czmisc16.php#coges2 (membership required in order to view without interruption)
2 CONT ** m1. Alice Coggeshall (dau/coheir of Sir William Coggeshall, widow of Sir John Tyrrell of Herons). m2. John Langham (son/heir of Sir William Langham of Pantfield.
2 CONT *** This conflicts with John Tyrrell having a second wife.
2 CONT * https://stirnet.com/genie/data/british/tt/tyrrell01.php#con1 (membership required in order to view without interruption)
2 CONT ** Sir John Tirrell of Heron, Sheriff of Essex & Hertfordshire (a 1423, Treasurer of the Household to King Henry VI) m. Alice Coggeshall (d 1422, dau of Sir William Coggeshall of Little Stamford Hall, m2. John, son/heir of Sir Wil
2 CONC liam Langham of Pantfield)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT ===Alice Coggeshall
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice was born Abt. 1388 in England and died in 1422 in England. She is buried in East Horndon, Essex, England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Sir John  Tyrrell ca. 1407. He was born 1390 in Heron, England and died 1437 in England.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Granddaughter of the famous English soldier, Sir John Hawkwood, Knight of Essex, who for many years during the wars in Italy was commanding General of the Armies of Florence. In a Chapel at East Horndon there remains to this day a
2 CONC  beautiful alabaster slab tablet to the memory of Lady Alice Tyrrell, upon which were outlined her figure and face, placed in the church 1422. Dicken says that she was a co-heiress to her father's fortunes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Tyrrell_%28died_1437%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Tyrrell (c.1382 – 2 April 1437),[1] of Heron in the Essex parish of East Horndon, was an English landowner, lawyer, administrator, and politician who was chosen three times as Speaker of the House of Commons. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT married firstly, at some time before 1411,[citation needed] Alice Coggeshall (died 1422), daughter and co-heiress of Sir William Coggeshall[1][13] by his wife Antiocha Hawkwood, daughter and heiress of Sir John Hawkwood,[14][15] b
2 CONC y whom he had five surviving sons[1] and four daughters,[16] including:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir Thomas Tyrrell (c. 1411 – 28 March 1477) of Heron, eldest son and heir not only to his father[1][13] but also to his uncle Edward Tyrrell (died 1442). He married Anne Marney, daughter of Sir William Marney (died 21 or 24 Aug
2 CONC ust 1414) by his wife Elizabeth Sergeaux, by whom he had four sons and two daughters:[1] …
2 CONT # William Tyrrell of Gipping, Suffolk, beheaded on Tower Hill 23 February 1462, who married Margaret Darcy, by whom he was the father of Sir James Tyrrell.[1]
2 CONT # William Tyrrell (died c. 1471) of Beeches in Rawreth, Essex, who married firstly Anne Fitz Simon, the daughter of Robert Fitz Simon, and secondly Philippa Thornbury, the daughter of John Thornbury.[1][30]
2 CONT # Alice Tyrrell (died 1460), who married firstly Hamo Strange, secondly William Skrene the younger (died 1431), eldest son of William Skrene, Chief Baron of the Irish Exchequer, and thirdly Thomas Pigot, and had a son, John Skrene
2 CONC  (died 1452), by her second husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married secondly, at some time before 1427,[31] Katherine Burgate (died after 1436). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
