1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00012534&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT From the English Wikipedia page on Philip I, Count of Katzenelnbogen:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_I,_Count_of_Katzenelnbogen
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip I of Katzenelnbogen (1402—1479), also known "Philip the Elder" was Count of Katzenelnbogen from 1444 to 1479 and was the last male descendant of the Counts of Katzenelnbogen (his two sons died before him). His parents were 
2 CONC John IV, Count of Katzenelnbogen (younger line) and Anne of Katzenelnbogen (older line), who merged the two lines of the family back together in 1402.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip married on 24 February 1422 in Darmstadt with Anna of Württemberg (1408–1471), daughter of Eberhard IV "the Younger" of Württemberg. In 1456, he obtained from the Pope a divorce from bed-and-board. In 1474 Philip married An
2 CONC na of Nassau-Dillenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip had three children with his first wife:
2 CONT *1. Philip the Younger (* 1427; † 27 February 1453), married in 1450 Ottilie of Nassau. In 1453 they had a daughter Ottilie of Katzenelnbogen.
2 CONT *2. Eberhard († 1456), canon of Cologne, was stabbed in Bruges (Flanders).
2 CONT *3. Anna (* 5 September 1443; † 16 February 1494), married in 1458 margrave Henry III of Hesse (15 October 1441 — 13 January 1483). In 1471, they had a son William III, who was the last male descendant of this line of the House of
2 CONC  Hesse.
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1444 Philip initiated a major renovation of the collegiate church of Sankt Goar.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1449 he bought off the rights on St. Goar held by abbot John of the Abbey at Prüm.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1470 he handed Upper Katzenelnbogen and its seat Darmstadt to his son-in-law Henry III of Hesse.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip's sons Eberhard and Philip the younger died before his death, so when Philip died in 1479, the Katzenelnbogen died out in the male line. The County of Katzenelnbogen fell to the Landgraviate of Hesse, which was ruled at the
2 CONC  time by Philip's son-in-law Henry III of Hesse in Marburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT External links
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Philip I of Katzenelnbogen (timeline)
2 CONT * http://www.graf-von-katzenelnbogen.de/pda.html History of the Counts of Katzenelnbogen
2 CONT * http://www.regionalgeschichte.net/hauptportal/bibliothek/texte/geschichte-mittelrhein/die-grafen-von-katzenelnbogen.html
