1 NOTE Sigismund (1368-1437), Holy Roman Emperor, son of the Emperor Charles IV. Sigismund was elected Holy Roman emperor in 1410. He was the author and protector of the Council of Constance, called together for the purpose of ending the
2 CONC  Hussite and other schisms; but the martyrdom of John Huss led to the Hussite War. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
1 NOTE Sigismund (1368-1437), Holy Roman emperor (1411-37) and king of Hungary 
2 CONT (1387-1437) and Bohemia (1419-37), the son of Holy Roman Emperor Charles 
2 CONT IV. In 1385 he married Queen Mary of Hungary (1370-95), thus acceding to 
2 CONT the throne of Hungary two years later. In 1396 he led a great army of 
2 CONT Crusaders from many parts of Europe against the Turks; the latter, under 
2 CONT the Ottoman sultan Bayazid I, inflicted a crushing defeat upon Sigismund's 
2 CONT forces at Nicopolis (now Nikopol), Bulgaria. Upon the death of Holy Roman 
2 CONT Emperor Rupert (1352-1410), Sigismund was elected to succeed him, but he 
2 CONT did not receive formal coronation at the hands of the pope until 1433. In 
2 CONT 1414 Sigismund persuaded the antipope John XXIII to convoke the Council of 
2 CONT Constance at which a longstanding dispute over the papal succession was 
2 CONT settled and ecclesiastical reforms were instituted. The council also tried 
2 CONT the Bohemian religious reformer John Huss (Jan Hus) and condemned and 
2 CONT executed him as a heretic. Sigismund succeeded to the throne of Bohemia in 
2 CONT 1419. His power in Bohemia was never more than nominal, however, as the 
2 CONT Bohemians believed him guilty of complicity in the death of Huss and 
2 CONT repeatedly rose in arms against him.
1 NOTE Sigismund of Luxembourg, aka Sigismund of Brandenburg, succeeded to the throne of Hungary by virtue of marriage to the daughter of Louis the Great, who died without a male heir. 1387.  King Mary (as she was called) had been depose
2 CONC d in 1386 by Charles III of Naples and imprisoned.  Sigismund rescued her, and they resumed the throne of Hungary.  Mary died in 1395, and Sigismund ruled Hungary alone until he died in 1437.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigismund of Brandenburg married Marie of Hungary, then became known as Sigismund of Hungary, and ruled Germany from 1410 to 1437, in rivalry with Jobst or Jossus of Moravia and rupert of the Palatine. Sigismund won out, and ruled
2 CONC  until he died in 1437, having succeeded his brother Wenceslaus to the throne.  Sigismund was succeeded by Albert II of Hapsburg, his son-in-law.
