1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''''===PLZ insert some historical trace that leads him illegitimate child of https://www.geni.com/people/Friedrich-III-Holy-Roman-Emperor/5406067539320083175 
2 CONT  Babtism/Conformation Certificate from Evangelic Church in Lubeck
2 CONT
2 CONT *Seit 1465 Vice-Konig as replacing his Father and halfbrother during their absence
2 CONT * Since 1470 citizen in Thorn as a Wholesale Merchant, 1471 Aldermen, 1473 Councilor, 1483 Mayor and President,
2 CONT  three times burgrave, Count / Graf / Burgrave magistrate in Chełmn and Castles of Świecie and Dybów
2 CONT  • His first childless marriage around 1471 was probably to an aunt of Reinh. Feldstedt. Justine Feldstedt, older widow with 13 children. 
2 CONT  • "One of the richest and most powerful Thorner patricians of his time", "a very respected man".
2 CONT  • 1479 at the Polish Reichtag in Peterkau. Often Ambassador at Estates and City Days.
2 CONT  • In 1480 He and Johann Rockendorf donated an altar in the St. John's Church in Thorn.
2 CONT  • roman Knight of Equestrian Order of Jerusalem.
2 CONT  • In 1490 He bought an estate in Sackerau (Zakrzewo). Hereditary Lord of Slawkowo, Gostkowo (= Kirchtauer Vogelsang), Niederbriesen, Bruckow, Preußisch Lanke and others
2 CONT  • In 1491 He campaigned for the reform of the Franciscan Monastery of St. Mary in Thorn.
2 CONT  • In 1495 He and Reinhold Feldstedt acquired the village of Klempin near Danzig. He had the right to live in Rogasen and Roggenhausen near Thorn.
2 CONT *Sailor in Hanza, owner of 4 ships, flisac boats, his own quays and estates all over the World for example in London, inherited estates in Nethetlands from his father's brother;
2 CONT *Manager and Captain of the Castle in Świecie. He commanded it's defense many times.
2 CONT * co-owner of a vineyard, stables of cold-blooded horses and town houses left by his father-in-law and next brother-in-law Watzenrode, his Son Lucas. His own House was by street Szeroka 19 in Thorn.
2 CONT  • Buried in St. Mary's stone number 61.
2 CONT [Weichbrodt, vol.3 p.181, vol.1 p.5.]
2 CONT  [Weichbrodt [Bd.3 p.181] 
2 CONT [ H.D.Lemmel: "Beiträge zu Copernicus und seiner Verwandtschaft", in: Genealogie Heft 1-2 1993]
2 CONT http://geneal.lemmel.at/Copernicus.html
2 CONT Hohenzollern (1415–1535) (Berlin: Duncker & Humblot, 1963)
2 CONT Neitmann K., Die Staasteverträge des Deutschen Ordens in Preußen 1230–1449 (Neue Forschungen zur Brandenburg-Preussische Geschichte, Bd. 6) (Köln–Wien: Böhlau, 1986).
2 CONT [Jacob Heinrich Zernecke Thornische Chronica]
2 CONT
2 CONT Połączony poprzez małżeństwo z Cristinum von Allen / von Altenstein / von Saxe-Altenburg z rodzinami:
2 CONT -Altenburg, Wettin, Habsburg-Lothrinian
2 CONT - Reuss - Ebersdorf, rodzina angielskiej Królowej Wiktorii i Cesarza Frederika I
2 CONT - Roggendorf
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Christina von Allen, who had married '''Heinrich Krüger''', the mayor of Thorun in 1495, [https://books.google.it/books?id=9r0RfQtpU6AC&pg=PA59&lpg=PA59&dq=Christina+von+Allen&source=bl&ots=G4LomWuDJH&sig=ACfU3U3cxDhaeeN-plB1h6Q7C
2 CONC FP6FHkzcg&hl=it&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwil7vnU-r_oAhWLw4sKHWPaDdEQ6AEwAnoECAkQAQ#v=onepage&q=Christina%20von%20Allen&f=false ...''book: '''The Life of Copernicus (1473-1543)''' Di Pierre Gassendi, Oliver Thill'']
2 CONT
