1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Beatrycze''' - '''królowa Niemiec''', '''księżna bawarska'''. [http://pl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatrycze_%C5%9Awidnicka Wikipedia PL]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Beatrix von Schlesien-Glogau''' - war die erste Ehefrau Ludwigs des Bayern, den sie um das Jahr 1308 wohl in ihrer Heimat Schlesien heiratete, da kein Dokument oder Bericht eines bayerischen Chronisten darüber vorhanden ist. [h
2 CONC ttp://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beatrix_von_Schlesien-Glogau Wikipedia DE]
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix of Świdnica
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix of Świdnica (Polish: Beatrycze Świdnicka, German: Beatrix von Schweidnitz ; b. 1290 - d. Munich, 25 August 1322), was a Polish princess member of the House of Piast in the Silesian branch of Jawor-Świdnica and by marriage 
2 CONC Duchess of Bavaria and German Queen.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the second daughter of Bolko I the Strict, Duke of Jawor-Świdnica, by his wife Beatrix, daughter of Otto V the Long, Margrave of Brandenburg-Salzwedel.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Life
2 CONT
2 CONT After her father's early death in 1301, Beatrix and her siblings were placed under the tutelage of their maternal uncle Herman II, Margrave of Brandenburg-Salzwedel until 1305, when the oldest son of Bolko I, Bernard, asumed the g
2 CONC overnment of his domains and the guardianship of his younger siblings, included Beatrix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Was precisely his brother Bernard who, wanted to secure an alliance with Bavaria, arranged Beatrix's marriage with Louis IV, Duke of Upper Bavaria. The wedding took place by 14 October 1308. During her marriage, Beatrix gave birth
2 CONC  six children, but only three survive adulthood: Mathilde -by marriage Margravine of Meissen-, Louis V the Brandenburger -later Duke of Upper Bavaria, Margrave of Brandenburg and Count of Tyrol- and Stephen II -later Duke of Lower
2 CONC  Bavaria-.
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Louis IV was elected King of Germany on 20 October 1314. However another faction had elected Frederick I of Austria as King on 19 October. The two rival Kings would continue their dispute for the rest of her life. She was one
2 CONC  of two rival Queens of Germany with Isabel of Aragon, wife of Frederick I.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix died long time after her husband's coronation as Holy Roman Emperor (in 1328). Two years after her death, Louis IV remarried with Margaret of Holland.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT [http://de.rodovid.org/wk/Person:10920]
