1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie of Alencon
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Alencon (29 March 1373 – 1417) was a French noblewoman, a Princess of the Blood, and the wife of John VII of Harcourt, Count of Harcourt and of Aumale, Viscount of Chatellerault, Baron of Elbeuf, of Mézières, of Lillebone
2 CONC , of La Saussaye.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie was born on 29 March 1373, at the Chateau d' Essay, Orne, France the daughter of Peter II of Alencon (1340- 20 September 1404) and Marie Chamaillart, Viscountess of Beaumont-au-Maine. Her paternal grandparents were Charles I
2 CONC I of Alencon (Killed 26 August 1346 at The Battle of Crecy) and Maria de La Cerda. Charles was a younger brother of King Philip VI of France. Her maternal grandparents were Guillaume Chamaillart, Viscount of Beaumont-Brienne, Sire
2 CONC  d'Anthenaise, and Marie de Beaumont, Dame de Beaumont-le-Vicomte. Marie's father was knighted in 1350. At The Battle of Poitiers in 1356, he was taken hostage in exchange for King John II of France. He did not return home until 1
2 CONC 370. On 20 October 1371, he married Marie Chamaillart (died 18 November 1425 at Chateau d'Argentan). Marie was their eldest daughter; she had seven siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]List of siblings
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre of Alencon (1374-1375)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean of Alencon (1375-1376)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Alencon (1377-1377)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne of Alencon (1378-6 August 1403
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine of Alencon (1380 Verneuil-sur-Avre -25 June 1462. She married firstly in 1411, Peter d' Evreux, Infante of Navarre, Count of Mortain, and secondly on 1 October 1413, Louis VII, Duke of Bavaria-Ingolstadt. By her last mar
2 CONC riage she had a son Johann (Born 6 February 1415) and an unnamed daughter. Both children died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite of Alencon (1383- after 1400). Nun at Argentan.
2 CONT
2 CONT John I of Alencon, Duke of Alencon (9 May 1385-25 October 1415 at The Battle of Agincourt). On 26 June 1396, he married Marie of Brittany (18 February 1391-18 December 1446). They had five children, including his heir, John II of 
2 CONC Alencon.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie married John VII, Count of Harcourt and of Aumale (1369-18 December 1452) in Paris on 17 May 1389 at the age of sixteen. He was the son of John VI, Count of Harcourt and Catherine de Bourbon. The marriage produced three chil
2 CONC dren, Through her eldest daughter Marie, Marie of Alencon was the ancestress of Mary, Queen of Scots, King Henry IV of France, King Louis XIV of France, and Henrietta Maria of France, Queen-Consort of King Charles I of England. Ma
2 CONC rie died in 1417 about two years after her husband, having distinguished himself at the Battle of Agincourt, was taken prisoner by the victorious English troops, led by King Henry V. John died in 1452.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children
2 CONT
2 CONT John VIII of Harcourt, Count of Aumale (9 April 1396 Chateau d'Harcourt, Calvados -17 August 1424 at The Battle of Verneuil). He was the senior French Commander at the battle. By mistress Marguerite de Preullay, he had one illegit
2 CONC imate son, Louis II of Harcourt
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Harcourt, Countess of Aumale (9 September 1398 Chateau d'Harcourt, Calvados -19 April 1476). She married, on 12 August 1416, Antoine of Vaudémont, Count of Vaudémont, Sire of Joinville (1401-22 March 1458), by whom she ha
2 CONC d five children including Frederic II of Vaudémont, Count of Vaudemont, Sire of Joinville (May 1428-31 August 1470 Joinville), who in his turn in 1445, married Yolande de Bar of Anjou, elder sister of Margaret of Anjou, Queen-Cons
2 CONC ort of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne of Harcourt, Countess of Harcourt (11 September 1399 Chateau d' Harcourt, Calvados -1456). She married firstly in 1414, Jean, Seigneur de Rieux et de Rochfort, Baron d'Ancenis (died 1431). She married secondly in 1434, Bert
2 CONC rand de Dinan, Baron de Chateaubriant, Marshal of Brittany. She had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT Pére Anselm "Histoire des Rois de France"
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Royal Family: A Genealogy" by Francois Velde
2 CONT
2 CONT le Maison des Ducs D'Alencon
2 CONT
2 CONT Stammtafeln zur Geschichte der Europaischen Staaten, 4 volumes, Marburg, 1953, 1975
