2 CONT Catherine had 11 siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Charles, Dauphin of Viennois (born and died 1386)
2 CONT     Jeanne (1388 – 1390)
2 CONT     Isabella (1389 – 1409), married (1) Richard II, King of England, no issue (2) Charles, Duke of Orléans, had issue
2 CONT     Jeanne (1391 – 1433), married John V, Duke of Brittany, had issue
2 CONT     Charles, Dauphin of Viennois (1392 – 1401), died young
2 CONT     Marie (1393 – 1438), unmarried, became a nun
2 CONT     Michelle (1395 – 1422), married Philip the Good, Duke of Burgundy, no surviving issue
2 CONT     Louis, Dauphin of Viennois (1397 – 1415), married Margaret of Burgundy, no issue
2 CONT     John, Dauphin of Viennois (1398 – 1417), married Jacqueline, Countess of Hainaut, no issue
2 CONT     Charles, Dauphin of Viennois (1403 – 1461), married Marie of Anjou, had issue; became Charles VII, King of France, after his father’s death
2 CONT     Philip (born and died in 1407)
2 CONT
2 CONT Owen and Catherine had at least six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Thomas Tudor (1429 – 1501) He became a monk at Westminster Abbey and was known as Edward Bridgewater.
2 CONT     Edmund Tudor, 1st Earl of Richmond (1430 – 1456) He married Lady Margaret Beaufort, and they were the parents of Henry Tudor, the future King Henry VII, and died of the plague shortly before his son’s birth.
2 CONT     Jasper Tudor, 1st Earl of Pembroke and 1st Duke of Bedford (1431 – 1495) He married Catherine Woodville, daughter of Richard Woodville, 1st Earl Rivers and Jacquetta of Luxembourg.  He had no legitimate children but did have t
2 CONC wo illegitimate children. One was Joan Tudor, an ancestor of Oliver Cromwell.
2 CONT     Owen Tudor (1432–1510) He became a monk at Westminster Abbey.
2 CONT     Tacinda Tudor (b. 1433) She married Reginald Grey, Baron Grey of Wilton and had issue.
2 CONT     (Daughter) Tudor (b. c. 1435)  She became a nun.
2 CONT     Margaret (Catherine) Tudor (born January 1437) She died shortly after birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine died at Bermondsey Abbey on January 3, 1437 following the birth of her last child and was buried in Westminster Abbey.
