1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Jasper Tudor, 1st Duke of Bedford, 1st Earl of Pembroke, KG (Welsh: Siasbar Tudur) (c. 1431 – 21/26 December 1495) was the uncle of King Henry VII of England and the architect of his successful conquest of England
2 CONC  and Wales in 1485.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was from the noble Tudor family of Penmynydd, North Wales. Jasper Tudor bore the arms of the kingdom, with the addition of a bordure azure with martlets or (that is, a blue border featuring golden martlets)."
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no contemporary, or near contemporary, evidence that he had an illegitimate daughter named Joan.  Please see the discussion at https://www.geni.com/discussions/170319
2 CONT ==================================================================================
