2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Frederick II Hohenzollern, Elector and Katherina von Sachsen, Kurfürstin zu Brandenburg 
2 CONT * Dorothea of Brandenburg (1446 – March 1519) was a princess of Brandenburg by birth and by marriage Duchess of Saxe-Lauenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAXONY.htm#BernhardIILauenburgdied1463A Project MedLands Saxony Dukes]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''BERNHARD von Sachsen-Lauenburg, son of ERICH IV Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg & his wife Sophie von Braunschweig''' (-16 Jul 1463, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Bernd”, who inherit
2 CONC ed “de Herschopp to Louenborch”, third of the three sons of “Hertoghe Ereke to Sassen, ein Her to Louenborch” and his wife[694].  He succeeded his brother in 1435 as BERNHARD II Herzog von Sachsen in Lauenburg und Ratzeburg.  '''m
2 CONC arried  (2 Feb 1429) ADELHEID von Pommern, daughter of BOGISLAW VIII Duke of Pomerania in Hinterpommern & his wife Sophie von Holstein ([1410]-after 1445).'''  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum records that “Hertoghe Ber
2 CONC nd, Hertoghen Ereken sone to Sassen, unde eyn Here to Louenborch” married “Alheys, des Hertoghen dochter to Pomeren in der Slesye”[695]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bernhard von Sachsen-Lauenburg & his wife ADELHEID von Pommern had two children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         '''JOHANN von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (18 Jul 1439-15 Aug 1507, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Johanns”, who succeeded his father, as the son of “Hertoghe Bernd, Hertoghen E
2 CONC reken sone to Sassen, unde eyn Here to Louenborch” and his wife[696].  He succeeded his father in 1463 as JOHANN V Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg.  '''married  (Lüneburg 12 Feb 1464) DOROTHEA von Brandenburg, daughter of FRIEDRICH I
2 CONC I Markgraf and Elector of Brandenburg & his wife Katharina von Sachsen (1446-1519 before 20 Mar, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).'''  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Dorothea”, who married “Hertoghen Hans te Loenborch”
2 CONC , second of the two daughters of “Marggreve Frederick de elder, Marggreve Frederikes sone to Brandenborch” and his wife[697].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann & his wife DOROTHEA von Brandenburg had thirteen children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>* a)        ''' ERICH von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-20 Oct 1522).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Erekes” first among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” and 
2 CONC his wife[698].  Canon at Köln Cathedral 1490.  Canon at Hildesheim Cathedral 1492.  Elected Bishop of Hildesheim 1503/1504.  Bishop of Münster 1508.
2 CONT >>>* b)         '''MAGNUS von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-1 Aug 1543, bur Ratzeburg Cathedral).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Magnus” second among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen
2 CONC  under so Louenborch” and his wife[699].  He succeeded his father in 1507 as MAGNUS I Herzog von Sachsen-Lauenburg. 
2 CONT >>>* c)         '''BERNHARD von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-3 Jan 1524).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Bernd” third among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” and
2 CONC  his wife[700].  Provost at Münster Cathedral 1510.  Canon and provost at Köln, St Gereon 1512.
2 CONT >>>* d)         '''JOHANN von Sachsen-Lauenburg''' (-20 Nov 1547).  Botho’s Chronicon Brunsvicensium Picturatum names “Hans” fourth among the seven sons of “Hertoghe Hans, Hertoghen Berndes sone to Sassen under so Louenborch” and 
2 CONC his wife[701].  Bishop of Hildesheim 1504, resigned 1527.   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann had two illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>>* i)          '''JOHANN von Sachsen''' .  A priest in Berkenthin, near Ratzeburg 1538.
2 CONT >>>>>* ii)         '''BERNHARD von Sachsen''' ([1530-Livonia [1592/1612]).  He served in the Swedish army.  '''married firstly (before 1555) ---''' (-1590).  '''married secondly (before 1591) DOROTHEA von Lewald, daughter of JOHAN
2 CONC N von Lewald [Liebenrode] zu Malla & his wife Magdalene von Rosen a.d.H. Hochrosen.'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bernhard von Sachsen & his unknown first wife had three children'''
2 CONT
