1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Primary Sources
2 CONT 1463/4 12 Kal. April. (21 March.) Siena. (f. 153.)	<br>
2 CONT To '''Humphrey Audeley, nobleman, donsel, and Elisabeth, noblewoman, relict of James Lottrell''', of the diocese of Bath and Wells. Absolution from sentence of excommunication incurred by their having formerly, not being ignorant 
2 CONC that they were related in the second degree of affinity, contracted marriage per verba legitime de presenti, and consummated it, although they did not have it solemnized before the church; with dispensation to contract the said ma
2 CONC rriage anew (de novo), have it solemnized before the church and remain therein, decreeing the offspring born, if any, and that to be born of the marriage legitimate for all legal purposes. (fn. 2)Oblate siquidem nobis. (G. de Picc
2 CONC olominibus. | lxxx. A. de Urbino. N. [de] Benzis.) [In the margin: Februarii and Jo. Horn, O. Principis. 2/3 p.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: 'Vatican Regesta 513: 1464', in Calendar of Papal Registers Relating To Great Britain and Ireland: Volume 11, 1455-1464, ed. J A Twemlow (London, 1921), pp. 677-678. British History Online http://www.british-history.ac.uk/
2 CONC cal-papal-registers/brit-ie/vol11/pp677-678 [accessed 22 September 2017].
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Touchet,_5th_Baron_Audley (Humphrey's father)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=102049446
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir Humphrey Touchet (born circa 1435 - May 6, 1471). He married Elizabeth Courtenay, widow of Sir James Luttrell. Like his father, he supported the House of Lancaster. He was taken prisoner at the battle of Tewkesbury and tried 
2 CONC before Richard, Duke of Gloucester and the Duke of Norfolk. Executed with other Lancastrian leaders in the Market Square he was buried under the pavement in the Chapel of St Nicolas, in the Abbey Church of St Mary the Virgin."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Humphrey Audley:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p4730.htm#i47298
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Humphrey Audley [1]
2 CONT *M, #47298, 
2 CONT *b. after 1430, 
2 CONT *d. 4 May 1471
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Sep 2005
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.02%
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Humphrey Audley was born after 1430. He was the son of James Tuchet, 5th Lord Audley (of Heleigh) and Eleanor de Holland.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 4 May 1471 at Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire, England, killed in action.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Tewkesbury on 4 May 1471.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT An ancestor of the Audley family of Norfolk.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
