2 CONT From Medlands
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#ThomasHolanddied1360B
2 CONT
2 CONT son of Sir ROBERT de Holand of Upholland, Lancashire & his wife Matilda La Zouche '''(1314-in Normandy 26 or 28 Dec 1360, bur Stamford, Church of the Grey Friars).  He served the king in various military expeditions in Flanders, B
2 CONC ayonne, and Brittany, and fought at the battle of Crécy 26 Aug 1346.  During his absence in Prussia, his wife went through a form of marriage with William Montagu Earl of Salisbury.  In May 1347, he petitioned Pope Clement VI who 
2 CONC ordered Joan to return to Sir Thomas 17 Nov 1349.  Appointed Joint Lieutenant and Captain of Normandy 28 Oct 1359, jointly with Philippe de Navarre Comte de Longueville.  Summoned to a Council 1353/4 as Lord Holand.  He was one of
2 CONC  the founder Knights of the Order of the Garter.  He succeeded as Earl of Kent, de iure uxoris.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m (1339 or before) as her first husband, JOAN of Kent''', daughter of EDMUND Earl of Kent & his wife Margaret Baroness Wake (29 Sep 1328-Wallingford Castle, Berkshire 7, 8 or 21 Aug 1385, bur 29 Jan 1386 Greyfriars Church, Stam
2 CONC ford, Lincolnshire, probably later transferred to London).  '''She separated from her first husband shortly after their marriage'''.  She married secondly (bigamously, before 10 Feb 1341, annulled by Papal Bull 17 Nov 1349) as his
2 CONC  first wife, William de Montagu.  '''She returned to her first husband in [1349] after her second marriage was annulled'''.  She succeeded her brother in 1352 as Countess of Kent, Baroness Woodstock and Baroness Wake, suo iure.  S
2 CONC he was known as the Fair Maid of Kent.  She married thirdly (Papal dispensation 10 Sep 1361, St Stephen’s Chapel, Palace of Westminster or Canterbury Cathedral or Windsor Castle 10 Oct 1361) Edward "of Woodstock" Prince of Wales. 
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Earl Thomas & his wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1.         THOMAS de Holand ([1350]-25 Apr 1397, bur Bourne Abbey, Lincolnshire).  He succeeded his father as Earl of Kent.    
2 CONT *-        see below.  
2 CONT
2 CONT *2.         EDMUND de Holand ([1351/52]-young).  
2 CONT
2 CONT *3.         JOAN de Holand (1350-Nantes Nov 1384, bur Nantes, Abbaye de Notre dame de Prières).  m (London May 1366) as his second wife, JEAN V "le Vaillant" Duke of Brittany, son of JEAN IV Duke of Brittany & his wife Jeanne de F
2 CONC landre ([Nov/Dec] 1339 or [30 Sep/8 Dec] 1340-Nantes 1/2 Nov 1399, bur Nantes Cathedral). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *4.         JOHN de Holand (after 1358-executed 9/10 Jan 1400, bur Pleshy, Collegiate Church).  Appointed Lieutenant of Ireland in Aug 1382.  In [May] 1384, he murdered a Carmelite friar who had charged John of Gaunt with high tre
2 CONC ason.  In Jul 1385, he killed the Earl of Stafford's eldest son, in revenge for the death of his squire who had been killed in a quarrel by one of the Earl of Stafford's archers, but he was pardoned 2 Feb 1386.  Appointed Constabl
2 CONC e of the army which John of Gaunt took to Spain to enforce his claim to the throne of Castile, it was on John de Holand's advice that John abandoned this unsuccessful enterprise.  He was created Earl of Huntingdon 2 Jun 1388, and 
2 CONC Duke of Exeter 29 Sep 1397.  He was accused of complicity in the murder of Thomas Duke of Gloucester 29 Oct 1399.  He joined in the plot to seize King Henry IV, but was captured at Prittlewell, Essex and taken to Pleshy Castle whe
2 CONC re he was executed.  He was declared a traitor by Parliament in Jan 1401, and his possessions confiscated and titles forfeited[695].  m (Plymouth 24 Jun 1386) as her second husband, ELIZABETH of Lancaster, divorced wife of JOHN Ha
2 CONC stings Earl of Pembroke, daughter of JOHN "of Gaunt" Duke of Lancaster & his first wife Blanche of Lancaster (Burford, Shropshire before 21 Feb 1363-24 Nov 1425, bur Burford Church, Shropshire).  She deserted her first husband, wa
2 CONC s seduced by her second husband, whom she hurriedly married as she was pregnant.  She married thirdly (before 12 Dec 1400) as his second wife, Sir John Cornwall.  Duke John & his wife had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT **a)         CONSTANCE de Holand (1387-12 or 14 Nov 1437, bur London, St Katherine´s by the Tower).  m firstly (1404) THOMAS Mowbray Duke of Norfolk, son of THOMAS Mowbray Duke of Norfolk & his second wife Elizabeth FitzAlan of Ar
2 CONC undel (1385-executed 1405).  m secondly (1413) Sir JOHN Grey of Ruthin, son of REYNOLD Grey Lord Grey of Ruthin & his first wife Margaret de Roos of Helmsley, Yorkshire (-27 Aug 1439).  
2 CONT
2 CONT **b)         RICHARD de Holand (-3 Sep 1400).  
2 CONT
2 CONT **c)         EDWARD de Holand (-young).  
2 CONT
2 CONT **d)         ALICE de Holand ([1392]-before 1406).  m (before 1400) as his first wife, RICHARD de Vere, son of AUBREY de Vere Earl of Oxford & his wife Alice FitzWalter ([1385]-15 Feb 1417, bur Earl's Colne).  He succeeded his fat
2 CONC her in 1400 as Earl of Oxford.  
2 CONT
2 CONT **e)         JOHN de Holand (Dartington, Devon 29 Mar 1395-5 Aug 1447 bur London, Church of St Katharine by the Tower).  He was taken prisoner at the battle of Baugé 22 Mar 1421 and remained in captivity for five years[696].  He w
2 CONC as created Duke of Exeter 6 Jan 1444.  m firstly (before 15 Jul 1427) as her second husband, ANNE Stafford, widow of EDMUND Mortimer Earl of March and Ulster, daughter of EDMUND Stafford Earl of Stafford & his wife Anne Ctss of Bu
2 CONC ckingham (-20 or 24 Sep 1432, bur London, Church of St Katharine by the Tower).  m secondly (licence 20 Jan 1433) as her second husband, dona BRITES de Portugal, widow of THOMAS Earl of Arundel and Surrey, illegitimate daughter of
2 CONC  dom JOÃO I King of Portugal & his mistress dona Inez Perez Esteves ([1386]-Bordeaux 23 Oct 1439, bur Arundel).  m thirdly as her third husband, ANNE Montagu, widow firstly of Sir RICHARD Hankeford and secondly of Sir LEWIS Johan,
2 CONC  daughter of JOHN Montagu 3rd Earl of Salisbury & his wife Matilda Fraunceys (-28 Nov 1457 bur London, Church of St Katharine by the Tower).  Duke John & his first wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT ***i)          HENRY de Holand (Tower of London 27 Jun 1430-drowned Sep 1475).  He succeeded his father in 1447 as Duke of Exeter.  He took part in Lord Egremont's rebellion in the north May 1454, was captured and sent to Pontefra
2 CONC ct Castle, and from there to Wallingford Castle.  A Lancastrian supporter, he fled to Scotland after the defeat at Towton and was attainted by Parliament 4 Nov 1461 and all his honours forfeited.  He escaped to Flanders, where he 
2 CONC seems to have been reduced to extreme poverty[697].  He returned to England during the brief restoration of King Henry VI in 1471, but was severely wounded at the battle of Barnet 14 Apr 1471 and captured.  He was released 20 May 
2 CONC 1475 and joined the king's expedition to France, but was drowned on the return journey between Calais and Dover[698].  m (before 30 Jul 1447, divorced 12 Nov 1472) as her first husband, ANNE of York, daughter of RICHARD Duke of Yo
2 CONC rk & his wife Cicely de Neville (Fotheringay Castle 10 Aug 1439-12 or 14 Jan 1476, bur St George’s Chapel, Windsor).  A manuscript pedigree dated to [1500] names "Cecily Duchess of York" as mother of "Anne Duchess of Exeter, also 
2 CONC wedded to Sir Thomas Saint Leger", and her children "Anthony Saint Leger, Anne"[699].  Duke Henry & his wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT ****(a)       ANNE de Holand (-[26 Aug 1467/6 Jun 1474]).  A manuscript pedigree dated to [1500] names "Cecily Duchess of York" as mother of "Anne Duchess of Exeter, also wedded to Sir Thomas Saint Leger", and her children "Anthon
2 CONC y Saint Leger, Anne"[700].  m (Greenwich Oct 1466) as his first wife, THOMAS Grey Lord Ferrers, son of Sir JOHN Grey Lord Ferres (of Groby) & his wife Elizabeth Wydeville (-20 Sep 1501, bur Astley, Warwickshire).  He was created E
2 CONC arl of Huntingdon in 1471, and Marquess of Dorset in 1475.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ***Duke Henry had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:  
2 CONT
2 CONT ****(b)        Sir ROBERT de Holand .  m MARGARET, daughter of ---.  Sir Robert & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT *****(1)        JOAN de Holand .  m firstly JOHN Kendall .  m secondly Sir JOHN Trelawny .  
2 CONT
2 CONT *****(2)        ELIZABETH de Holand .  m as his second wife, JOHN Reskimir .  No children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ***ii)         ANNE de Holand (-26 Dec 1486).  m firstly (1441) Sir JOHN Neville, son of RALPH Neville Earl of Westmoreland & his first wife Elizabeth Percy (-7 Mar 1450).  Lord Neville.  m secondly (1452) her first husband's uncl
2 CONC e, JOHN Neville Lord Neville, son of Sir JOHN Neville Lord Neville & his wife Elizabeth de Holand (-killed in battle Towton 1461).  m thirdly as his second wife, JAMES Douglas 9th Earl of Douglas, son of JAMES Douglas 7th Earl of 
2 CONC Douglas & his second wife Beatrice Sinclair (1425-Lindores Abbey [after 22 May] 1491, bur Lindores Abbey).  
2 CONT
2 CONT **Duke John had two illegitimate children by an unknown mistress:
2 CONT
2 CONT ***iii)        WILLIAM de Holand .  
2 CONT
2 CONT ***iv)        THOMAS de Holand .  
2 CONT
2 CONT *5.         MATILDA de Holand ([1359]-before 13 Apr 1392).  m firstly (Papal dispensation 5 Sep 1363) as his second wife, HUGH de Courtenay, son of Sir HUGH de Courtenay & his wife Elizabeth --- (-20 Feb 1374).  He was summoned to
2 CONC  parliament 8 Jan 1371, whereby he is held to have become Lord Courtenay.  m secondly (1380) as his first wife, VALERAN de Luxembourg Comte de Ligny et de Saint-Pol, son of GUY Comte de Ligny [Luxembourg] & his wife Mathilde de Ch
2 CONC âtillon Ctss de Saint-Pol (1355-château d'Yvoy 22 Apr 1415, bur Yvoy).  
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS de Holand, son of THOMAS de Holand of Broughton, Buckinghamshire & his wife Joan Ctss of Kent ([1350]-25 Apr 1397, bur Bourne Abbey, Lincolnshire).  He succeeded his father in 1360 as Earl of Kent, Lord Woodstock, Holand an
2 CONC d Wake.  He was appointed Marshal of England 13 Mar 1380, until 30 Jun 1385.  The will of "Thomas of Holand Earl of Kent and Lord Wake", proved 10 May 1397, chose burial “in the abbey of Brune”, bequeathed property to “Alice my wi
2 CONC fe...Thomas my son”[852]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m (after 10 Apr 1364) ALICE FitzAlan, daughter of RICHARD FitzAlan Earl of Arundel & his wife Eleanor of Lancaster ([1350]-17 Mar 1416).  The will of "Richard Earl of Arundel and Surrey", dated 5 Dec 1375, bequeathed property to “
2 CONC Richard my son...my son Thomas Bishop of Ely...John my son...Joane my daughter [...Countess of Hereford]...Alice my daughter...the eldest daughter of my said son John...Henry and Edward the younger sons of my said son John...Willi
2 CONC am another son of my said son John...my nephews and nieces sons and daughters of Roger le Strange and to my sister Dame Alaine le Strange wife to the said Roger...my...uncle John Arundell”[853].  The will of "Richard Earl of Arund
2 CONC el and Surrey", dated 4 Mar 1392, bequeathed property to “my...wife Philippa...hangings of the hall...with the arms of my sons the Earl Marshal, Lord Charlton and Monsr William Beauchamp...my sons Richard and Thomas...my daughter 
2 CONC Charlton...my daughter Elizabeth...my daughter Mareschal...my daughter Margaret...my brother the Archbishop of York...my...sister of Hereford...my...sister of Kent...my mother of Norfolk...my...niece of Gloucester”[854].  The will
2 CONC  of "Thomas of Holand Earl of Kent and Lord Wake", proved 10 May 1397, bequeathed property to “Alice my wife...Thomas my son”[855].  The will of "Elizabeth Juliers Countess of Kent", dated 20 Apr 1411, proved 29 Jun 1411, chose bu
2 CONC rial “in the church of the Friars Minors in the city of Winchester in the tomb of John late Earl of Kent late my husband”, bequeathed property to “my...sister Alice Countess of Kent...Joan Countess of Kent”[856].  Earl Thomas & hi
