1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ady Joan Holland, (1350–1384), was a Duchess consort of Brittany, married to John V, Duke of Brittany. [a] She was the daughter of Joan of Kent and Thomas Holland, 1st Earl of Kent. Her marriage to John V took plac
2 CONC e in London in May 1366. She had no children. Sources[edit]  Wikipedia _________________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Holland, 1st Earl of Kent, had issue, by the Lady Joan (shortly afterwards Princess of Wales), two sons: Thomas, 2nd Earl of Kent and John, Earl of Huntingdon & Duke of Exeter. He had also two daughters: '''Joan, the second
2 CONC  consort of John IV, Duke of Brittany'''; and Maud, married, first, to Hugh, Lord Courtenay, and, secondly, to Waleran, Count De St. Pol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * Joan Holland (born 1350, died after 25 December 1384) married (1366) John IV de Montfort (born 1365, died 1 November 1399), Count of Montfort, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT
