1 NOTE Earl of Exeter. After his father�s death and the remarriage of his mother to the Black Prince, John lived with them at Berkhampstead where he was under the supervision of the Prince�s yeoman John de la Haye. The family then left f
2 CONC or Gascony where Edward III had given lands to his son. They returned to Berkhampstead in 1372 where they lived until the Black Prince�s death in 1376. [THELMA.GED]
