2 CONT Sir Thomas Montagu BIRTH	13 Jun 1388 Wiltshire, England DEATH	3 Nov 1428 (aged 40) Departement d'Indre-et-Loire, Centre, France BURIAL	 Bisham Priory Bisham, Windsor and Maidenhead Royal Borough, Berkshire, England  MEMORIAL ID	62
2 CONC 844503 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 2 FLOWERS 61 AKA Thomas de Montacute, fourth earl of Salisbury, soldier, was the elder son of John Montagu, third earl of Salisbury and his wife, Maud Montagu (d. 1424), daughter of Adam Fraunceys, mayor of London,
2 CONC  and widow of John Aubrey, and of Sir Alan Buxhull (d. 1381). He died at Tourelles, France of wounds received in battle there, fighting during Joan of Arc's first major military victory.
2 CONT
