2 CONT Lady Alice Montagu Neville
2 CONT BIRTH 1406
2 CONT Salisbury, Wiltshire Unitary Authority, Wiltshire, England
2 CONT DEATH 9 Dec 1462 (aged 55–56)
2 CONT Bisham, Windsor and Maidenhead Royal Borough, Berkshire, England
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Bisham Priory
2 CONT Bisham, Windsor and Maidenhead Royal Borough, Berkshire, England 
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 84289509 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1420, Alice married Richard Neville, who became the 5th Earl of Salisbury by right of his marriage to Alice.
2 CONT Their main home was at Bisham Manor in Berkshire although their lands lay chiefly around Christchurch in Hampshire and Wiltshire. She is buried at the Montacute Mausoleum at Bisham Abbey Bisham,
2 CONT Togather they had 10 children:
2 CONT Joan Neville, 1423 - 9 September 1462, who married William FitzAlan, 16th Earl of Arundel
2 CONT Cecily Neville, 1424 - 28 July 1450, who married Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Warwick
2 CONT Richard Neville, 16th Earl of Warwick 1428 - 1471
2 CONT Alice Neville, 1430- 1503, who married Henry FitzHugh, 6th Baron FitzHugh
2 CONT John Neville, 1st Marquess of Montagu 1431 - 1471
2 CONT George Neville 1432 - 1476, who became Archbishop of York and Chancellor of England
2 CONT Eleanor Neville, 1438 - 1504, who married Thomas Stanley, 1st Earl of Derby
2 CONT Katherine Neville, 1442 - 25 March 1504, who married firstly William Bonville, 6th Baron of Harington and secondly William Hastings, 1st Baron Hastings. By her first husband, she was the mother of Cecily Bonville
2 CONT Thomas Neville, 1443 - 1460, who was knighted in 1449 and died at the Battle of Wakefield
2 CONT Margaret Neville, 1444 - 20 November 1506, who married John de Vere, 13th Earl of Oxford. (Bio and research by Audrey DeCamp Hoffman. In loving memory of Alice De Montague Neville, my 12th Great Grandmother.)
