2 CONT 3.         HENRI de Blois-Châtillon (-after 31 Jul 1400).  “Henry Despote de Romanie fils de defunct Charles Duc de Bretagne...” is named as present in the marriage contract dated 6 May 1384 between Louis, oldest son of Louis I Ki
2 CONC ng of Sicily [Anjou-Valois], and Luzia Visconti[540].  A decision dated 31 Jul 1400 relates to a dispute between “Henrico de Britannia” and “Ioannem de Britania comitem Penthuriæ dicti Henrici germanum prolatum”[541].  
2 CONT
