2 CONT Spalatin, Georg (1851). Historischer Nachlass und Briefe. p. 89.
2 CONT "Frederick the Wise". Devillier Donegan Enterprise. Retrieved 25 December 2013.
2 CONT "Frederick the Wise". October 26, 2014.
2 CONT Martin E. Marty, Martin Luther: A Life. (Penguin Lives) Paperback, 2008, p. 18
2 CONT Borkowsky, Ernst (1929). Das Leben Friedrichs des Weisen. Jena. pp. 56–57.
2 CONT Geoffrey Parker; Caleb Carr; et al. (2001). "Martin Luther Burns at the Stake, 1521". In Robert Cowley (ed.). The collected What if?: eminent historians imagining what might have been. New York: G. P. Putnam's Sons. p. 511. ISBN 0
2 CONC -399-15238-5.
2 CONT
2 CONT  This article incorporates text from a publication now in the public domain: Jackson, Samuel Macauley, ed. (1914). "Frederick III, The Wise". New Schaff–Herzog Encyclopedia of Religious Knowledge (third ed.). London and New York: 
2 CONC Funk and Wagnalls.
2 CONT
