2 CONT
2 CONT Amadeus II (c. 1046 – January 26, 1080) was Count of Savoy from 1060 to 1080, ruling jointly with Peter until 1078. He was the son of Otto of Savoy (Oddone in Italian).
2 CONT
2 CONT Documents about his life are rather scarce. His effective rule after Peter's death was only nominal, as the reins remained in his mother Adelaide's hands. The two visited Rome in 1073.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Joan (Giovanna in Italian) of Geneva and had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Humbert II of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Adelaide (d. 1090)
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Ausilia, married Umberto di Beaujeu
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Constance, married Otto II of Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Amadeo II, Count of Savoy, b. ca. 1032 in Geneva, Switzerland, d. 26 January 1080
2 CONT
2 CONT     Father: Eudes Savoy, b. ca. 1002 in Geneva, Switzerland, d. 19 January 1057/60
2 CONT
2 CONT     Mother: Adelais Suza, b. 1004 in Geneva, Switzerland
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Joan de Geneva
2 CONT
2 CONT     Married.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Humbert II, Count of Maurienne and Savoy, b. ca. 1062 in Savoy, France, m. Gisele (Gille) of Burgundy, 1090, d. 17 October 1103
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
