2 CONC ck II, Philip giving Frederick 20,000 "marcs" to defray the cost of his election (November, 1212). Thus was inaugurated the policy by which France meddled in the affairs of Germany and for the first time the French king claimed, l
2 CONC ike the pope, to have a voice in the imperial election. 
