2 CONT
2 CONT '''GIACOMO di Caretto''', son of ENRICO [II] Marchese di Caretto & his second wife Agatha --- (Finale 1220-before 21 Oct 1268).  Marchese di Savona.  "Petrus de Gorrena" wrote to "domino Jacobo marchioni de Saona" about the incarc
2 CONC eration of one of his vassals, by charter dated 20 Apr 1242[1229].  "Dominus Jacobus de Carreto marchio Saone" donated property to Santa Maria di Casanova by charter dated 8 Mar 1245[1230].  "Dominus Jacobus de Carreto marchio Sau
2 CONC one filius condam domini Henrici de Carreto marchionis" donated property to Staffarda monastery by charter dated 5 Dec 1246[1231].  Marchese di Noli e Finale.  Imperial Vicar of Northern Italy 1248, Marchese di Novello, Monchiero,
2 CONC  Lequio e Saliceto 1251.  A charter dated 18 Feb 1251 records an agreement of the commune of Genoa which refers to the damage caused by "Jacobum de Carreto"[1232].  The testament of "Bonefacius Montisferrati marchio", dated 12 Jun
2 CONC  1253, appoints "dominam Margaritam comitissam uxorem mea matrem ipsius Guilelmini et dominum comitem de Sabaldia et dominum Tomam de Sabaldia fratrem suum et Dalfinum de Vianesio et dominum Jacobum de Careto et dominum Georgium e
2 CONC t dominum Manuellem de Ceva et Bastardinum de Monteferrato" as guardians of his son[1233].  A charter dated 14 Nov 1256 records an agreement between the people of "Montisregalis" and "Jacobum de Carretto marchionum Savoæ"[1234]. 
