1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guy_Pallavicini
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Guy''' or '''Guido Pallavicini''', called '''Marchesopoulo''' by his Greek subjects,[1] was the first marquess of Bodonitsa in Frankish Greece from 1204 to his death in or shortly after 1237. He was one of the most important Fr
2 CONC ankish rulers in Greece, and played a major role in the short-lived Kingdom of Thessalonica: in 1208–1209 he supported the Lombard rebellion against King Demetrius of Montferrat, but by 1221 he was the kingdom's regent (bailli), a
2 CONC nd was left to defend the city against the ruler of Epirus, Theodore Komnenos Doukas. Left unsupported by the Latin Empire, and with a projected crusade to relieve the city delayed, he surrendered the city in December 1224. The be
2 CONC lated arrival of the crusade helped to save his own fief from falling to the Epirotes, however, and he was soon able to return there, dying on or shortly after 1237.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/LATIN%20LORDSHIPS%20IN%20GREECE.htm#GuidoPallavicinBoudonitza
2 CONT
2 CONT  Two brothers: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.    '''     GUIDO Pallavicini''' (-after 2 May 1237).  He was invested with the fief of Boudonitza and built the castle on his land[440].  Marchese of Boudonitza.  <br/>
2 CONT '''m''' SIBYLLE, daughter of ---.  Guido & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         UBERTINO Pallavicini (-after 1264).  Marchese of Boudonitza.  He joined the alliance against Guillaume de Villehardouin Prince of Achaia in 1257 to prevent the latter gaining control of the island of Eubœa[441]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *b)         MABILIA Pallavicini (-Feb 1264).  The Cronica Fratris Salimbene de Adam names "Mabilia [filia domnus Markesopolus Pellavicini]" & his wife "de Burgundia" as the wife of "domno Açoni marchioni Hestensi"[442].  The testa
2 CONC ment of "Azzo…Estensis et Anconitanus marchio", dated 13 Feb 1264, bequeathed property to "…dominæ Mambiliæ uxori nostræ…"[443].  She bequeathed property in Parma to her brother Ubertino by her will dated 1264[444].  '''m''' (1238
2 CONC ) as his second wife, AZZO [VII] Marchese d´Este, son of AZZO [VI] "Azzolino" d'Este Marchese di Ancona & his third wife Alix de Châtillon ([1205]-17 Feb 1264, bur Ferrara San Francesco). 
2 CONT
2 CONT *c)         ISABELLA Pallavicini (-1286).  She succeeded her brother as Marchesa of Boudonitza[445].  On her death without children, the succession was disputed by her husband and her cousin Tomaso, who settled the matter by seizi
2 CONC ng the castle[446]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         RUBINO Pallavicini . <br> '''m''' ---.  The name of Rubino´s wife is not known.  Rubino & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *a)         --- Pallavicini .  '''m''' ---.  One child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT **i)          TOMASO Pallavicini (-[1290/1300]).  He seized the castle of Boudonitza after the death of his cousin Isabella and established himself as Marchese of Boudonitza[447].  -         see below. 
