0 @N6000000003051316639@ NOTE [From Wikipedia.org]
1 CONT Thomas I (d. 1296) was the fourth margrave of Saluzzo from 1244 to his death. He succeeded his father Manfred III.
1 CONT
1 CONT Under the reign of Thomas, Saluzzo blossomed, achieving a greatness which had eluded his ancestors. He grafted a state whose borders remained unchanged for over two centuries. He extended the march to include Caramagnola. He was o
1 CONC ften at odds with Asti and he was a prime enemy of the Charles of Anjou and his Italian pretensions. During his tenure, he made Saluzzo a free city, giving it a podestà to govern in his name. He defended his castles and roccaforti
1 CONC  (strongholds) vigorously and built many new ones in the cities. He was succeeded by his son Manfred.
