1 CONT Manfred III of Saluzzo
1 CONT Manfred III (d. 1244) was the third marquess of Saluzzo, from 1215 to his death. He was the son of Boniface of Saluzzo and Maria di Torres of Sassari (in Sardinia). Since his father died in 1212, he succeeded his grandfather Manfr
1 CONC ed II as marquess on the latter's death in 1215. His paternal grandmother Azalaïs or Adelasia of Montferrat was regent during his minority until 1218. During that period, his grandmother paid tribute to Count Thomas I of Savoy.
1 CONT This article does not cite any references or sources.
1 CONT Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources. (help, get involved!)
1 CONT Unverifiable material may be challenged and removed.
1 CONT This article has been tagged since January 2007.
1 CONT Manfred fought the expansionistic policies of Thomas, as had his father, and he defended the borders of his march with care. He died in 1244 and was succeeded by his son Thomas.
1 CONT
