1 CONT Titles 8th Earl of Arundel
1 CONT EDMUND FITZ ALAN, Earlof Arundel, son and heir, born 1 May 1285, in the C
1 CONT astle of Marlborough. Hiswardship was obtained by John, Earl of Surrey a
1 CONT nd Sussex, whose granddaughter he married. He was knighted, with Edward, t
1 CONT he King's son, and many others, 22 May 1306. On 9 November 1306 he was sum
1 CONT moned to Parliament as Earl of Arundel, and took part in the Scottish wa
1 CONT rs of that year. On 25 February 1307/8 he officiated as Pincerna at the co
1 CONT ronation of Edward II. In 1316 he was Captain General north of the Tren
1 CONT t. For a long time he was in opposition to the King, and was violent again
1 CONT st Piers
1 CONT Gaveston, who had beaten him in a tournament. However in 1321 he changed
1 CONT sides, and married his first son to a daughter of Hugh le Despenser, bei
1 CONT ng
1 CONT thereafter one of the few nobles who adhered to the King. In 1323 he was
1 CONT Chief Justiciar of North and South Wales. Warden of the Welsh Marches 132
1 CONT 5. Having been captured in Shropshire by the Queen's party, he was, witho
1 CONT ut trial, beheaded at Hereford, 17 November 1326 in his 42nd year. He w
1 CONT as subsequently attainted, when his estates and honours became forfeite
1 CONT d. His widow [who, in her issue was, in 1347, sole heir of her brother Joh
1 CONT n, Earl of Surrey and Sussex, and consequently of the great family of Ware
1 CONT nne] was
1 CONT living 1330, but died before 23 May 1338. Source CP 1:241-2
