0 @N6000000002188569367@ NOTE Louis II of Naples
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis II of Anjou.
1 CONT Louis II of Anjou.
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis II of Anjou (1377–April 29, 1417), was the rival of Ladislas as King of Naples. He was a member of the House of Anjou.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Biography
1 CONT
1 CONT Born in Toulouse, Louis II was the son of Louis I of Anjou, King of Naples, and came into his Angevin inheritance, which included Provence, in 1384, with his rival Charles of Durazzo (father of Ladislas), of the senior Angevin lin
1 CONC e, in possession of Naples.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1386, the underage Ladislas was expelled soon after his father died. Louis II was crowned King of Naples by the Avignonese antipope Clement VII on November 1, 1389 and took possession of Naples the following year. He was ousted
1 CONC  in turn by his rival in 1399.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1409, Louis liberated Rome from Ladislas' occupation; in 1410, as an ally of the antipope John XXIII he attacked Ladislas and defeated him at Roccasecca (1411). Eventually Louis lost his Neapolitan support and had to retire. Hi
1 CONC s claim to Naples passed to his son, Louis III.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Yolande of Aragon (1384–1443) in Arles in 1400, giving him a possibility of inheriting the throne of Aragon through her right. Her father, King John I of Aragon had died in 1396, and her uncle king Martin I of Aragon di
1 CONC ed in 1410.
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis II died at his chateau of Angers, the heart of Anjou; he is buried there.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis and Yolande had five surviving children:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Louis III of Anjou, titular King of Naples, Duke of Anjou, etc.
1 CONT    2. René of Anjou, King of Naples, Duke of Anjou, etc.
1 CONT    3. Charles of Le Maine (1414–1472), Count of Maine
1 CONT    4. Marie of Anjou (1404 – 1463), married 1422, Bourges Charles VII of France
1 CONT    5. Yolande (1412, Arles – 1440), married 1431, Nantes Francis I, Duke of Brittany
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Monarchs of Naples and Sicily
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Louis I Duke of Anjou
1 CONT 1384–1417 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Louis III
1 CONT Count of Maine
1 CONT 1384–1417
1 CONT Count of Provence and Forcalquier
1 CONT 1384–1417
1 CONT Count of Piedmont
1 CONT 1384–1417
1 CONT Titular King of Naples
1 CONT 1384–1389, 1399–1417
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Ladislas King of Naples
1 CONT 1389–1399 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Ladislas
