0 @N6000000004303404764@ NOTE WIKIPEDIA:
1 CONT
1 CONT Amadeus IV of Savoy
1 CONT
1 CONT Amadeus IV (1197 – June 24 or July 13 1253) was Count of Savoy from 1233 to 1253.
1 CONT The legitimate heir of Thomas I of Savoy and Marguerite of Geneva, he had however to fight with his brothers for the inheritance of Savoy lands after their father's death. His brothers Pietro and Aimone spurred a revolt in Aosta V
1 CONC alley against Amadeus, but he was able to crush it with the help of Manfred III of Saluzzo and Boniface II of Montferrat, who were his sons-in-law. Together with his brother Thomas, he fought against the communes of Turin and Pine
1 CONC rolo, but with uncertain results.
1 CONT He was succeeded by his young son Boniface, who died soon.
1 CONT
1 CONT Family and children
1 CONT He married twice:
1 CONT 1.	Anne of Burgundy, daughter of Hugh III, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT 1.	Beatrice of Savoy (d. 1258), married firstly in 1233 Manfred, Margrave of Saluzzo (d. 1244), married secondly on April 21, 1247 Manfred of Sicily
1 CONT 2.	Margaret of Savoy (d. 1254), married firstly on December 9, 1235 Boniface II of Montferrat, married secondly Aymar III, Count of Valentinois
1 CONT 1.	Cecilia of Baux, "Passerose", daughter of Barral of Baux
1 CONT 1.	Boniface of Savoy
1 CONT 2.	Beatrice of Savoy (1250 – February 23, 1292) married Peter of Chalon and Juan Manuel of Castile.
1 CONT 3.	Eleonor of Savoy, married in 1269 Guichard de Beaujeu
1 CONT 4.	Constance of Savoy, died after 1263
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by Thomas I
1 CONT Count of Savoy 1233–1253
1 CONT Succeeded by Boniface and Thomas II
1 CONT Children
1 CONT 1.	 Beatrice de Savoy b: ABT 1215 in Savoy, France
1 CONT 2.	 Marguerite de Savoy b: ABT 1215 in Savoy, France
0 @N6000000002187829676@ NOTE Amadeus IV of Savoy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Amadeus IV (1197–1253) was Count of Savoy 1233–1253. He married twice:
1 CONT
1 CONT Anne of Burgundy 
1 CONT Beatrice of Savoy (d. 1258), married firstly in 1233 Manfred, Margrave of Saluzzo (d. 1244), married secondly on April 21, 1247 Manfred of Sicily 
1 CONT Margaret of Savoy (d. 1254), married firstly on December 9, 1235 Boniface II of Montferrat, married secondly Aymar III, Count of Valentinois 
1 CONT Cecilia of Baux, "Passerose", daughter of Barral of Baux 
1 CONT Boniface of Savoy 
1 CONT Beatrice of Savoy (1250 – February 23, 1292) married Peter of Chalon and Juan Manuel of Castile. 
1 CONT Eleonor of Savoy, married in 1269 Guichard de Beaujeu 
1 CONT Constance of Savoy, died after 1263 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Thomas I Count of Savoy
1 CONT 1233–1253
1 CONT  Succeeded by:
1 CONT Boniface 
0 @N6000000001220382466@ NOTE [2753682.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT !Second Earl of Lincoln.  He is called the second Earl, although the title was never attribut ed to him in any charter, by reason that he died before his mother, through whom the dignit y came.  Dugdale states that he married, in 
1 CONC 1247, "an outlandish lady from the parts of Savoy , brought over purposely for him by Peter de Savoy, uncle to the queen, which occasioned muc h discontent amongst the nobles of England." This lady was Alice, daughter of the Marqu
1 CONC ess o f Saluces, in Italy, and a cousin of the queen. [Magna Charta Barons, p. 102-3]
