1 CONT ch, Bishop of Chichester, b. 1197-d. 1253] relates to a young son of the C
1 CONT ountess of Arundel--a daughter of one of the De Warennes--who lay very i
1 CONT ll in Lewes Castle. At last all appeared to be over and the body was le
1 CONT ft unattended; but later a girl named Johanna entered, and knelt and pray
1 CONT ed to St. Richard de Wych for the soul of the boy, who immediately gave si
1 CONT gns of life and ultimately recovered.
