0 @N6000000001876707031@ NOTE <!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN"
1 CONT           "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd">
1 CONT <html  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xml:lang="en" lang="en"><head>
1 CONT <title></title>
1 CONT <meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/>
1 CONT <meta http-equiv="Content-Style-Type" content="text/css"/>
1 CONT </head>
1 CONT <body>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt"><b><i>Source</i></b></span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt"><i>http://awt.ancestry.com/cgi- 
1 CONT bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&amp;db=michelotti&amp;id=I014298&amp;ti=4317</i></span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT ID: I014298 </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Name: Richard de Arundel <span style="font-size:12pt"><i>See Notes 1 2 3</i> </span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Sex: M </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Birth: ABT 1313 in Arundel, Sussex, England</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Death: 24 JAN 1375/76 in Arundel, Sussex, England </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Burial: Lewes Priory, Sussex, England </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Note: </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">EARLDOM OF SURREY</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">IX.9.</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">EARLDOM OF ARUNDEL</div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT XIV.10 or 3. RICHARD FITZ ALAN, called &quot;Copped Hat&quot; </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">&#160; son and heir of Edmund [12th Earl of Arundel], born about 1313. </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">In 1330-31 he was fully restored in blood and honours and in </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">December of that year 1330-1331 obtained restitution of the Castle and </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Honour of Arundel from the </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">widow of John, Earl of Kent, becoming Earl of Arundel; he took a distinguished part 
1 CONT in the wars with France; </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Admiral of the West 1340-41 and 1347-47; </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">commanded the second division at the Battle of Cr&#233;cy, </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">and was at the fall of Calais in 1347; </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">on June 30, 1347 he succeeded to the vast estates of the family of Warenne, </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">by the death, s.p.legit of his mother's brother, John, Earl of Surrey and Sussex. </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">By fine levied 1349-50, he settled the Castle, town, and manor of Arundel on himself 
1 CONT and his [then] wife Eleanor, for their joint lives, with remainder to the heirs male of 
1 CONT his body by his said wife. </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">On the death of Joan, the widow of his said uncle, John, Earl of Surrey, in 1361, but 
1 CONT not before, he assumed the title of Earl of Surrey, </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">and in 1366 settled the Warenne estates on his issue. </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT He married, 1stly, 9 February 1320/1, in the King's Chapel at Havering-atte-Bower 
1 CONT [he about 7, she about 8], Isabel, daughter of Sir Hugh le Despenser the younger, 
1 CONT [Lord le Despenser], by Eleanor, daughter and co-heir of Gilbert [de Clare], Earl of 
1 CONT Gloucester. </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Obtained 4 December 1344, a Papal mandate for the annulment of his marriage to 
1 CONT Isabel le Despenser, on the ground of his minority and of his never willingly 
1 CONT consented to the match. </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT He married 2ndly, 5 February 1344/5, at Ditton, [a lady with whom he had previously 
1 CONT cohabited],<span style="font-size:12pt"><b> Eleanor </b><b><i>(a Plantagenet)</i></b>, widow of John de Beaumont [2nd Lord 
1 CONT Beaumont], daughter of henry, Earl of lancaster, by Maud, daughter and heir of Sir 
1 CONT Patrick de Chawices or Chaworth. She, who was 1st cousin to his 1st wife, and 2nd 
1 CONT cousin once removed to the Earl, died 11 January 1372, at Arundel, and was buried 
1 CONT at Lewes. He died 24 January 1375/6, also at Arundel, in his 70th year, and was 
1 CONT also buried at Lewes. Source CP 1:243</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT Father:Edmund FitzAlan de Arundel b: 1 MAY 1285 in Marlborough Castle. WIL, 
1 CONT ENG </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Mother:Alice de Warenne b: BET 1285 AND 1287 in of Arundel,SSX, ENG&#009;</div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT Marriage1 Mistress </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Marriage Beginning Status: Friends Children </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Eleanor FitzAlan</div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT Marriage2 Isabel le Despenser b: ABT 1312 </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Married: 9 FEB 1320/21 in King's Chapel, Havering-atte-Bower, ESS, ENG </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Event: Annulled 4 DEC 1344 </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Note: Divorced 1345 </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Children<span style="font-size:12pt">:</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Edmund de Arundel b: ABT 1327</div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT Marriage<span style="font-size:12pt"> 3 </span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Eleanor<span style="font-size:12pt"> <i>(Plantagenet) </i>of Lancaster b: ABT 1311 in Grismond Castle, 
1 CONT Monmouthshire, Wales </span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Married: 5 FEB 1344/45 in Ditton, ENG </div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Children<span style="font-size:12pt">: </span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Joan de Arundel</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">John de Arundel b: in Maltravers</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Thomas de Arundel b: ABT 1352</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Richard de Arundel b: ABT 1346</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Alice de Arundel b: 1352 in Arundel Castle, SSX, ENG</div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt"><b><i>Notes from Sources:</i></b></span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><span style="font-size:12pt">1) Title: The Complete Peerage</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Book</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Page: 1:243, 7:4, 156, 417, 11:394, 566, 12[1]:44, 344, 434, 617, [2]:287, 548, 
1 CONT 663, 899 </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT <span style="font-size:12pt">2) Title: Plantagenet Ancestry, Douglas Richardson, 2004</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Page: 317 </div>
1 CONT <div align="left"><br />
1 CONT <span style="font-size:12pt">3) Title: Magna Carta Ancestry, Douglas Richardson, 2005</span></div>
1 CONT <div align="left">Page: 334</div>
1 CONT <div align="left">~~~~~~</div>
1 CONT </body>
1 CONT </html>
