0 @N6000000002322286584@ NOTE He led his country in a miraculous recovery from the Hundred Years' War,
1 CONT reversing the the disastrous Anglo-French settlement of 1360. In his court,
1 CONT Charles, an intellectual and religious man, surrounded himself with luxury
1 CONT and men of educated tastes. Besides reorganizing the army, creating a new
1 CONT navy, instituting tax changes, and bringing Flanders, Spain and Portugal into
1 CONT French alliances, he was also concerned with redecorating the Louvre to house
1 CONT a mangificient library and with finishing the castle of Vincennes.
