1 CONT
1 CONT Charles V (21 January 1338 – 16 September 1380), called the Wise, was King of France from 1364 to his death and a member of the House of Valois. His reign marked a high point for France during the Hundred Years' War, with his armi
1 CONC es recovering much of the territory ceded to England at the Treaty of Brétigny.
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 Early life
1 CONT     * 2 The Regency and the uprising of the Third Estate
1 CONT     * 3 The Treaty of Bretigny
1 CONT     * 4 King of France
1 CONT     * 5 Le Sage
1 CONT     * 6 The war resumes
1 CONT     * 7 Papal Schism
1 CONT     * 8 Death
1 CONT     * 9 Legacy
1 CONT     * 10 Ancestors
