0 @N6000000002187840112@ NOTE John, Duke of Berry
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT John of Valois, the Magnificent, (November 30, 1340 – March 15, 1416) was Duke of Berry and Auvergne and Count of Poitiers and Montpensier. He was the third son of King John II of France and Bonne of Luxemburg; amongst his sibling
1 CONC s were Charles V, King of France, Louis I, King of Naples and Philip II, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the middle of the Hundred Years' War and serious internal conflicts, John was a consensual figure in France. He acted several times as a peace maker between French factions and is notable by his attempts of peace between his ne
1 CONC phews Louis of Valois, Duke of Orléans and John, Duke of Burgundy.
1 CONT
