0 @N6000000002188108552@ NOTE Philippa of Lancaster
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT  Philippa of Lancaster, Queen of Portugal, princess of EnglandPhilippa of Lancaster, LG (1359 – July 19, 1415) was an English princess, daughter of John of Gaunt, 1st Duke of Lancaster (a son of Edward III of England and Philippa 
1 CONC of Hainault) by his wife and cousin Blanche of Lancaster. Blanche was the daughter of Henry of Grosmont, 1st Duke of Lancaster and Isabel de Beaumont.
1 CONT
1 CONT Philippa became Queen consort of Portugal by her marriage with king John I, celebrated in 1387 in the city of Porto. This marriage was the final step in the Portuguese-English alliance, against the France-Castile axis. Philippa is
1 CONC  remembered for being a generous and loving queen, and by being the mother of the "Illustrious Generation" (in Portuguese, Ínclita Geração) of princes, whose members were:
1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche (1388-1389), named after her grandmother, who died as an infant; 
1 CONT Afonso (1390-1400), named after several Kings of Portugal, including his great-grandfather Afonso IV, who died at the age of 10; 
1 CONT Edward (1391-1438), named after his great-grandfather Edward III, a writer and an intellectual, who succeeded his father; 
1 CONT Peter (1392-1449), named after his grandfather Peter I of Portugal, First Duke of Coimbra, remarkable ruler and a traveled man, who served as Regent during the minority of his nephew Afonso V; 
1 CONT Henry the Navigator (1394-1460), First Duke of Viseu, who guided Portugal to the Great era of The Discoveries; 
1 CONT English Royalty 
1 CONT House of Plantagenet 
1 CONT
1 CONT Edward III 
1 CONT Children 
1 CONT    Edward, Prince of Wales 
1 CONT    Lionel, Duke of Clarence 
1 CONT    John, Duke of Lancaster 
1 CONT    Edmund, Duke of York 
1 CONT    Thomas, Duke of Gloucester 
1 CONT    Joan of England 
1 CONT    Isabella, Countess of Bedford 
1 CONT Grandchildren 
1 CONT     Richard II 
1 CONT     Philippa, Countess of Ulster 
1 CONT     Philippa, Queen of Portugal 
1 CONT     Elizabeth, Baroness Fanhope and Milbroke 
1 CONT     Henry IV 
1 CONT     Catherine, Queen of Castile 
1 CONT     Edward, Duke of York 
1 CONT     Richard, Earl of Cambridge 
1 CONT     Constance of York 
1 CONT     Anne, Countess of Eu 
1 CONT Isabella (1397-1472), who married Philip III of Burgundy and was one of the most powerful and admired women in Europe; 
1 CONT Blanche (1398), also died in childhood; 
1 CONT John (1400-1442), Duke of Aveiro, a very respected noble and the grandfather of the two greatest Iberian monarchs in the 16th century, Manuel I of Portugal and Isabella I of Castile; 
1 CONT Ferdinand (1402-1433) "the Saint Prince," a warrior, who was captured during the Disaster of Tangier and died prisoner of the Moors. 
1 CONT Philippa died of plague in 1415, a few days before the expedition to Ceuta.
