1 CONT [edit] Cultural References
1 CONT
1 CONT The novel The Notebooks of Malte Laurids Brigge by Rainer Maria Rilke describes the old age of Charles VI at length.
1 CONT
1 CONT The story "Hop-Frog, or The Eight Chained Ourang-Outangs" by Edgar Allan Poe involves a scene strikingly similar to the Bal des Ardents. (Full text at Wikisource)
1 CONT
1 CONT The Edith Pattou novel East mentions Charles of France to be the white bear.
1 CONT
1 CONT King Charles VI, and his madness, are mentioned at length in the historical novel Het Woud der Verwachting/Le Foret de Longue Attente/In a Dark Wood Wandering (1949) by Hella S. Haasse.
1 CONT
