0 @N6000000000437147119@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Duke Name Suffix:<NSFX> IV, Of Burgundy
0 @N6000000002187840303@ NOTE Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh IV of Burgundy (March 9, 1213 – October 27, 1271) was duke of Burgundy between 1218 and 1271. Hugh was the only son of duke Eudes III and Alice (or Alix) of Vergy. He was married twice, first to Yolande of Dreux, then to Beat
1 CONC rice of Champagne, princess of Navarre, and had the following issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT From Yolande of Dreux, daughter of Count Robert III "Gasteblé" of Dreux and of Braine: 
1 CONT Margaret, Lady of Molinot (1229–1277), married William, count of Mont St Jean 
1 CONT Eudes, count of Nevers and Auxerre (1230–1236) 
1 CONT John (1231–1268), married Agnes of Dampierre and had Beatrice of Burgundy, heiress of Bourbon (through Agnes) 
1 CONT Alice (1233–1273), married Henry III, Duke of Brabant 
1 CONT Robert II, Duke of Burgundy (1248–1306) 
1 CONT From Beatrice of Champagne, daughter of Theobald IV of Champagne: 
1 CONT Hugh, viscount of Avallon (1260–1288) 
1 CONT Beatrice, Lady of Grignon (ca.1260–1329), married Hugh XIII, count of La Marche 
1 CONT Isabelle, Lady of Vieux-Château (1270–1323), married Rudolph I, Holy Roman Emperor 
1 CONT In 1239, Hugh joined the Crusade organized by Emperor Frederick II and king Theobald I of Navarre. The Burgundian troops allied with Richard of Cornwall, who took Ascalon and negotiated a peace with Egypt in 1241. Hugh also claime
1 CONC d the Kingdom of Thessalonica, although it had been recaptured by the Byzantines some years before.
1 CONT
1 CONT Under the rule of Hugh IV, the duchy of Burgundy expanded to include the counties of Chalon and Auxonne.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT Dukes of Burgundy family tree 
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Eudes III Duke of Burgundy
1 CONT 1218–1271 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Robert II 
0 @N6000000005076731366@ NOTE Duc de Bourgogne
0 @N6000000009304951404@ NOTE #Générale#Il succéda à son père en 1218 à l'âge de 6 ans & confirma les privilèges de communes de Beaune & de Dijon en 1228. Il acquit le comté de Chalon & Aussone de Jean, comte de Bourgogne, par un échange qu'ils firent ensemble
1 CONC  en 1237. Il accompagna le roi St Louis au premier voyage d'outremer en 1248. Depuis, il fit le pélerinage de St Jacques en Galicie, où le roi de Castille, qui se qualifiait de roi des romains, lui donna en fief pour lui & ses suc
1 CONC cesseurs une rente de dix mille maravedis, & le duc lui promit de l'assister, pour se maintenir dans l'empire auquel il avait été élu. L'acte est daté de Ségovie, le 21 Septembre 1258. Etant à Paris au mois de janvier 1265, il fit
1 CONC  un traité avec Baudouin de Courtenay II, du nom, empereur de Constantinople, qui lui fit don, et à ses héritiers, du royaume de Thessalonique & de plusieurs autres seigneuries. Il fit son testament le 26 Septembre 1272, confirma 
1 CONC au mois d'Octobre suivant, les privilèges de la ville de Dijon, émancipa son fils Robert le 22 du même mois, en lui cédant son duché, dont il se retint l'usufruit. Il mourut la même année au mois de Février, que l'on comptait enco
1 CONC re 1272.
0 @N6000000005076728763@ NOTE Hugues de Bourgogne was born before 1273. He was the son of Hugues IV de Bourgogne, Duc de Bourgogne.1 He married Marguerite de Bourgogne, daughter of Jean I de Bourgogne, Comte de Bourgogne, in 1284.1 He died in 1294.1
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 74. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
0 @N6000000002322312510@ NOTE Daughter of Hugh IV duke of Burgundy. When Rudolf I married Isabella, he
1 CONT combated the expansionist policy of France on his western frontier, and,
1 CONT coupled by Rudolf's compelling Otto IV, Count of Palantine, to pay homage
1 CONT (1289), the powerful Catholic French influence at the papal court prevented
1 CONT Rudolf from ever being crowned Holy Roman Emperor by the pope. As well,
1 CONT Rudolf was unsuccessful in securing the election of his son, Albert, as
1 CONT German king of as King of the Romans.
0 @N6000000002240801510@ NOTE Daughter of Hugh IV duke of Burgundy. When Rudolf I married Isabella, he
1 CONT combated the expansionist policy of France on his western frontier, and,
1 CONT coupled by Rudolf's compelling Otto IV, Count of Palantine, to pay homage
1 CONT (1289), the powerful Catholic French influence at the papal court prevented
1 CONT Rudolf from ever being crowned Holy Roman Emperor by the pope. As well,
1 CONT Rudolf was unsuccessful in securing the election of his son, Albert, as
1 CONT German king of as King of the Romans.
