0 @N6000000002322303354@ NOTE She was named for her great-aunt St. Elizabeth of Hungary and received a
1 CONT strict and pious education. Her husband was a good ruler but an unfaithful
1 CONT husband. Despite of any corrupt court life, she was able to maintain her
1 CONT devout habits, help the sick and the poor, and found charitable
1 CONT establishments. When her son rebelled, she was able to ride between the two
1 CONT armies and reconcile father and son.  She died later on her way to the
1 CONT battlefield to make peace between her son and the king of Castile in 1336.
