0 @N6000000003615871684@ NOTE The strangest case of annulment and resultant illegitimacy that I kn 
1 CONT ow of isthat of Richard FitzAlan, 9th Earl of Arundel and his first wi
1 CONT fe Isabel le Despenser. They were married as children and had at least t
1 CONT wo kids: Edmund FitzAlan and Isabel FitzAlan; however at a later date, Ric
1 CONT hard FitzAlan decided that he would much rather be married to Eleanor, t
1 CONT he daughter of the Earl of Lancaster, so he claimed that he was too you
1 CONT ng to actually consent to the marriage and that for that reason the marria
1 CONT ge was annulled. The pope apparentlyagreed with the reason and the marria
1 CONT ge was annulled and Edmund and Isabel FitzAlan were declared illegitima
1 CONT te and the 10th Earl of Arundel was the eldest son from the second marriag
