0 @N6000000003615871619@ NOTE 11th Earl Arundel 
1 CONT Cause of Death:Beheaded
1 CONT RICHARD FITZ ALAN, Earl of Arundel, and Earl of Surrey, son and heir, by 2
1 CONT nd wife, born in 1346. He was bearer of the Crown at the coronation of Ric
1 CONT hard II, 16 July 1377, was a member of the Council, and was made Admir
1 CONT al of the West and South, 1377, and subsequently, 1386, of all England. K.
1 CONT G., distinguished himself in the French Wars, and "won a brilliant naval v
1 CONT ictory over the French, Spanish, & Flemish fleets offMargate in 24 Mar
1 CONT ch 1387"; and was made Governor of Brest in 1388, being oneof the five Lo
1 CONT rds Appellant in  the Parliament of that year.
1 CONT Together withthe Duke of Gloucester he later took an active part in the o
1 CONT pposition to King Richard, who, in 1388, was entirely in that Duke's powe
1 CONT r. In 1394 he obtained a pardon for all political offences, but was treach
1 CONT erously seized, 12 July1397, tried at Westminster, and beheaded at Cheaps
1 CONT ide on 21 September 1397.
1 CONT He married [contract dated 28 September, Papal dispensation, the same mont
1 CONT h, 1359] Elizabeth, daughter of William [Bohun], Earl of Northampton, by E
1 CONT lizabeth, daughter of Bartholomew Badlesmere. She died 3 April 1385, and w
1 CONT as buried at Lewes.
1 CONT He married 2ndly [without Royal license, for which he was fined 500 marks
1 CONT ], 15 August 1390, Philippe, widow of John Hastings, and daughter ofEdmu
1 CONT nd [Mortimer], Earl of March, by Philippe, daughter and heir of Lionel, Du
1 CONT ke of Clarence.
1 CONT He was buried at Austin Friars', in Bread Street, London,and, having be
1 CONT en attainted, all his honors were forfeited. His widow [by whom he h
1 CONT ad no issue] was born 21 November 1375, at Ludlow, married 3rdly, afterAp
1 CONT ril 1398, Thomas [Poynings], Lord St. John of Basing, and died 24 Septemb
1 CONT er 1401, at Halnaker, Sussex, being buried at Boxgrove.
