0 @N6000000002322286438@ NOTE In France, Louis was highly popular. From the time of the assembly at Tours
1 CONT (1506) he was known as "the Father of the People". He simplified and improved
1 CONT the administration of justice, sought to protect his lowest subjects against
1 CONT oppression, and financed his wars without increase in direct taxation, until
1 CONT 1509. He kept his kingdom free from civil war and, until the end of his
1 CONT reign, from invasion. Popular, yet he was noted for his disastrous Italian
1 CONT wars and an invasion at several points by a Holy League of England, etc.
