1 CONT
1 CONT Blanche of Lancaster, Countess of Derby was born on 25 March 1345.2 She was the daughter of Henry Grosmont of Derby Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Lancaster and Isabella de Beaumont.1 She married John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster, son of
1 CONC  Edward III, King of England and Philippe de Hainaut, on 13 May 1359 at Reading Abbey, Reading, Berkshire, England. She died on 12 September 1369 at age 24 at Bolingbroke Castle, Lincolnshire, England, from the bubonic plague.2 Sh
1 CONC e was buried at Old St. Paul's Cathedral, London, England.2
1 CONT      Blanche of Lancaster, Countess of Derby gained the title of Countess of Derby.
