0 @N6000000002188021900@ NOTE Catherine of Lancaster
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Katherine of Lancaster (also known as Catherine Plantagenet and as Queen Catalina of Castile and Leon) (1372/1373 – 2 June 1418) was the daughter of John of Gaunt, 1st Duke of Lancaster, and his second wife, Constance of Castile.
1 CONT
1 CONT She married Enrique III of Castile in 1393 at Burgos. As her mother was daughter of Pedro of Castile, the marriage helped to restore a semblance of legitimacy to the Trastamara line.
1 CONT
1 CONT The couple had three children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Maria of Castile (1401-1458), who married Alfonso V "the Magnanimous", King of Aragon and Naples, 
1 CONT Catharina of Castile, who wed Enrique of Aragón, Duque de Villena, 
1 CONT Juan II (1405-1454), who succeeded his father as King of Castile . His mother Katherine and his uncle, Ferdinand, served as co-regents during his minority, and Katherine alone was regent after Ferdinand's death in 1416. 
1 CONT Queen Catalina died at Valladolid of a stroke, possibly precipitated by her great obesity, leaving her thirteen year-old son at the mercy of self-interested courtiers.
0 @N6000000002176681748@ NOTE Daughter of John of Gaunt of England, but cannot trace her to any of John of
