0 @N6000000005076966933@ NOTE http://humphrysfamilytree.com/Royal/john.gaunt.html
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT John of Gaunt (see here and here), Duke of Lancaster,
1 CONT born Mar 1340,
1 CONT mar 1stly, 1359 to Blanche Plantagenet [descendant of Aoife Mac Murrough] and had issue:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1.   Philippa Plantagenet, mar John I, King of Portugal and had issue.
1 CONT 2.   Elizabeth Plantagenet, mar John Holland, 1st Duke of Exeter and had issue.
1 CONT 3.   Henry IV, born 1366, succeeded 13th Oct 1399 (House of Lancaster).
1 CONT
1 CONT through his wife inherited Kenilworth Castle, Warwickshire (later held by Robert Dudley),
1 CONT he was the effective ruler late Edward III - early Richard II,
1 CONT appears in Richard II by Shakespeare,
1 CONT the TV movie Richard II (1978) has John Gielgud as John of Gaunt,
1 CONT patron of John Wycliffe, the "Morning Star of the Reformation", who produced the first English translation of the Bible 1382,
1 CONT mar 3rdly, 1396, to his long-time mistress Catherine Roet [born 1350], by whom he had already had illegitimate issue,
1 CONT his children by Catherine Roet were legitimated by statute 1397 "for all purposes save succession to the crown" (i.e. this line is not in the Royal line of succession, but of course we have other Royal Descents),
1 CONT he died 3rd Feb 1399, age 58 yrs, bur St.Paul's Cathedral, London,
1 CONT see biography,
1 CONT never king himself, but within months of his death his son became king,
1 CONT Catherine died 10th May 1403, Lincoln, age 53 yrs, bur Lincoln Cathedral,
1 CONT he had issue by Catherine Roet:
1 CONT
1 CONT 1.   John de Beaufort, 1st Earl of Somerset, born 1373,
1 CONT mar Margaret Holland [descendant of Edward I and of Aoife Mac Murrough] and had issue:
1 CONT 1.   John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset, had issue:
1 CONT 1.   Margaret Beaufort (see here), mar Edmund Tudor, Earl of Richmond and had issue (House of Tudor).
1 CONT 2.   Thomasine Beaufort, mar Reginald de Grey, 7th Baron Grey de Wilton and had issue.
1 CONT 2.   Edmund Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset (second creation), mar Eleanor Beauchamp [descendant of Edward I] and had issue:
1 CONT 1.   Henry Beaufort, 2nd Duke of Somerset, associated with Joan Hill and had illegitimate issue:
1 CONT 1.   Charles Somerset, 1st Earl of Worcester.
1 CONT 2.   Margaret Beaufort, mar Humphrey Stafford, Earl of Stafford and had issue.
1 CONT 3.   Joan Beaufort,
1 CONT mar 1stly to James I, King of Scotland and had issue,
1 CONT mar 2ndly to Sir James Stewart and had issue.
1 CONT
1 CONT 2.   Joan de Beaufort (see here),
1 CONT born c.1379, Beaufort Castle, Anjou,
1 CONT mar 2ndly, 1396, to Ralph Neville, 1st Earl of Westmoreland and had issue.
