0 @N6000000001563284692@ NOTE Being a fierce opponent to the Roman Catholic Pope, he opened the last medieval battle between emperorship and popehood.  Despite being excommunicated by Pope John XXII,  he became Roman Emperor of the German Reich in 1328.
1 CONT
1 CONT He set out to aggrandize his branch of the family.  He invested his eldest son with the Margravate of Brandenburg when the Ascanian house became extinct.  He saw to it that the sons by his 2nd marriage (to Margaret of Holland) suc
1 CONC ceeded to the country of Holland.  However, when Ludwig died his sons began a process of dividing Bavaria into individual fiefs. This continued until it was pretty much reunited in 1506.
0 @N6000000001578926464@ NOTE Being a fierce opponent to the Roman Catholic Pope, he opened the last medieval battle between emperorship and popehood.  Despite being excommunicated by Pope John XXII,  he became Roman Emperor of the German Reich in 1328.
1 CONT
1 CONT He set out to aggrandize his branch of the family.  He invested his eldest son with the Margravate of Brandenburg when the Ascanian house became extinct.  He saw to it that the sons by his 2nd marriage (to Margaret of Holland) suc
1 CONC ceeded to the country of Holland.  However, when Ludwig died his sons began a process of dividing Bavaria into individual fiefs. This continued until it was pretty much reunited in 1506.
0 @N6000000002322312632@ NOTE Duke of Upper Bavaria from 1294 and united Bavaria 1340-1347, first of the
1 CONT Wittlesbach line of German Emperors, his reign was marked by incessant
1 CONT diplomatic and military struggles to defend the right of the empire to elect
1 CONT an emperor independently of the papacy, to consolidate his own position, and
1 CONT to improve the status of his family. Louis finally managed to force John of
1 CONT Bohemia to nenounce all claims to Italy and to acknowledge Louis emperor in
1 CONT 1339. See message with third wife, Margaret.
0 @N6000000002187825509@ NOTE Louis IV, Holy Roman Emperor
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis IV, Holy Roman Emperor.Louis IV of Bavaria of the House of Wittelsbach (born 1282) was duke of Bavaria from 1294/1301 together with his brother Rudolf I, also count of the Palatinate until 1329 and, German king since 1314 an
1 CONC d crowned as Holy Roman Emperor in 1328. Louis died on October 11, 1347 when he suffered a stroke during a bear-hunt in Puch near Fürstenfeldbruck. He is buried in the Frauenkirche in Munich.
1 CONT
1 CONT Louis was the son of Louis II, Duke of Upper Bavaria, and Mechthild, a daughter of King Rudolph I.
