0 @N6000000002188378247@ NOTE Ernest, Elector of Saxony
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Ernst, Elector of Saxony (b. Meissen, 24 March 1441 - d. Colditz, 26 August 1486) was Elector of Saxony from 1464 to 1486.
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 Biography
1 CONT     * 2 Ancestry
1 CONT     * 3 Children
1 CONT     * 4 See also
1 CONT     * 5 References
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Biography
1 CONT
1 CONT Ernst was founder of the Ernestine line of Saxon princes, ancestor of George I of Great Britain, Prince Albert of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha, as well as his wife and cousin Queen Victoria of the United Kingdom, and their cousins Leopol
1 CONC d II of Belgium and Empress Carlota of Mexico.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was the second son (but fourth in order of birth) of the eight children of Frederick II, Elector of Saxony and Margarete of Austria, sister of Frederick III, Holy Roman Emperor.
1 CONT
1 CONT The death of his older brother Frederick (1451) made him the new heir apparent to the position of Elector of Saxony.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1455 Ernst was kidnapped along with his brother Albert, an episode famous in German history as the "Prinzenraub" (i. e. The Stealing of the Princes).
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1464, he succeeded his father as Elector of Saxony, and annexed Thuringia in 1482, and three years later (Treaty of Leipzig, 1485) shared his territory with his brother Albert, until he arranged the division of the common posse
1 CONC ssion.
1 CONT
1 CONT In the Division of Leipzig he received area around Wittenberg, the south Thuringian part, the Vogtland and parts of the Pleissnerland. As residence he selected Wittenberg. He provided for the welfare of the country and introduced 
1 CONC the constitution.
1 CONT
1 CONT One year after the division elector Ernest died in Colditz, at the age of 46 years, the consequence of a fall off a horse.
1 CONT
