1 CONT
1 CONT Henry VI (6 December 1421 – 21 May 1471) was King of England 1422–1461 (though with a Regent until 1437) and then 1470–1471, and a claimant to the kingdom of France 1422–1453.
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 Child King
1 CONT     * 2 Henry's marriage to Margaret of Anjou
1 CONT     * 3 Increasing unpopularity and insanity
1 CONT     * 4 Wars of the Roses
1 CONT     * 5 Death and legacy
1 CONT     * 6 Henry's character
1 CONT     * 7 Ancestry
