1 CONT [edit] Popular culture
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Legend and literature
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Miracles were attributed to the king, and he was informally regarded as a saint. Hymns to him still exist.
1 CONT     * In 1590, William Shakespeare wrote a trilogy of plays about the life of Henry VI: Henry VI, part 1, Henry VI, part 2, and Henry VI, part 3. Henry also appears as a ghost in Richard III.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Film and television
1 CONT
1 CONT Henry has been played on film and television by:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * James Berry in the silent short Richard III (1911), dramatising a part of Shakespeare's play
1 CONT     * Miles Mander in Tower of London (1939), a horror film loosely dramatising the rise to power of Richard III
1 CONT     * Terry Scully in in the BBC series An Age of Kings (1960), which contained all the history plays from Richard II to Richard III
1 CONT     * Carl Wery in the West German TV version of Shakespeare's play König Richard III (1964)
1 CONT     * David Warner in War of the Roses (1965), which was a filmed version of the Royal Shakespeare Company performing all three parts of Henry VI and Richard III, and in the BBC series The Wars of the Roses (1989), which included 
1 CONC all of Shakespeare's history plays performed by the English Shakespeare Company; Peggy Ashcroft also played his queen, Margaret of Anjou, in both series
1 CONT     * Peter Benson in the BBC Shakespeare versions of all three parts of Henry VI and Richard III (1983)
1 CONT     * Edward Jewesbury in Richard III (1995), with Ian McKellen as Richard
1 CONT     * James Dalesandro in Richard III (2007), a modern day version
1 CONT
