1 CONT Sir Edmund Tudor, 1st Earl of Richmond was the son of Sir Owen Tudor <p10200.htm> and Catherine de France <p10187.htm>. He was born circa 1430 at Much Hadham Palace, Hertfordshire, England.1 He married Margaret Beaufort, daughter 
1 CONC of Sir John Beaufort, 1st Duke of Somerset <p10198.htm> and Margaret Beauchamp <p10198.htm>, on 1 November 1455 at Bletsoe Castle, Bedfordshire, England.1 He died on 3 November 1456 at Carmarthen Castle, Carmarthenshire, Wales.2,3
1 CONC  He was buried at St. David's Cathedral, St. David's, Pembrokeshire, Wales.1 He was buried at Church of the Greyfriars, Carmarthen, Carmarthenshire, Wales.1  He was invested as a knight on 15 December 1449. He gained the title of 
1 CONC 1st Earl of Richmond on 23 November 1452.1
