1 CONT king, he continued the work of his father, Charles VII, in strengthening and
1 CONT unifying France after the Hundred Years' War with England which ruled a
1 CONT large part of France when he was born. Louis regarded war as a precarious
1 CONT enterprise and made it only with reluctance. Diplomacy and inheritance were
1 CONT the means he preferred for extending his royal domain as a tireless worker.
