0 @N6000000004533233465@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Thomas Holland, 1st Earl of Kent (d. 1360) was an English nobleman andmilitary commander during the Hundred Years War.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was from a gentry family in Holland, Lancashire. In his earlymilitary career, he fought in Flanders (including at the Battle ofSluys), and then in Gascony. He was one of the founding Knights of theGarter in 1344. He took part i
1 CONC n Edward III's campaign of 1346, andheld a command at Crecy.
1 CONT
1 CONT Around the same time he married Joan of Kent, daughter of Edmund ofWoodstock and granddaughter of Edward I. Between 1353 and 1356 he wassummoned to Parliament as Baron de Holland.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1354 Holland was the king's lieutenant in Brittany during theminority of the Duke of Brittany, and in 1359 co-captain-general forall the English continental possessions.
1 CONT
1 CONT His brother-in-law John, Earl of Kent, died in 1360, and Hollandbecame Earl of Kent in right of his wife.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was succeeded as baron by his son Thomas, the earldom still beingheld by his wife (though the son later became Earl in his own right).Another son, John became Earl of Huntingdon and Duke of Exeter.
