0 @N6000000002188309292@ NOTE Thomas of Lancaster, 1st Duke of Clarence
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT English Royalty
1 CONT House of Lancaster
1 CONT
1 CONT Armorial of Plantagenet
1 CONT Henry IV
1 CONT    Henry V
1 CONT    John, Duke of Bedford
1 CONT    Thomas, Duke of Clarence
1 CONT    Humphrey, Duke of Gloucester
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas of Lancaster, 1st Duke of Clarence (29 September 1388 Kenilworth Castle – 22 March 1421 Battle of Baugé) was the second son of King Henry IV of England and his first wife, Mary de Bohun.
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas married Lady Margaret Holland, widow of John Beaufort, 1st Earl of Somerset and daughter of Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent in November or December of 1411. No children were born from this union, though Thomas was stepfath
1 CONC er to her six children from her first marriage.
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas fought in the Siege of Rouen (July 1418 - 19 January 1419), where he commanded the sieging force; and in the Battle of Baugé on 22 March 1421. He was killed, by Sir Alexander Buchanan or Sir John de la Croise, during the la
1 CONC tter and was buried in Canterbury Cathedral.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Titles
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Knight, Order of the Bath (12 October 1399 - 22 March 1421)
1 CONT     * Knight, Order of the Garter (1400 - 22 March 1421)
1 CONT     * Duke of Clarence (9 July 1412 - 22 March 1421); extinct upon his death until the Third Creation of it in (1461)
1 CONT     * 1st Earl of Aumale (9 July 1412 - 22 March 1421); extinct upon his death
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Offices held
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Lord High Steward of England (1399-1421) - he was the last permanent holder of this office, the highest in medieval England.
1 CONT     * Chief Governor of Ireland (1401-1413)
1 CONT     * Lord High Admiral (1405-1406)
1 CONT     * Lieutenant of Aquitaine (1412-1413)
1 CONT     * Lord High Steward of Chester (1415)
1 CONT     * Constable of the Army (1417)
1 CONT     * Lieutenant-General (United Kingdom) of the Army in France and Normandy (1417 and 1421)
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Weir, Alison (2002). Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy. The Bodley Head London, U.K.. ISBN 0-7126-4286-2.  pages 102 & 123
1 CONT     * Cokayne, G.E. (2000). The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant. Alan Sutton.  Vol I pg 368, Vol III pg 258 & 259
