1 CONT Called by Henry's biographer Desmond Seward "the most brilliant commander of the entire Hundred Years War after Henry himself.  A complete professional, he was a daring raider into enemy territory who could extricate his men from 
1 CONC the most dangerous situations; at the same time he was a skilled artilleryman and expert in siegecraft ... Above all, he had a shrewd grasp of strategy and tactics. He was popular with the troops and dreaded by the enemy."
1 CONT Salisbury is a desperate homicide,
1 CONT He fighteth as one weary of his life. (Shakespeare)
1 CONT
1 CONT [Weis 12] Lt.Gen. of Normandy
