0 @N6000000006296760683@ NOTE Alice Montagu was born in 1407, the daughter and only legitimate child, of Thomas Montacute, 4th Earl of Salisbury </wiki/Thomas_Montacute,_4th_Earl_of_Salisbury> and Eleanor Holland </wiki/Eleanor_Holland>, who was the daughter o
1 CONC f Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent </wiki/Thomas_Holland,_2nd_Earl_of_Kent> and Alice Fitzalan </wiki/Alice_Fitzalan>, daughter of Richard FitzAlan, 10th Earl of Arundel </wiki/Richard_FitzAlan,_10th_Earl_of_Arundel> and Eleanor o
1 CONC f Lancaster </wiki/Eleanor_of_Lancaster>.
1 CONT In 1420, she married Richard Neville </wiki/Richard_Neville,_5th_Earl_of_Salisbury>, who became Earl of Salisbury </wiki/Earl_of_Salisbury> on the death of his father-in-law in 1428. At the same time, Alice became Countess of Sali
1 CONC sbury.
1 CONT The main home of the family was at Bisham </wiki/Bisham> Manor in Berkshire </wiki/Berkshire> although their lands lay chiefly around Christchurch </wiki/Christchurch> in Hampshire </wiki/Hampshire> and Wiltshire </wiki/Wiltshire>
1 CONC .
1 CONT She died some time before 9 December </wiki/December_9> 1462 </wiki/1462> and was buried in the Montacute Mausoleum at Bisham Abbey </wiki/Bisham_Abbey>.
1 CONT She and Richard had ten children:
1 CONT Joan Neville, 1423 - 9 September 1462, who married William FitzAlan, 16th Earl of Arundel </wiki/William_FitzAlan,_16th_Earl_of_Arundel>
1 CONT Cecily Neville </wiki/Cecily_Neville,_Duchess_of_Warwick>, 1424 - 28 July 1450, who married Henry de Beauchamp, 1st Duke of Warwick </wiki/Henry_de_Beauchamp,_1st_Duke_of_Warwick>
1 CONT Richard Neville, 16th Earl of Warwick </wiki/Richard_Neville,_16th_Earl_of_Warwick> 1428 - 1471
1 CONT Alice Neville, 1430- 1503, who married Henry FitzHugh, 6th Baron FitzHugh </w/index.php?title=Henry_FitzHugh,_6th_Baron_FitzHugh&action=edit&redlink=1>
1 CONT John Neville, 1st Marquess of Montagu </wiki/John_Neville,_1st_Marquess_of_Montagu> 1431 - 1471
1 CONT George Neville </wiki/George_Neville,_archbishop_of_York> 1432 - 1476, who became Archbishop of York </wiki/Archbishop_of_York> and Chancellor of England </wiki/Chancellor_of_England>
1 CONT Eleanor Neville, 1438 - 1504, who married Thomas Stanley, 1st Earl of Derby </wiki/Thomas_Stanley,_1st_Earl_of_Derby>
1 CONT Katherine Neville </wiki/Katherine_Neville,_Baroness_Hastings>, 1442 - 25 March 1504, who married firstly William Bonville, 6th Baron of Harington </wiki/William_Bonville,_6th_Baron_of_Harington> and secondly William Hastings, 1st
1 CONC  Baron Hastings </wiki/William_Hastings,_1st_Baron_Hastings>. By her first husband, she was the mother of Cecily Bonville </wiki/Cecily_Bonville,_Baroness_Harington_and_Bonville>
1 CONT Thomas Neville, 1443 - 1460, who was knighted in 1449 and died at the Battle of Wakefield </wiki/Battle_of_Wakefield>
1 CONT Margaret Neville, 1444 - 20 November 1506, who married John de Vere, 13th Earl of Oxford </wiki/John_de_Vere,_13th_Earl_of_Oxford>
