0 @N6000000002188309509@ NOTE John II, Duke of Lorraine
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT John II of Anjou (Nancy, 1425 – December 16, 1470, Barcelona) was Duke of Lorraine from 1453 to his death. He inherited the duchy from his mother, Duchess Isabelle, during the life of his father, Duke René of Anjou, also Duke of L
1 CONC orraine and titular king of Naples. As heir-apparent of Naples, he was styled the Duke of Calabria, and spent most of his time engaging in plots for Angevin recovery of Naples. In 1466, the Catalonians chose his father as King of 
1 CONC Aragon, and he was created Prince of Girona, as heir-apparent. He went into Catalonia to press the family's claims, but died, supposedly by poison, in Barcelona.
1 CONT
1 CONT By his marriage to Marie de Bourbon (1428–1448), daughter of Charles I, Duke of Bourbon, he had four children:
1 CONT
1 CONT    1. Isabelle (b. 1445), d. young
1 CONT    2. René (b. 1446), d. young
1 CONT    3. Marie (b. 1447), d. young
1 CONT    4. Nicholas (1448–1473).
1 CONT
1 CONT He also had several illegitimate children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * John (d. 1504), Count of Briey, married Nancy St. Georges
1 CONT     * Albert, seigneur d'Essey
1 CONT     * a daughter, married Jean d'Ecosse
1 CONT     * Jeanne d'Abancourt, married Achille, Bastard of Beauveu
1 CONT     * Marguerite
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] See also
