0 @N6000000002188378226@ NOTE Christina of Saxony
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Christina of Saxony (b. Torgau, 25 December 1461 - d. Odense, 8 December 1521), was a Saxon Princess who became Queen Consort of Denmark, Norway, and Sweden. She was born a granddaughter of Frederick the Gentle of Saxony, and daug
1 CONC hter of Ernest, Elector of Saxony and Elisabeth of Bavaria-Munich.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Biography
1 CONT
1 CONT She was married to Hans, King of Denmark, Norway and Sweden on 6 September 1478. She was Queen consort of Denmark and Norway from 1483 to 1513 and of Sweden from 1497 to 1501.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was the mother of Christian II, Franciscus, Knud and Elisabeth, who later married Joachim I Nestor, Elector of Brandenburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1497, her husband was made king of Sweden; in 1499, Christina was crowned queen of Sweden in Uppsala and in 1500, Queen Christina was made regent in Sweden during her husband's absence from this country. When a rebellion broke 
1 CONC out in Sweden against Denmark and the union in 1501, Christina was besieged in the castle of Tre Kronor in Stockholm. She surrendered on 9 May 1502, after the Danish soldiers had been reduced from 1,000 men to 70 by sickness and s
1 CONC tarvation. She was taken prisoner by Sten Sture the Elder and held at Vadstena Abbey until 1503, when she was released against ransom and returned to Denmark.
1 CONT
1 CONT Christina of Saxony died in 1521, aged 59.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Åke Ohlmarks, "Alla Sveriges drottningar"
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Succession
