0 @N6000000002187755112@ NOTE Humbert II of Savoy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT With the name of Humbert II of Savoy are known two famous members of the Savoy dynasty. The first was Humbert II the Fat, of whom this page is about, the other one is Humbert II King of Italy Il Re di Maggio.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT Humbert II, surnamed the Fat, was Count of Savoy from 1080 until his death in 1103.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was married to Gisela of Burgundy, daughter of William the Great of Burgundy and Stephany de Longwy, and had 4 children:
1 CONT
1 CONT Amedeo 
1 CONT William, Bishop of Liège 
1 CONT Adelaide, (d. 1154), married to Louis VI of France 
1 CONT Agnes, (d. 1127), married to Arcimboldo VI (Archibald VI in English ?) of Burgundy 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Amadeus II Count of Savoy Succeeded by:
1 CONT Amadeus III 
